PVD("cambodia_ndp_2019-2023",{"docs":["","CMB NDP 2019 2023"],"s":{"1":[[1,"101","7","Disaster Preparedness Coordination and Exercise Programme","Disaster preparedness has improved through coordination of Humanitarian Respond Forum (HRF) and NCDM and annual conduct of CamRex, with extension to some sub- national exercises.",""],[1,"236","5","Data and Information Management and Dissemination System","Promoting the collection, analysis, management, use and dissemination of the relevant data and information, sourcing from geographic information system (GIS), and information and communication technology and innovations.",""],[1,"236","6","Business Continuity and Risk Assessment Incentive Scheme","Incentivizing businesses to strengthen business continuity and conduct location- specific risk assessments of their operating environment and supply chain with a clear understanding of their hazard exposure, vulnerability and risks to hazards.",""],[1,"236","7","Disaster Risk Information Integration for Business Investment Planning","Integrating disaster risk information into business investment planning and management across private sector entities, in particular Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs), through business associations, chambers of commerce and national and local platforms on DRR.",""],[1,"236","8","Public-Private Partnership Awareness and Education Initiative","Mobilizing public-private partnership initiatives for awareness raising, advocacy and education to strengthen private sector attitudes towards risk-sensitive development.",""],[1,"236","9","Local Risk Assessment Guidelines for Development Planning","Formulating guidelines for local risk assessments and their use in local development planning, with a complement of traditional, indigenous and local knowledge and practices, and science and technology.",""],[1,"236","10","Hazard, Exposure, and Social Vulnerability Monitoring Capacity Building","Building the knowledge and capacity of local and national government officials, civil society, communities and volunteers to monitor hazards, exposure and social vulnerabilities.",""],[1,"236","11","Public Disaster Awareness Campaign","Raising public awareness of disasters by taking the opportunities provided by the International Day for Disaster Reduction and the World Tsunami Awareness Day.",""],[1,"236","12","Revision of National and Local Disaster Risk Reduction Strategies and Plans","Revising the existing national and local disaster risk reduction strategies/ plans in line with the Sendai Framework and SDGs.",""],[1,"236","13","Disaster Risk Reduction Incentive Regulatory Reform","Improving the legal, policy and regulatory environment to incentivize businesses to reinforce DRR.",""],[1,"236","14","Implementation of Health Aspects of the Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction","Promoting implementation of health aspects of the Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction 2015-2030, with a view to ensuring more systematic cooperation, coherence and integration between disaster and health risk management.",""],[1,"236","15","Local DRR Strategy Inventory and Sendai Alignment","Undertaking an inventory of available local DRR strategies/plans and work towards achieving the Sendai Framework Target on \"risk-informed local DRR strategies/plans\" by 2020.",""],[1,"236","18","National Disaster Risk Transfer and Insurance Mechanisms","Promoting national mechanisms for disaster risk transfer and insurance as appropriate.",""],[1,"236","19","Disaster Risk Reduction Mainstreaming and Resilience Partnerships","Increasing resilience and integrating disaster risk reduction into common practice through intensified partnerships between the private sector, local government and other stakeholders.",""],[1,"236","20","Disaster Risk Reduction Financing Mechanism","Promoting appropriate financial mechanisms to integrate disaster risk reduction considerations and measures to support the building of disaster resilient communities by engaging development funds, banks, private foundations and stakeholders.",""],[1,"237","1","Community-Based Disaster Risk Management Institutionalization","Institutionalizing community-based disaster risk management (CBDRM) to strengthen the resilience of households and communities.",""],[1,"237","2","Disaster and Climate Risk Reduction Education and Comprehensive School Safety Implementation","Strengthening education on disaster and climate risk reduction and accelerating the implementation of comprehensive school safety.",""],[1,"237","4","Disaster Preparedness and Contingency Plan Update","Updating disaster preparedness and contingency plans at local, national and regional levels with a multi-stakeholder and multi-sectoral approach, ensuring comprehensive and accessible service and referral mechanisms to promote specific needs of women and children, the elderly, people with disabilities and other at-risk populations.",""],[1,"237","5","Multi-Hazard Early Warning System Strengthening","Strengthening multi-hazard early warning systems to ensure last-mile accessibility.",""],[1,"237","6","Public-Private Cooperation for Disaster Preparedness and Recovery","Expanding private sector engagement in preparedness for response, recovery, and to \"Build Back Better\" through more systematic public-private cooperation.",""],[1,"237","7","Local Disaster Recovery Planning Capacity Building","Building capacity of local authorities, including strengthening leadership of women, persons with disability and youth to develop local disaster recovery plans that include retrofitting, reconstruction, building code enforcement, post-trauma programmes, resilient livelihoods, shelter provisions for displaced populations etc.",""]],"2":[[1,"100","17","Food Security and Nutrition Commitment","The RGC of Cambodia (RGC), including CARD, has made a commitment to address food security and nutrition (FSN) and to eliminate food insecurity and hunger.","RGC of Cambodia | CARD"],[1,"101","2","Food Security and Nutrition Planning and Coordination Framework","CARD led development of the planning framework and coordination mechanisms for FSN.",""],[1,"101","2","Water Supply and Sanitation Improvement","improvement of water supplies and sanitation has exceeded planning targets and continues strongly",""],[1,"101","2","Improved Coordination of Responses to Shocks","there has been improved coordination of responses to shocks",""],[1,"101","5","National Nutrition Awareness and Workshop Initiative","Awareness raising of the importance of nutrition via establishment of the National Nutrition Day on 6 November every year and the National Workshops on Food Security and Nutrition.",""],[1,"101","6","FSN Trainer Pool Training and Professional Development","the FSN Trainer Pool has continued to serve a vital role in the delivery of training and in the facilitation of cross-sectoral coordination, whilst at the same time committing to ongoing professional development.",""],[1,"101","9","Advocacy for Additional Public Funding for Food Security and Nutrition","Advocacy for additional public funding for FSN, including for MoH and MoP for nutrition-specific and nutrition-sensitive interventions, for the treatment of acute malnutrition and salt iodization, ironic fish and soy sauce and rice micronutrient fortification.","MoH | MoP"],[1,"101","16","Breast Milk Substitute and Food Fortification Regulation Enforcement","Enforcement of the regulations for breast milk substitutes and food fortification is a continuing battle.",""],[1,"101","17","Increased Public Funding and Private Sector Investment Mobilization for FSN","Maintaining sectoral commitments for FSN and meeting cross-sectoral challenges requires increased public funding for the future and creative means are required for securing private sector investments to support FSN.",""],[1,"126","15","Nutrition and Poverty Reduction Initiative","Foods with rich nutrition/a reduction of serious poverty (a minimum 3% of general population)",""],[1,"176","10","Value Chain Improvement in Production and Processing","Improve value chain in production & processing-including fortification.",""],[1,"176","11","Food Quality and Safety Improvement Measures","Improve food quality and safety (import, export & local market).",""],[1,"176","12","Sustainable Agricultural Techniques Promotion","Promote efficient, value- adding sustainable agricultural techniques.",""],[1,"176","18","Link Food Security and Nutrition with Social Protection","Enhance social safety nets and ensure ongoing link between FSN and social protection.",""],[1,"176","19","WASH Access and Behavior Change Improvement","Improve access to & behavior change for WASH.",""],[1,"177","6","FSN Governance Institutional Strengthening Investments","Institutional investments for strengthening FSN governance at both national and sub- national level.",""],[1,"177","7","FSN and Social Protection Linkage Expansion","Building linkages between FSN and Social Protection and expanding coverage of nutrition related Social Protection measures.",""],[1,"177","10","Resource Mobilization Advocacy","Advocacy for securing additional financial and in-kind contributions from government, the private sector, development partners, the media and academia.",""]],"3":[[1,"24","5","Green Production and Consumption Incentives","Address environment weaknesses which have been inherent to the past economic model and protect the natural resource endowment by nudging/ incentivizing greener production and consumption.",""],[1,"24","5","Economy Decarbonization Measures","In parallel, also meet Cambodia's commitments to climate change action, including de-carbonization of the economy and alongside measures.",""],[1,"58","8","Green Technology and Low-Emission Services Development","Services and technology ensuring the development and adoption of green technology and services, and with low emission of carbon (implementing technology transfer and research projects)",""],[1,"242","1","Climate Change Adaptation and Resilience Measures","change adaptation and resiliency measures as well as explore the possibility of studying financial resiliency to respond to disasters caused by climate change.",""],[1,"242","2","Integrated Water Resource Management Plan Development and Implementation","Further promoting the development and implementation of integrated water resource management plans in order to expand water supply in response to demand, and minimize the risks caused by flood and drought, as well as to ensure long-term water security.",""],[1,"242","15","Climate-Smart Private Sector Investment Promotion","Promoting resilience to climate change and facilitating for the progress of building a low-carbon society, including attracting the private sector in climate-smart investments.",""],[1,"242","16","NDC Implementation Roadmap Development","Developing a roadmap for implementing the NDC to implement the UN Framework Convention on Climate Change.",""],[1,"242","17","Increase National Budget Allocation for Climate Change Response","Increasing national budget allocation for climate change responses.",""],[1,"243","1","Climate-Smart Investment Policy and Regulatory Framework","Presenting policies and regulations to the private sector to implement the climate smart investments.",""]],"4":[[1,"2","2","Implementation of the National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023","The Royal Government of Cambodia shall continue the implementation of the National Strategic Development 2019- 2023.",""],[1,"2","3","Urgent Promulgation of the Law","This law shall be promulgated as a matter of urgency.",""],[1,"5","1","Strategic Planning Synchronization","the RGC has synchronised the timeframe of the National Strategic Development Plan with that of the RGC's Political Platform and the Rectangular Strategy.",""],[1,"5","5","Rectangular Strategy Phase IV Implementation","the Rectangular Strategy for Growth, Employment, Equity and Efficiency is still crucial and suitable for Cambodia to pursue its implementation by keeping the four angles, expanding the coverage, and prioritizing the policies and mechanisms to be more concrete as the Rectangular Strategy Phase IV",""],[1,"137","3","Continuation of Rectangular Strategy Phase IV","the Rectangular Strategy Phase IV has the same shape as the Rectangular Strategy Phase III, identifying \"Four Strategic Goals\" and \"Four Priorities\" as a commitment to continue implementing the Rectangular Strategy Phase IV.",""],[1,"138","8","Continued Implementation of RS-IV","Continued the implementation of the RS-IV is a step forward for Cambodia to advance to a new phase of development",""]],"5":[[1,"24","4","De-concentration and Devolution Reform","Additionally, ensuring political and administrative accountabilities via renewed de-concentration and devolution, and wider public/ civil service reforms.",""],[1,"145","5","Decentralization and Administrative Autonomy Reform","Delegating power, transferring functions, resources and techniques to all levels of administrative entities under line ministries-institutions, public establishments, sub- national administration to achieve a reasonable level of autonomy in terms of decision- making, supervision and management of human and financial resources; while clearly defining accountability and responsibility of public entities and public officials",""],[1,"145","5","District and Provincial Innovation Governance Initiative","Encouraging unified administration at khan-district, provincial and capital levels to consider and implement innovation solutions to ensure effective functioning and resource utilization",""],[1,"146","11","Decentralization and De-concentration Reform Implementation","The RGC will further promote the implementation of decentralization and de- concentration reform by focusing on:",""],[1,"146","12","Decentralization and Deconcentration of Administrative Powers","Delegate the power, function transfer, transfer of resources and technology sharing through decentralization and deconcentration mechanisms to administrative units at all levels under the guidance of the Ministry, institutions, public institutions and sub- national administrations to obtain appropriate autonomy, including decision-making, management and resource allocation.","the Ministry"],[1,"146","15","National Program on Sub-National Democratic Development","National Committee for Democratic Development (NCDD) has developed a National Program on Sub-National Democratic Development with the following commitments.","National Committee for Democratic Development (NCDD)"],[1,"147","2","Sub-national Administration Structure and Management Reform","Continuing to strengthen and modify SNA structures and management systems: Defining the roles and responsibilities of each sub-national administration more clearly and making local development more efficient, transparent, accountable, inclusive and social equity with the focus on the examination and organization of a new administrative system and structure of the municipality and district administration to ensure the promotion of roles and responsibilities of the municipality and district administration to become a major local administration in providing basic services and development.",""],[1,"147","2","Strengthened Monitoring and Evaluation for Sub-national Administration","At the same time, monitoring and evaluatiing mechanisms on duty implementation will also be strengthened to encourage and enhance the capacity of SNAs in the implementation of legal, regulatory and set labor standards to improve.",""],[1,"147","3","Decentralized Human Resource Management System for Sub-National Administrations","Promoting effective and effective management and human resource development at SNAs through the development and implementation of a decentralized human resource management system by empowering the sub- national administration in selecting, appointing, fining and other matters.",""],[1,"147","4","Transfer of Priority Functions to Sub-National Administrations","Continuing to promote the transfer of priority functions to SNAs to ensure that SNAs are fully capable and fully functioning in the management of public service delivery and direct economic development of the people.",""],[1,"147","4","One Window Administrative Services Expansion and Modernization","At the same time, administrative services through the \"One Window\" mechanism will continue to be expanded, upgraded and modernized to all capital, provinces, municipalities, districts/Khans, communes/Sangkats throughout the country to make it easier for citizens to quickly access the service, transparency, efficiency and accountability.",""],[1,"147","5","Decentralization of Finance for SNA Financial Strengthening","Continuing to promote decentralization of finance to ensure the strengthening of the SNA's financial resources, including streamlined financial resources and associated financial resources, and further improving the SNA's financial management system and capacity to ensure SNAs have adequate financial resources and capabilities in managing, allocating and utilizing efficiently the financial resources.",""],[1,"147","8","National and Sub-national Governance and Regulatory Reform","Continuing to adjust the roles and responsibilities of the national and sub- national levels by promoting the monitoring of SNA's work by reviewing and revising regulatory frameworks, structure, roles and responsibilities of the national and sub- national levels and strengthening the law enforcement and promoting autonomy and accountability.",""],[1,"147","9","Support for Transfer of Functions and Resources to SNAs","Strengthening and supporting the transfer of functions and resources transferred to SNAs by promoting ownership and responsibility for providing public services and local development in both infrastructure and social services under the authority profession, innovation, effectiveness, transparency, accountability, inclusiveness and social equity.",""],[1,"147","10","Civil Service Capacity and Local Governance Strengthening","Continuing to enhance the professional capacity of civil servants of the MOI, the Councils and civil servants in the SNAs, by developing quality capacities through the development and implementation of the system of quality development, improving the local governance system in accordance with the principles within Decentralization and Deconcentration Policy; develop ing and implementing IT system and media to the public and other stakeholders.","MOI"],[1,"148","1","Stakeholder Collaboration for Public Service Delivery Capacity Development","Continuing to strengthen collaboration with CSOs, the private sector and other stakeholders by mobilizing the necessary resources to support capacity development and enhance the efficiency of effective public service delivery and close to people.",""],[1,"148","2","Support and Coordination for Sub-National Administrations","Continuing to monitor and support the SNAs by continuing to lead the coordination of supporting sub-national administrations to strictly comply with the Law on Administrative Management of Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts/Khans, Law on Administrative Management of Communes/Sangkats and relevant legal documents; and continuing to support administrative affairs, laws, legal documents, local development and cooperation in the national and international levels.",""],[1,"148","6","Internal Audit and Integrity Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen internal audits and promote the integrity of national and sub-national levels, expanding scope and strengthening the quality of internal audit and further promoting integrity and strengthening good governance systems, procurement procedures, public forum preparation, strategic dissemination on social accountability and promotion and monitoring the integrity of SNA's governance.",""],[1,"148","7","Strengthening Service Delivery by Sub-National Authorities","Continuing to implement the functions transferred to the SNAs for a better implementation, enabling SNAs to carry out the functions that have been transferred and provide administrative services at the same OWSOs at SNAs; and continuing to encourage the SNAs to provide quality, transparent, efficient and timely administration services to the needs of the people.",""],[1,"148","8","Sub-national Public Service Planning and Budgeting Support","Continuing to urge SNAs to plan and budget for public services delivery to advise and support clear budgeting and planning for public services delivery, public forums, consultations with citizens to collect inputs for planning and budgeting at sub- national levels and continuing to respond to needs of the local people.",""]],"6":[[1,"6","2","Government-Led Development Resource Allocation","the RGC will take full charge of the entire development process to ensure that all resources, government and external development partners', are clearly directed to priorities and sectors chosen.",""],[1,"44","6","Bilateral and Multilateral Development Partner Consultation","The RGC has continued to conduct bilateral and multilateral consultations with key development partners such as Japan, Korea, Australia, Europe and UN agencies to review and obtain direct the support of those partners in accordance with national development priorities.",""],[1,"44","6","Joint Technical Working Group Mechanism","the RGC has implemented a joint technical working group mechanism to promote the effectiveness of partnerships at the sectoral level.",""],[1,"46","12","Bilateral and Multilateral Development Cooperation Expansion","Strengthened and expanded bilateral relations with international friends, international organizations and the UN agencies for assistance in the development of the country in all sectors.",""],[1,"159","2","Development Cooperation and Partnership Strategy 2019-2023","Formulating and implementing \"Development Cooperation and Partnership Strategy 2019-2023\"",""],[1,"159","3","Active Participation in Regional and Global Affairs","Continue to participate actively in regional and global affairs in order to increase development opportunities, particularly to boost confidence in security, safety, and investment environment of Cambodia, as well as to ensure the prestige of Cambodia.",""],[1,"159","4","Implementation of International Development Effectiveness Commitments","Continuing to implement all commitments agreed by Cambodia in the International Forum on Development Effectiveness along with strengthened implementation of existing consultation mechanism to discuss various topics related to national development.",""],[1,"159","5","NGO Law Enforcement and Partnership Strengthening","Further strengthening partnership with non-governmental organizations through enforcing the law on associations and non-governmental organizations in order to promote efficiency, transparency, and accountability of the cooperation.",""],[1,"159","8","Development Cooperation and Partnership Strategy 2019-2023","Preparing and implementing Development Cooperation and Partnership Strategy 2019-2023 to continue to strengthen and align with the development cooperation with the priorities in the RS-IV and align with the global principles on the effectiveness in the development based on the ownership, inclusive partnership, and results for the basis in mobilizing national development resources.",""],[1,"159","9","Government Ownership and Development Resource Coordination Mechanism","Continuing to strengthen the ownership and leadership of the government by including the global principles on the effectiveness in the development in the national principle and mechanism in mobilizing and coordinating the utilization of the development resources.",""],[1,"159","10","Inclusive Development Financing Partnership","Continuing to strengthen inclusive partnership in mobilizing development financing from all development actors to ensure consistency, promote public services delivery and strengthen the use of the national system.",""],[1,"159","11","Development Cooperation Consultation Mechanisms","continuing to implement the consultation mechanisms set in Development Cooperation and Partnership Strategy 2019-2023.",""],[1,"159","12","Results-Based Development Monitoring System","Strengthening the result-based development by preparing the monitoring system and principle on two-way accountability to be a basis for strengthening the evidence- based partnership.",""],[1,"159","13","NGO Partnership Strengthening through Legal and Governance Reform","Continuing to strengthen partnership with NGOs through strengthening Law on Association and Non-Governmental Organizations as well as promoting the efficiency, transparency, and accountability of the cooperation.",""],[1,"160","8","Participation in Economic Cooperation and Integration Initiatives","Further participating actively in international, regional and bilateral economic cooperation and integration initiatives.",""],[1,"160","9","Inter-Ministerial and Stakeholder Coordination for Service Delivery Improvement","Promoting cooperation and coordination between the RGC's ministries-institutions and related development stakeholders to strengthen the national capacity and system to improve service delivery and competitiveness of Cambodia.",""],[1,"160","10","Business Trend Monitoring Capacity Building","Continuing to build capacity for monitoring business trends in all sectors.",""],[1,"160","11","Inter-Ministerial Coordination and Regulatory Enforcement Strengthening","the RGC will continue to strengthen the inter-ministerial coordination, the enactment of laws and necessary regulations to implement the obligations as the member state of the international and regional organizations and building the capacity of the relevant line ministries and agencies to manage and urge the effective enforcement of laws and regulations.",""],[1,"162","8","Investment Negotiation Capacity Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen and develop the investment negotiation capacity to the CDC's officials to have more skills and experience.",""]],"7":[[1,"239","3","Real Estate Registration Programme","Implementing the registration of real estate to reach 78% by 2019, 84% by 2020, 90% by 2021, 96% by 2022, and 100% by 2023 of an estimated total of 7 million land titles.",""],[1,"239","5","State Land Registration Acceleration","Accelerating the registration of state land that is the subject of the economic land consession for the remaining 119 companies and other state lands.",""],[1,"239","6","Construction Information on Land Titles Regulation Review","Studying regulations to include construction information on titles.",""],[1,"239","7","Land Dispute Resolution Acceleration Mechanism","Accelerating the land dispute resolutions through all mechanisms, including the National Authority for Land Dispute, Cadastral Commission, Mobile Dispute Resolution Team and the additional mechanisms established by the MLMUPC for the social harmony.","MLMUPC"],[1,"239","8","State Land Encroachment Prevention","Preventing encroachment on all types of state land, including forest land, land in protected fishing areas, land in natural and environmental protected areas, road sides and railways.",""],[1,"239","9","Expansion of Geodetic Benchmarks for Property Mapping","Expanding the 2nd, 3rd, and 4th geodetic benchmarks to support the mapping and listing of properties throughout the country.",""],[1,"239","10","Update the National Geographical Name List","Update the geographical name list of the Kingdom of Cambodia for newly formed villages and communes/Sangkats.",""],[1,"239","22","National Residential Information and Data Management System","Launching the residential information and data management for the whole country.",""],[1,"240","1","Construction Site and Housing Loan Information Mapping","Developing the map for the temporary construction sites and poor communities and housing loan information in the capital and provinces.",""]],"8":[[1,"245","4","Public Financial Management Reform Program","the RGC will take concrete actions to further strengthen and refine the harmonization of planning along with monitoring and evaluation, with the execution of public investment expenditure, and development-cooperation-financing, via the Public Financial Management Reform Program (PFMRP).",""],[1,"245","4","Alignment of Planning and Budgeting Frameworks","To ensure improved alignment, greater links and synergies will be made between planning efforts (undertaken within the NSDP and the PIP overseen by the MOP), and revenue and capital budgeting (within the Budget Strategic Framework carried out by LMs/LAs and overseen by the MEF).",""],[1,"248","2","Planning and Resource Allocation Strengthening and Refinement","The RGC will also further strengthen and refine planning and resource allocation processes and the capacities of the governmental institutions.","MOP"],[1,"251","3","Planning and Budget Harmonization under PFMRP","the RGC will accelerate efforts to deliver synergies between the PIP process and the development of capital budgets within Budget Strategic Plans (under the PFMRP).",""],[1,"251","4","Public Investment Program Strengthening","The MOP specifically, will strengthen the PIP to provide an investment resource envelope to serve as an operational and financing tool to implement the policy priorities identified in the NSDP.","MOP | MEF | LMs/LAs | RGC | CDC"],[1,"258","5","Performance-Based Budgeting Roll-Out","In line with the ongoing roll-out of performance-based budgeting under the phases 3 and 4 of RGC's PFMRP reforms1, the LMs/LAs are expected to plan and implement projects and programs following a standard Programmatic Structure (PS).",""],[1,"258","5","Programmatic Structure and Budget-M&E Synchronization","The PS, the budget and the M&E framework should be synchronized to ensure full harmony between these three.",""],[1,"258","6","Public Financial Management Reform Program","Public Financial Management Reform Program see link: http://www.pfm.gov.kh/index.php/en/",""]],"9":[[1,"24","4","Public and Civil Service Reform","Additionally, ensuring political and administrative accountabilities via renewed de-concentration and devolution, and wider public/ civil service reforms.",""],[1,"64","11","Policy Implementation Effectiveness and Service Delivery Mechanism Strengthening","Continued to prioritize the effectiveness of both the policy implementation and the establishment of necessary mechanisms to provide services to the people more effectively.",""],[1,"64","12","Public Administration Reform Program","Continued to implement the the RGC's three reforms i.e. (1) Public Administration Reform Program, (2) Public Financial Management Reform, and (3) Sub-National Democratic Development Reforms.",""],[1,"64","12","Public Financial Management Reform","Continued to implement the the RGC's three reforms i.e. (1) Public Administration Reform Program, (2) Public Financial Management Reform, and (3) Sub-National Democratic Development Reforms.",""],[1,"64","12","Sub-National Democratic Development Reforms","Continued to implement the the RGC's three reforms i.e. (1) Public Administration Reform Program, (2) Public Financial Management Reform, and (3) Sub-National Democratic Development Reforms.",""],[1,"83","2","Administrative and Public Financial Management Reform Programme","The ministry promoted administrative reforms and public financial management reforms and strengthened the capacity of civil servants as well as law enforcement, regulation development, and public service delivery.",""],[1,"83","2","Civil Service and Public Service Delivery Capacity Strengthening","The ministry promoted administrative reforms and public financial management reforms and strengthened the capacity of civil servants as well as law enforcement, regulation development, and public service delivery.",""],[1,"83","16","Public Financial Management and Procurement Reform Program","Strengthened the implementation of Public Financial Management and Procurement Reform Program.",""],[1,"118","2","Public Finance Management Reform Program","the Royal government still continues to carry out the reform program in public finance management in order to increase effectiveness in the preparation and implementation of the budget, especially the linkage of budget to prioritized policies that has been set out.",""],[1,"125","6","Governance Reform Acceleration","Rectangular core focuses on accelerating governance reform, identifying further progress on public financial management reform.",""],[1,"126","9","Public Administration Reform for Effective Governance","public administration reform to provide effective administration and governance through implementation and compliance to international standard of governance of private sector.",""],[1,"126","14","Administration and Governance Reform Procedure","Administration and governance reform procedure is being implemented including civil services which bases on strong qualification and a firm budget accountability and process, public financial management reform phase III and IV)",""],[1,"134","10","Public Administration and Public Financial Management Reform","Support policy reform through public administration and public financial management reform to address structural issues, for example, facilitating trade and automation, logistics, electricity, informal fees, productivity improvements.",""],[1,"135","1","Institutional Coordination and Good Governance Strengthening","Over the next five years, with a peace, political stability and territorial integrity, the RGC in the sixth mandate of the National Assembly continues to focus on: 1) Human resource development, people's welfare, and social protection and other social benefits programs; 2) Institutional coordination and good governance.",""],[1,"138","11","Institutional Reform and Capacity Building","For the Sixth Legislature of the National Assembly, the RGC of Cambodia (RGC) will focus on (1) Institutional reform and capacity building, (2) Strengthening accountability",""],[1,"138","11","Accountability Strengthening","For the Sixth Legislature of the National Assembly, the RGC of Cambodia (RGC) will focus on (1) Institutional reform and capacity building, (2) Strengthening accountability",""],[1,"139","3","Council of Ministers Governance Rationalization","Rationalizing the roles and duties, management structure, and inter-institutional coordination by focusing on strengthening ownership, responsibility and clear division of accountability of each ministry-institution, especially through the firm enforcement of the Law on the Organization and Function of the Council of Ministers.",""],[1,"139","4","Public Sector Leadership and Code of Conduct Reform","Strengthening leadership, sense of ownership and responsibility and internal unity of the institutions, formulating and strictly implementing the code of conduct, and selecting people with high qualification for the management position in the public sector.",""],[1,"139","12","Decentralization and Deconcentration Reform Program Implementation Strengthening","Strengthening the implementation of the Decentralization and Deconcentration (D&D) Reform Program",""],[1,"141","15","Cross-Sector Reform Facilitation Mechanism","Strengthening the mechanisms for facilitating cross-sector reforms and relevant stakeholders.",""],[1,"141","16","National Public Administration Reform Implementation, Monitoring, and Evaluation","Promoting, monitoring, and evaluating the implementation of the National Program on Public Administration Reform.",""],[1,"141","17","Civil Servant Training and Capacity Development","Training and developing the capacity of the civil servants.",""],[1,"141","19","Civil Service Information Technology Modernization","Modernizing the information technology (IT) for the administration of civil servants",""],[1,"141","20","Civil Servant Document Management IT System","Managing fact sheets and civil servant documents through IT system.",""],[1,"141","21","Civil Servant and Retirement Data Management IT System","Managing civil servant's data and data for retirement through IT system.",""],[1,"141","22","Civil Service IT Modernization System","Developing an IT system to support the modernization of civil services.",""],[1,"145","5","Civil Service and Pension Payment Reform","Increasing the salaries of civil servants and members of armed forces every year together with pensions of retirees and veterans by disbursing through the banking system on a biweekly basis",""],[1,"145","5","Performance-Based Management System","Putting in place the performance-based management system by using Key Performance Indicators (KPIs), particularly for officials at supervision and management levels",""],[1,"145","5","Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Putting in place monitoring and evaluation mechanism to help improve performance, implementation",""],[1,"146","1","Inter-Ministerial Policy Coordination and Implementation Mechanism","measures, strategic directions and inter-ministerial coordination for the preparation and implementation of government policies",""],[1,"146","1","Public Administration Information Sharing Mechanism","Strengthening information sharing mechanism at all levels of public administration to enhance management effectiveness and respond to the demand of public service users in this rapidly changing national and international context",""],[1,"146","5","Payroll and Benefits Reform","Reforming the payroll and other benefits.",""],[1,"146","6","Cross-Sectoral Reform Coordination Mechanism","Strengthening coordination mechanisms for cross-sectoral reforms and with relevant stakeholders.",""],[1,"146","7","Monitoring and Evaluation of the National Program for Public Administration Reform","Promoting the monitoring and evaluation of the National Program for Public Administration Reform.",""],[1,"146","8","Civil Servant Training and Capacity Development","Training and developing the capacity of the civil servants.",""],[1,"146","10","Civil Service IT Modernization","Modernizing IT for the administration of civil servants.",""],[1,"146","13","DM-Level Innovation and Unified Administration Reform","Promote innovation and unified administration at DM level to ensure efficiency in function and resource utilization.",""],[1,"146","14","Public Administration Information Sharing Mechanisms","Strengthen sharing mechanisms and information sharing in the public administration at all levels across the country to improve management efficiency and respond to the needs of users of public services in the rapidly evolving national and international context.",""],[1,"146","16","Reform Management Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen the management of reforms: Ensuring the promotion of ownership of the RGC, ministries, agencies at national and sub-national levels in the leadership, management, coordination and implementation of the reform process, continuing to strengthen harmonization with the Public Administration Reform",""],[1,"147","1","Public Financial Management Reform Linkage and Efficiency Improvement","Public Financial Management Reform to be more linked, reducing operating costs and improving the efficiency of the implementation of these reforms.",""],[1,"183","8","Civil Service Capacity Strengthening and Administrative Efficiency Improvement","Strengthening the capacity of the civil servants and improving administrative efficiency.",""],[1,"183","9","NGO Partnership Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen partnerships with domestic and foreign NGOs.",""],[1,"183","10","Public Financial Management Reform Phase IV","Implementing the public financial management reform Phase IV.",""]],"10":[[1,"254","3","Capacity Strengthening for Planning Focal Points","Strengthening capacities within government agencies, specifically planning focal points within line ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"254","5","Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","The M&E Framework aims to quantify progress against the plans by examining results-chains, contextual factors and causalities.",""],[1,"254","7","Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","Within the context Figure 6.1: M&E within the Policy Cycle of the NSDP, the M&E framework, and its supporting systems provide feedback on implementation of the RGC's policies; informing and enabling operational and management Strategic Policy Choices decisions to fine tune delivery; and at a higher level, the adjustment of policies.",""],[1,"254","7","Policy Review and Revision Mechanism","For policy adjusting, it requires reviewing of policy stance, and subsequent revision of end goals.",""],[1,"254","7","Performance Management Integration for M&E","Therefore, the M&E can be served within performance management systems, providing M&E delivery criteria to be matched with financial and human resource data.",""],[1,"256","2","NSDP Results Framework and Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","The NSDP M&E framework specifically, links these high-level outcomes, to lower level outcomes and to outputs which can be influenced by policy choices and actions, so offering a mechanism for tracking and guiding implementation of polices at plan level.",""],[1,"257","11","Specification and Collection of Missing Indicator Data","Work is now required to specify sources and collect these data.",""],[1,"257","12","Annual NSDP Review Process","the review process will take place annually, and will be led by the MOP in consultation with LMs/LAs.","MOP | LMs/LAs"],[1,"258","2","Annual Indicator and Target Review Mechanism","Annual reviews will also include an assessment of the quality of indicators and the supporting data.",""],[1,"258","3","Development of Result Frameworks for Development Plans","implementing ministries and agencies, and subnational administrations will continue to develop their own result frameworks to support their development plans.",""],[1,"258","4","Sectoral Monitoring and Evaluation by Local Ministries and Local Authorities","it is the responsibility of each of LMs/LAs to carry out the M&E at output and input levels - that is for, the projects and services, and the expenditures and actions, to deliver the corresponding sectoral results.",""],[1,"258","4","Results Chain and Theory of Change Framework for Subsidiary Plans","all results chains should identify underlying assumptions and be informed by a theory of change and be supported by preliminary analyses of the critical paths and constraints",""],[1,"259","3","Subnational Data Profile Generation","with ongoing improvements in data collection, greater disaggregation of administrative and statistical data is now possible. This will permit subnational authorities over the course of the cycle, to generate data profiles at different levels.",""],[1,"259","3","Province-Level Statistical Data Provision","Statistical datasets which can already be provided at province level include the Cambodia Demographic and Health Survey (CDHS), a major source of data.",""],[1,"259","3","Province-Level Poverty Estimation","the NIS/MOP has provided estimated poverty rates based on the Cambodia Socio-economic Survey (CSES)","NIS/MOP"],[1,"259","3","Province-Level GDP Estimation Pilot","continues to pilot the generation of the GDP estimates at province level.","NIS/MOP"],[1,"259","5","Indicator Framework Establishment and M&E Support","The MOP will make efforts to mitigate these over the course of the NSDP cycle.","MOP | LMs/LAs | subnational administrations"],[1,"260","1","National Monitoring and Evaluation Framework Harmonization","ongoing efforts will be needed to ensure indicators and frameworks (the NSDP, the CSDGs and the SRF) are synergized and kept up to date.",""],[1,"260","2","Indicator Data Coordination Mechanism","The MOP will also prioritize efforts to improve coordination between the producers and users of indicator data to ensure needs are met.",""],[1,"260","2","Public Policy Data Market Management Arrangement","The MOP aims to do this by coordinating via the work of General Directorate of Planning (GDP), and the output of National Institute of Statistics (NIS) as a monopoly provider of statistical data.",""],[1,"260","4","Strengthening M&E Coordination and Data Standardization","Efforts are needed to ensure that as far as possible definitions and data generation processes are comparable, and where possible agencies should be engaged to follow international, or at least nationally accepted definitions and practices.",""],[1,"260","5","Administrative Data Standardization and Consolidation Framework","the MOP will extend this to administrative datasets and compilation processes; (2) specification of common sources and definitions within national data frameworks (the NSDP, the CSDGs and the SRF) to encourage consolidation; and (3) recognizing that standardization is not deliverable overnight, inform the users of the differences and discourage the comparison of incomparable variables.","MOP"],[1,"261","1","Education and Health Information System Improvement Partnership","its ongoing partnership with LMs/LAs will work to improve the two most prominent databases, which are available in public domain: the Education Management Information System (EMIS); and the Health Information System (HIS).",""],[1,"261","3","Key Capacity Development Measures","the MOP, with other ministries agencies, will undertake a series of measures to develop key capacities:","MOP | other ministries agencies"],[1,"261","4","National Monitoring and Evaluation System for NSDP and CSDGs","Set up a national system for the M&E of the result of the NSDP implementation and the CSDGs achievement.",""],[1,"261","5","NSDP and CSDG Progress Reporting Mechanism","Prepare, with closely cooperation with the LMs/LAs and other stake holders, Annual Progress Report (APR), the Mid-term Review (MTR) and the Final Report of the NSDP implementation, and Progress Report on the CSDGs achievement.",""],[1,"261","6","National Monitoring and Evaluation Strategy and Technical Guidelines","Formulate new technical guidelines and a National M&E Strategy, and disseminate these widely, and support with familiarization training.",""],[1,"261","7","Major Projects Tracking System","Strengthen systems for major projects tracking (delivered by the three-year rolling Public Investment Plan).",""],[1,"261","8","NSDP-BSP Monitoring and Evaluation Linkage","Link and synergize the NSDP M&E with indicators and data used to monitor budgeting via the Budget Strategic Plan (BSP) process.",""],[1,"261","9","Planning and Statistics M&E Training Packages","Provide training packages for officials-in-charge of planning and statistics; and ad hoc training on the basics of the M&E, data collection, analysis for other focal points in the line ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"261","10","One-Stop Technical Assistance Service for Ministries and Agencies","Establish a one-stop technical assistance service for ministries and agencies on indicator selection, data collection, data analysis/interpretation, formulation of results framework and so forth (as requested).",""],[1,"261","11","Joint Reporting and Review Preparation Mechanism","LMs/LAs need to provide inputs in close cooperation with the MOP requirement for preparing the APR, the MTR, and the end report of the NSDP implementation and for preparing the CSDG achievement progress report.","LMs/LAs | MOP"],[1,"276","4","National Working Group on Monitoring and Evaluation Support","MOP is set to continue to support the roles of the National Working Group on Monitoring and Evaluation (NWGM&E), serving as its chair.","MOP | National Working Group on Monitoring and Evaluation (NWGM&E)"]],"11":[[1,"32","3","Strategic Plan and Program on Social Accountability","the organization an implementation of the Strategic Plan and Program on Social Accountability in close partnership with civil society to provide key information pertaining to implementation, budget utilization, service delivery and implementation of projects of commune/sangkat administrations and local authorities",""],[1,"32","3","Strengthening Accountability Between Councils, Citizens, and Institutions","accountability between the council and the people, between the council and its administrative officers, and between the councils and the ministries and agencies has been gradually strengthened",""]],"12":[[1,"196","14","Policy Framework and Regulatory Development","Continuing to develop a policy framework and regulations.",""],[1,"196","15","Postal Sector Modernization and Partnership Expansion","Continuing to modernize the postal sector in line with international standard, especially receiving and distributing deposits to push the postal sector more efficiently and progressively at the international level with partnerships with domestic and international companies.",""],[1,"196","17","Training in Posts, Telecommunications, and ICT","Continuing to focus on (1) trainings of students and civil servants on posts, telecommunication, and ICT",""],[1,"196","17","Research and Innovation Support","and (2) research and innovation focusing on key activities include:",""],[1,"196","18","Training Capacity Strengthening through Private Sector and University Collaboration","Collaborating with the private sector and universities to strengthen training capacities.",""],[1,"196","20","E-Learning Training Promotion","Promoting e-learning training.",""],[1,"196","21","Promotion of Overseas and International Researchers and Innovators","Promoting overseas and international researchers and innovators.",""]],"13":[[1,"187","3","Digital Connectivity Infrastructure Expansion and Mobile Network Modernization","Enhancing digital connectivity by ways of expanding fiber optic cable distribution network infrastructure, backbone fiber optic infrastructure, and undersea fiber optic cables, along with the improvement and modernization of mobile telephone network to ensure quality, cost-competitive and nationwide service for all.",""],[1,"196","16","Telecommunications Backbone Expansion to Rural Areas","Continuing to expand the telecommunications backbone infrastructure to remote rural areas and potential economic and tourism potentials through (1) building fiber optic networks to all the provinces and districts that fill the ICT and (2) building a submarine fiber optic network from the Kingdom of Cambodia to China and developing the Greater Mekong Subregion-based telecommunications infrastructure.",""]],"14":[[1,"140","10","Public Service Digitalization and One-Window Service Integration","Improving the quality of public services through the use of information technology, service integration mechanism in the One Window Service mechanism.",""],[1,"140","15","Public Service Delivery Efficiency and Accountability Guidelines","Developing and implementing legal documents and guidelines for strengthening the efficiency and accountability of public service delivery units at national and sub- national levels.",""],[1,"140","16","Public Service Standards and ICT-Enabled Service Delivery","Promoting the development and implementation of public service standards in public service units to improve the standards of public service delivery and the use of ICT in the delivery of public services.",""],[1,"140","18","Expansion of Public Service Delivery Mechanisms","Continuing to expand the implementation of public service delivery mechanisms.",""],[1,"140","19","Public Service Delivery Innovation and Competition Promotion","Continuing and expanding the implementation of movement to promote competition of improving the innovation in public service delivery.",""],[1,"140","20","Public Service Delivery Innovation Fund","Establishing and introducing an innovation fund for improving public service delivery through promoting the innovation in public service delivery.",""],[1,"141","1","Model Public Service Unit Case Studies and Innovation Dissemination","Preparing case studies on model public service units and public service innovation and dissemination to promote the movement of public services delivery.",""],[1,"141","3","Public Service Quality Training and Dissemination Workshops","Training focal points and conducting dissemination workshops on improving the quality of public services at national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"141","4","Feedback and Complaints Handling Mechanism Improvement","Improving the efficiency of the implementation of the feedback and complaints handing mechanism at all public service delivery units.",""],[1,"141","5","Public Service Feedback and Complaints Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening the efficiency of the implementation of receiving and solving feedback mechanisms and complaints of service users at all public service delivery units.",""],[1,"142","12","Public Service Information Dissemination Expansion","The RGC will focus on (2) Strengthening and expanding public dissemination of updated information related to public services, legal instruments and national policy documents",""],[1,"142","12","Public Service Feedback and Complaints Handling Mechanism","The RGC will focus on (4) Enhancing the implementation mechanism for receiving feedback and handling complaints from public service users together with the assessment on the possible usage of automation system to support it",""],[1,"148","5","Civil Registration and Digital Identification System Development","Continuing to manage the identities of individuals more clearly identified by increasing the registration status of civil servants and promoting identification, developing civil registration systems, organizing unified systems, dividing people's data and launching electronic systems for providing services to the people with efficiency and transparency.",""]],"15":[[1,"74","11","Rural ICT Awareness and Adoption Mainstreaming","Mainstreamed awareness and promoting the use of ICT for the development of rural communities, especially for vulnerable people such as disabled persons, women, children, elderly, and ethnic people through volunteers, students and local authorities.",""]],"16":[[1,"126","10","Digital Economy Forum for the Fourth Industrial Revolution","digital economy forum implements in the 4th industrial revolution, the complexity of financial sector, an extensive collection of banking products, an ongoing reduction of non-bank users.",""],[1,"203","4","Long-Term Digital Economy Strategic Framework","Developing and implementing a long-term digital economy strategic framework while classifying digital sector as a sub-sector in the national accounts.",""],[1,"203","5","Telecommunication and ICT Policy and Regulatory Update","Further updating and implementing the telecommunication and ICT development policy, Master Plan for Information and Communication Technology as well as Law on Telecommunication, and relevant regulations, along with the development and implementation of a long-term ICT strategic framework.",""],[1,"203","6","Supporting Infrastructure Expansion and Development","Further strengthening and expanding the development of necessary supporting infrastructures, including ICT infrastructure, domestic postal and express delivery infrastructure and logistics and electronic payment infrastructure while assessing the possibility of developing a national internet gateway.",""],[1,"203","7","Digital Development Legal Framework","Promoting the establishment of a legal framework to support digital development, including the implementation of digital government and information security strategy, E-Commerce law, cybercrime law as well as amendment of laws and related regulations which underpin growth and prevent risks in this sector.",""],[1,"203","8","Digital Education and Training Program","Developing education and training program by focusing on the broad use of digital technology and incorporation of the use and awareness of digital technology into the academic curriculum, in line with market demand, along with the establishment of partnership mechanism between businesses and universities and vocational training institutions to create new digital skill development and training programs.",""],[1,"203","9","Entrepreneurship and Digital Ecosystem Development","Developing entrepreneurship and digital ecosystems that are conducive to the creation of new businesses, promoting the use of digital system in business, and establishing an entrepreneur cooperation mechanism within the RGC or some forms of partnership with the private sector.",""],[1,"205","11","ICT Industrial Park Development","Establishing an ICT industrial park and showing the evolution of the latest technology.",""],[1,"205","12","Rural ICT Awareness and Training Programme","Mainstreaming the awareness and promotion of the use of ICT in rural areas, especially for vulnerable people such as disabled persons, women and children, to reduce threats to women and children on the internet, and to provide short training courses on ICT to ministries and agencies, capital/provinces and other relevant entities.",""],[1,"205","14","Trade Policy and E-Commerce Regulatory Development","Developing policy, both legal and regulatory, in the field of trade, while responding to digital economy and industrial revolution 4.0: (1) developing trade policies in line with national, regional and global context, (2) promoting the establishment of law on E- commerce, (3) coordinating, strengthening and promoting the implementation of laws and regulations related to business activities through electronic system and management of market activities by issuing licenses and monitoring of risks, (4) continuing to manage system and filling of notices of secure transaction (www.setfo.gov.kh) to be more effective, safe, secure and reliability, and (5) developing the establishment, analysis, and evaluation of laws and legal regulations related to trade in line with the global context",""],[1,"205","15","Digital Economy Entrepreneurship and Business Practice Support","Developing entrepreneurship and business practices in the digital economy and responding to the Industrial Revolution 4.0: (1) strengthening the work of the Chamber of Commerce in all centers and disseminating the benefits of organizing and forming business associations through regulatory documents as well as strengthening the capacity of existing business associations, (2) continuing to promote and attract local and foregn traders and investors to participate in developing and producing of potential products, and (3) strengthening and expanding the number of workshops or training on packaging quality, base price, standards, and trademarks which showcase the idea of creating new products and how products circulate in the market.",""]],"17":[[1,"206","1","National Media Promotion and Broadcasting Expansion","Continuing to promote the national media and to encourage the private media to realize the efficiency potential, making broadcasting coverage widely reach people both in the country, in regions and in other continents.",""],[1,"206","2","Technical Material Modernization Plan for National Broadcasting","Preparing a technical material modernization plan for the national broadcasting team to respond to the need of the national official broadcasting.",""],[1,"206","3","Establishment of Sub-national Radio and Television Stations","Continuing to promote the establishment of sub-national radio and television stations in the provinces, prioritizing the provinces in north-western and north-eastern parts of the country",""],[1,"206","4","Technical Training and Capacity Building for Sub-national Media Officials","Promoting the technical trainings and capacity building for sub-national program and information production officials to allow national radio stations to broadcast live events at the national level and produce social education programs and issues related to women and children.",""],[1,"206","5","Press Law Implementation and Media Regulatory Framework Development","Promoting the implementation of the Law on the Press and continuing its research efforts to develop new legal frameworks for regulating the information and audiovisual sector in the framework of the rule of law, ensuring both the rights to freedom of expression, journalism, and democracy.",""],[1,"206","6","Private Sector and Civil Society Participation in the Information and Audiovisual Sector","Continuing to encourage and broaden the participation of the private sector, CSOs and NGOs in the information and audiovisual sector.",""],[1,"206","8","Social, Legal, Gender, and Child Awareness Promotion Programs","Creating all types of promotion such as social education, legal education, education programs on gender and children and awareness programs for all in collaboration with relevant ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"206","9","National Media Responsibility and Rapid Response Obligation","Through their modern media, all national media are obliged to contribute to promoting Cambodia's national identity and prestige on the international stage as well as to the timely reaction of all broadcasts and information that may be distorted and can cause harm to the harmony and the national peace or affect the rights of individuals as well as affecting the dignity of the general public.",""]],"18":[[1,"64","13","Public Transportation Service Automation System","Continued to implement the automation system to provide public transportation services to eliminate unofficial expenses, complicated procedures, transparency, fast delivery, and confidence to provide services closer to the citizen effectively.",""],[1,"65","18","Integrated Vehicle Registration and Identification Automation","Integrating registration of vehicle identification and vehicle registration with the automation system of the General Department of Customs and Excise, General Department of Taxation and the Directorate General of Identification.",""],[1,"187","18","Port Data Exchange System Deployment","Continuing to prepare and deploy port data exchange system.",""],[1,"189","13","Information Centers and Sectoral IT Development Plan for Logistics","Establishing the information centers and sectoral development plan for information technology in logistics.",""],[1,"190","4","Automated Driving License Management and Public Transport Service Expansion","Strengthening the management of registrations, technical checks and licensing of automated driving licenses and expanding the public transport service locations closer to the people.",""],[1,"190","5","Automated Transport Administration Systems and Inspection Expansion","Strengthening, promoting, and training on the use of automated systems for both national and sub-national officials (vehicle registration, driver's license, vehicle inspection, and logistics business registration).",""],[1,"190","5","Vehicle Inspection Center Expansion and Mobile Inspection","Promoting the additional establishment of vehicle inspection centers, and mobile vehicle inspection.",""],[1,"190","6","Automated Vehicle Management and Licensing System","Managing, monitoring and registering vehicles, issuing driving licenses, technical checks and public delivery through the automatic system.",""],[1,"190","7","Data Center Installation and Digital Service Security Upgrade","Installing data centers with high technology, maintaining data security, reducing costs, increasing accountability for services delivery.",""],[1,"190","8","Integrated Automatic Registration and Identification System","Continuing to integrate automatic registration system, ID card and vehicle number plates with the automatic system of the General Department of Taxation and the Directorate General of Identification.",""],[1,"190","9","Licensing Process Review and Streamlining","Reviewing the ability in the issuance of licenses of domestic and cross-border transportation, business licenses as soon as possible, with transparency and accountability.",""]],"19":[[1,"144","24","Good Governance Promotion Policy","the MONASRI has launched a policy of \"Promoting Good Governance through Education, Prevention of Inactive Phenomena, Increasing Accountability, Efficiency and Strengthening the rule of law\"",""],[1,"144","26","Legislative Drafting and Inspection Reform Support","continuing to participate in completing the draft Law on Inspection, Sub-decree on Inspection Procedures, draft Sub-decree on Professional Ethics of Inspection Officials and the drafting of relevant regulations as required by the Ministry",""],[1,"144","26","Public Legal Awareness Population Surveys","continuing to conduct population surveys on the understanding of local laws in the target provinces",""],[1,"144","27","Legal Awareness and Priority Laws Dissemination Campaign","continuing to promote the 11 priority laws to the people to raise their awareness about laws, rights, and obligations set in the laws, Land Law, Forestry Law, Fishery Law, Law on Domestic",""],[1,"145","1","Priority Laws Dissemination Preparation and Public Outreach","continuing to analyse situation and primary study on the 11 priority laws to measure the understanding level and legal requirements of the people by geography before starting the official law dissemination and (3) preparing roundtable discussions on TV and talk shows on radio.",""],[1,"145","4","Legal Dissemination and Law Enforcement Inspection Activities","Capital and provincial Department of the National Assembly-the Senate and Inspection of 25 provinces and cities will continue to disseminate laws, organize public forums, conduct surveys on people's understanding on laws, receive complaints and investigate, monitor law enforcement and inspection within departments within the 25 capital and provinces.",""],[1,"146","1","Judicial Service Strengthening and Justice Administration Modernization","Enhancing judicial service by improving work effectiveness of enforcement officials, strengthening public confidence in the judicial system, and fighting all kinds of abuse and violation in the society through (a) strengthening law enforcement, (b) strengthening cleanliness and professional ethics of enforcement officials, (c) strengthening work discipline mechanism and modernization of justice administration, (d) stepping up the provision of legal service, and (e) strengthening and improving conflict resolution mechanism which effectively respond to actual circumstances in the society",""],[1,"148","11","Law and Judicial Reform","Continuing to implement the Law and Judicial Reform to achieve seven Strategic Objectives",""],[1,"148","14","Improved Access to Legal and Judicial Information","Providing better access to legal and judicial information.",""],[1,"148","16","Judicial and Prosecutorial Services Strengthening","Strengthening the judicial services, including judicial and prosecutorial services.",""],[1,"148","17","Alternative Dispute Resolution Mechanisms","Introducing alternative dispute resolution mechanisms.",""],[1,"148","18","Legal and Judicial Sector Institutional Strengthening","Strengthening legal and judicial sector institutions to fulfill their mandates.",""],[1,"149","1","Legal and Judicial Framework Development and Promotion","Developing and promoting legal and judicial frameworks.",""],[1,"149","2","Women and Children Legislation Dissemination Strengthening","Strengthening and enhancing the dissemination law and legislations related to women and children.",""],[1,"149","5","Legal and Gender-Sensitive Training for Law Enforcement and Legal Professionals","training on fundamental laws, legislation related to woman and children and other skills to law enforcement officials, officials and Legal professionals.",""],[1,"149","6","Alternative Dispute Resolution Mechanisms","Developing alternative dispute resolution mechanisms.",""],[1,"149","7","Case Register Management System","Establishing new system for case register management.",""],[1,"149","9","Law Enforcement Monitoring and Evaluation","Conducting the monitoring and evaluation of law enforcement.",""],[1,"149","11","Capacity Building and Implementation Strengthening","Building capacity and strengthening the overall management and implementation.",""],[1,"149","12","Judicial Infrastructure Expansion and Improvement","Expanding and improving the ministry's infrastructure and municipal and provincial courts.",""],[1,"149","13","Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening and Expansion","Strengthening and expanding M&E.",""]],"20":[[1,"24","4","Public Security and Judicial Services Reform","first by reforming public security and judicial services, to deliver the trust of the general the public.",""],[1,"26","2","Anti-Corruption Education, Prevention, and Prosecution Measures","The RGC has given high priority to anti-corruption work and has expanded and enhanced the effectiveness of three core measures, including (1) strengthening education \"to stop corrupt practices, (2) preventing corruption, and (3) suppressing of crimes by referring all cases to court.",""],[1,"26","3","Anti-Corruption Education Mainstreaming Initiative","Implemented and mainstreamed Education to stop corruption practices to all targets by (1) including general education curricula from elementary to high school (Grades 4-12) (2) directing dissemination at national and sub-national levels, private institutions, academic institutions, and press organizations, along with the distribution of education materials produced by the Anti Curruption Unit and (3) organizing the celebration of the International Day Against Corruption and creating a poetry competition, writing short stories, singing songs, chapei songs, painting, comedy, etc. which is related to anti- corruption.",""],[1,"26","6","Transparency Observation of Recruitment, Examinations, Auctions, and Public Procurement","Participated in observation of the RGC's official recruitments, vocational school examinations, high school diploma examinations and observation on auction of seized forest products, and public procurement to strengthen transparency of collection of revenue and efficiency of expenditure by the ministries and institutions.",""],[1,"26","7","Asset and Liability Declaration System","Declaration of assets and liabilities every 2 years of new positions, resignation, termination, retirement, great success with the good cooperation of anti-corruption focal points at all ministries, institutions and provinces and the dissemination of the Law on Anti-Corruption.",""],[1,"27","4","Regional and International Anti-Corruption Cooperation","Cambodia to strengthen, expand and enhance regional and international anti- corruption efforts",""],[1,"28","5","Legal Framework Development and Drafting Programme","In order to strengthen the rule of law, the Ministry of Justice has collaborated with the development partners to develop and draft some important basic laws that Cambodia needs.","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"28","5","Judicial and Legal Reform Package","Additionally, the Ministry of Justice is also drafting Law on Criminal and Civilian Assistance and a number of legal documents.","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"28","5","Review and Comment on Draft Laws","The Ministry of Justice also plays an important role in reviewing and commenting on a number of laws drafted by the government ministries and institutions, especially comments related to the penalties.","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"28","6","Legal Code Dissemination and Distribution Initiative","The MOJ has organized the dissemination of law books, especially the four basic principles (Civil Code, Civil Procedure, Penal Code and Code of Criminal Procedure) to all legislatives, executive, courts, and all universities, state institutions and justice police in the capital, provinces, municipalities, districts and Khans throughout the country.","MOJ"],[1,"28","8","Systematic Case Management and Court Information Systems","The MOJ tested systematic case management systems in some provincial courts and in 2016 added additional mandatory management information systems and the administrative affairs website in 2017.","MOJ"],[1,"29","2","Appeal Court Construction and Feasibility Assessment","the MOJ is preparing to build Tbong Khmum Appeal Court and Battambang Provincial Court of Appeal and is checking the possibility of building a appeal court in Sihanoukville.","MOJ"],[1,"29","3","Legal Defense Support for the Poor","The MOJ has cooperated with the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia to organize the defense of the poor.","MOJ | Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia"],[1,"150","2","Political Stability and Sovereignty Protection Measures","Securing national sovereignty and territorial integrity by not allowing foreign interference in Cambodia's internal affairs; firmly preventing and cracking down on activities related to color revolution or incitements that could lead to political instability and social unrest",""],[1,"150","2","Rule of Law and Human Rights Reinforcement","Reinforcing the rule of law, democracy, peace culture, social morality, respect for human rights and dignity and ensuring a conducive environment for the normal functioning of public institutions",""],[1,"150","2","Crime Suppression and Safe Village/Commune Policy","Undertaking preventive measures and other actions to suppress all kinds of criminal activities, including terrorism and its financing, money laundering, illegal drug trafficking and drug use, human trafficking and sexual exploitation, and other transnational crimes, as well as continuing carrying out the \"Safe Village/Commune\" policy",""],[1,"150","2","Traffic Safety and Public Order Measures","Taking additional measures to improve traffic safety and public order; eliminating illegal checkpoints; and enforcing transport safety regulations so as to penalize non- roadworthiness trucks that damage road infrastructure and cause traffic accidents",""],[1,"150","2","Immigration Enforcement and Deportation Measures","Strengthening the enforcement of the Law on Nationality and the Law on Immigration by preventing the entry of illegal migrants through airports, land and maritime borders, and pursuing the search, arrest, and deportation for illegal immigrants back to their home countries",""],[1,"150","3","National Sovereignty Protection and Internal Security Enforcement","To implement the priority policies of the RGC of Cambodia, the MOI will continue to focus on (1) the protection of national sovereignty and territorial sovereignty, as well as the prevention and opposition to illegal acts, political instability or social unrest;","MOI"],[1,"150","3","Crime Prevention and Transboundary Crime Suppression","preventing and cracking down on all types of crimes, including combating terrorism and terrorist financing, anti-money laundering, combatting illegal activities related to drug trafficking and drug use, combating illegal activities related to human trafficking and sex business as well as fighting transboundary crimes along with the continued implementation of the \"Village and Commune Safety Policy\";","MOI"],[1,"150","3","Traffic Safety and Public Order Strengthening","Strengthening of traffic safety and public order;","MOI"],[1,"150","3","Nationality and Immigration Law Enforcement","continuing the enforcement of nationality and immigration law by preventing the influx of immigrants from land boundaries, airports and water borders with the search for illegal immigrants living in the Kingdom of Cambodia for relocation;","MOI"],[1,"151","1","National Sovereignty and Border Integrity Protection","Strengthening the defense of national sovereignty and the implementation of Nationality Law and Immigration Law by continuing to protect national sovereignty and territorial integrity, to solve land and water issues, and to continue to strengthen the implementation of nationality and immigration law.",""],[1,"151","2","Crime Prevention and Suppression Measures","Strengthening the measures to prevent and suppress crimes by continuing to prevent and crack down on all kinds of crimes and to continue to enforce laws, to raise awareness and provide professional training to officials at the Police Academy and continue to build capacity to prevent crimes by technology system.",""],[1,"151","3","Traffic Safety and Public Order Enforcement and Education","Strengthening traffic safety and public order by strengthening the implementation of laws, dissemination of all forms of education, and maintaining public security and public order.",""],[1,"151","5","National Sovereignty and Territorial Integrity Protection","Continuing to protect the national sovereignty and territorial integrity, and preventing and opposing all illegal activities, causing political instability or social unrest, especially preventing and eliminating the effectiveness of the color revolutionary movements, while continuing to adhere to the principles, not allowing the use of Cambodian territory against neighboring countries.",""],[1,"151","7","Strengthened Immigration Law Enforcement and Immigration Service Efficiency","Continuing to strengthen the enforcement of Nationality Law and Immigration Law by enhancing the efficiency of immigration services",""],[1,"151","7","Border Security and Transnational Crime Prevention Measures","controlling the prevention of terrorism, transnational crimes of all types, protecting national interests and citizens in accordance with relevant laws and regulations",""],[1,"151","7","Foreign Residence and Occupation Compliance Enforcement","continuing to strengthen its effectiveness of the presence of accommodation and occupations of the foreigners in the country",""],[1,"151","9","Crime Prevention and Law Enforcement Crackdown","Continuing to prevent and crack down on all types of criminal offenses, including combating terrorism and terrorist financing, anti-money laundering, fighting illegal activities related to drug trafficking and drug use, fighting illegal activities related to human trafficking and sexual businesses.",""],[1,"151","12","Law Enforcement and Public Order Awareness Programme","Continuing to strengthen law enforcement and dissemination activities in all aspects by continuing to promote education, advising people to participate in preserving public order, respecting Road Traffic Law, respecting law enforcement, and enhancing professional skills for police officers and the traffic police; continuing to raise awareness on Water and Road Traffic Laws and explain to citizens of conscience to law enforcement.",""],[1,"151","13","Public Security and Public Order Maintenance","Continuing to maintain public security and public order by continuing to safeguard security at all national and international events and to maintain the order of strike demonstrations by preventing violence.",""],[1,"151","13","Community Participation in Security and Social Order","Continuing to promote community participation in the movement of security, safety and social order to increase every year.",""]],"21":[[1,"94","4","Teacher Training Center Reform","Reform 3: Reform of the teacher training centers.",""],[1,"94","5","Teacher Qualifications Reform","Reform 4: Pomoting teacher's qualifications.",""],[1,"94","7","Upper Secondary School Examination Reform","Reform 7: Reform of the exam at upper secondary school.",""],[1,"94","8","Curriculum and Basic Textbook Reform","Reform 8: Reform of the curriculum and basic books.",""],[1,"94","9","School Building Construction and Repair Programme","Reform 9: Construction of the school buildings and repairing.",""],[1,"94","14","New Generation Schools Establishment Reform","Reform 14: Establishment of new generation schools.",""],[1,"94","15","Career Path and Principal Training Reform","Reform 15: Preparing career path and pricipal training.",""],[1,"163","14","Human Resource Development through Education, Science, and Technology Quality Improvement","Human resource development in the Sixth Legislature of the National Assembly will continue to focus on (1) strengthening of the quality of education, science, and technology",""],[1,"164","6","Teacher Performance Pay and School Management Reform","Further increasing the salaries and other bonuses of teachers and education staff based on their performance, enhancing the management capacity of school principals by linking the performance with school budget, enhancing teachers' qualifications, teaching ability and career path by increasing teacher training and pedagogy to at least the bachelor degrees, deploying high quality teachers to the areas short of teachers and creating mechanisms to help weak students with concrete incentives, research and development of new teaching and learning methods; further reforming examination and regular assessment of learning outcome; increasing investment in learning materials, experimental equipment and teaching facilities, especially expanding the coverage of new generation schools and enhancing the involvements from the communities and parents.",""],[1,"164","7","Village and Commune School Construction and Support Programme","Continuing to invest in the construction of primary schools at village level and the secondary schools at commune level based on actual socio-economic situation; continuing to provide scholarships and essential support to the poor students, students in difficult areas and students with disabilities",""],[1,"164","7","National Basic Education Awareness Campaign","organizing nationwide campaign to raise awareness on the importance of basic education",""],[1,"164","7","Early Childhood Development and Kindergarten Expansion","increasing investment in early childhood development and establishment of kindergarten classes",""],[1,"164","7","Student Performance Monitoring Information System","promoting the development of information technology system to monitor student performance aimed at timely intervention and prevention of school dropout",""],[1,"164","8","Comprehensive School Inspection and Monitoring System","Strengthening comprehensive inspection of school management to ensure the complete teaching in accordance with the curriculum and to improve the school governance by organizing mechanisms for regular involvement from stakeholders and creating feedback boxes; preparing schools' monitoring system as well as",""],[1,"165","1","National Response System Strengthening","effective and timely response system form the national level.",""],[1,"165","1","Quality Control Mechanisms in General Education Institutions","reviewing and strengthening the role of the quality control mechanisms in general education institutions will also receive the RGC's attention.",""],[1,"165","3","Entrepreneurship and Foreign Language Learning Programs","by designing programs to incite entrepreneurship and foreign language learning",""],[1,"165","3","STEM Education and Science Center Establishment","strengthening the STEM by establishing education and science center",""],[1,"165","3","Youth Life Skills and Leadership Programme","continuing to promote the life skills program, especially leadership program for youth, ethics and morality",""],[1,"165","3","Children and Youth Councils in Schools","along with establishment of children and youth councils at all schools",""],[1,"165","9","Education, Youth and Sport Reform Programme","The MOEYS continues to implement the education, youth and sport reform by focusing on 5 pillars","MOEYS"],[1,"165","10","Education Management Reform Strategy","Reform Strategy for Education Management: (1) reforming the study management based on regular study evaluation of the students, improving teaching methodology and including the quality citizenship in the curriculum and base study books; (2) reforming the administration management focusing on ensuring the participation of the students' parents and local communities, implementing the school management, and implementing education policies and",""],[1,"166","1","Education Financial Management Reform","reforming financial management focusing on increasing financial autonomy and accountability at school, auditing education budget regularly and increasing the allocation of budget linked with the education policies",""],[1,"166","1","Teacher Training and Staff Performance Management Reform","reforming human resource management focusing on teaching methodology based trainings and on-job training program, increasing teacher trainings and implementing the evaluation of the work of the education staff",""],[1,"166","8","Early Childhood Education Manager Capacity Building","Building capacity of the managers in early childhood education.",""],[1,"166","9","Measures to Increase Regular Schooling and Complete Primary Education","Taking measures to increase the regular schooling and complete the primary education, especially the children with difficulty.",""],[1,"166","10","Physical Infrastructure and Clean Learning Environment Improvement for Schools","Developing physical infrastructure and clean learning environment following the standard of the primary school, especially the schools which do not have all levels or have difficulty.",""],[1,"166","11","Teacher Qualification and Deployment Improvement","Improving the qualifications of existing teachers and improving teacher deployment.",""],[1,"166","12","First Grade Reading and Mathematics Capacity Building","Strengthening the capacity of teachers and stakeholders in first grade reading and math programs.",""],[1,"166","13","Primary Teacher Training Quality Improvement","Strengthening the quality of training for primary teachers.",""],[1,"166","14","Textbook and Teaching-Learning Materials Supply Improvement","Improving the supply and use of textbooks and teaching and learning materials.",""],[1,"166","15","Inspection and Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening","Strengthening inspection and monitoring and evaluation at all levels.",""],[1,"166","16","School-Based Management Strengthening","Strengthening the implementation of school-based management.",""],[1,"166","17","High School Attendance and Retention Improvement Measures","Taking measures to improve attendance and retention in high school, particularly in disadvantaged groups.",""],[1,"167","1","Secondary School Infrastructure and Facilities Expansion","Expanding the infrastructure and facilities for secondary schools.",""],[1,"167","2","STEM and Foreign Languages Expansion Initiative","Strengthening and expanding STEM and foreign languages to meet the 21st Century Skills Framework.",""],[1,"167","3","Curriculum Framework Implementation","Promoting the implementation of effective curriculum framework.",""],[1,"167","4","School-Based Management Strengthening","Enhancing the school-based management approaches.",""],[1,"167","5","New Generation School Standard Implementation Expansion","Expanding the implementation of a new generation school standard.",""],[1,"167","6","Secondary School Quality Assurance Framework","Developing a quality assurance framework of secondary schools.",""],[1,"167","7","School Inspection Monitoring and Evaluation System Enhancement","Enhancing monitoring and evaluation system of school inspections.",""]],"22":[[1,"88","4","Technical and Vocational Training and Apprenticeship Programme","Training with short-term certificates (less than one year), technical and vocational diploma, associate degree/high diploma, bachelor's degree of technology, diploma of engineering, Master's Degree, and apprenticeship trainings to participants, students in industry, business, techniques, handicrafts, tourism service and agriculture.",""],[1,"88","9","UNited for Youth Employment in Cambodia","Carried out UN joint Programme: \"UNited for Youth Employment in Cambodia\" to develop youths and young women to gain access to decent work and productive employment.",""],[1,"93","6","Youth Career Guidance and Entrepreneurship Training Programme","The MOEYS has continued to strengthen technical skills and soft skills for the youths by disseminating job market information to youths and organizing forums on labor education and labor market information for youths and entrepreneurship trainings.","MOEYS"],[1,"93","6","Career Counseling Documentation and Counselor Training Preparation","The MOEYS has prepared the documentation on career counseling and information on secondar career counselor training skill.","MOEYS"],[1,"94","12","Youth Policy Action Plan Implementation","Reform 12: Implementing the action plan of the youth policy.",""],[1,"126","15","Vocational and Technical Training Improvement","A basis for vocational and technical training, courses were improved including secondary school study",""],[1,"134","6","Support for the National Technical and Vocational Education and Skills Development Fund","Support the implementation of the National Technical and Vocational Education 2017- 2025 and Skills Development Fund.",""],[1,"138","2","Youth Employment and Skills Development Initiative","Creating more jobs, in terms of both quality and quantity aspects, for the citizens of Cambodia, especially for the youth through skill training, provision of job market information, improvement in working condition and promotion of business and investment inside and outside the country.",""],[1,"165","2","Technical Education Master Plan Implementation","Updating and pushing for the implementation of the master plan for technical education at upper secondary schools aiming to enhance career orientation and expand technical education coverage nationwide",""],[1,"165","2","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Technical Education","promoting participation from the private sectors especially through the public-private partnership (PPP) mechanism",""],[1,"166","3","Youth Education and Vocational Training Opportunities","providing opportunities to the youths to obtain education and vocational training with quality and equity",""],[1,"167","8","Private Sector Partnerships for Technical Education","Expanding partnerships with the private sector and enterprises to enhance technical education.",""],[1,"167","9","Academic-Oriented and Technical Education Expansion","Strengthening academic-oriented education and expanding technical education.",""],[1,"170","1","National Technical Vocational Education and Training Policy Implementation","Continuing to implement the \"National Technical Vocational Education and Training Policy 2017-2025\" aiming to enhance technical skills training, especially at intermediate and advanced levels by covering multi-skill courses in response to the demand of the labour market, industry sector and new business start-ups.",""],[1,"170","2","School-Enterprise Training Cooperation","Enhancing training cooperation between schools and enterprises to improve the technical competency and productivity of the employed labor force, curriculum arrangement for skill transformation management aligned with new technological and pushing for the establishment of \"National Skills Development Fund\".",""],[1,"170","3","Technical Training Center Responsiveness Enhancement","Further enhancing technical training centers' responsiveness to the actual demand of each sector, especially in support of industrial development, through cooperation between the state, private sector and non-governmental organizations, along with the enhancement of the cooperation between training institutions and enterprises on technical skills training to improve the quality and responsiveness to new developments.",""],[1,"170","4","Technical and Vocational Training Institution Rationalization and Development","Rationalizing and developing the technical and vocational training institutions to supply various skills responding to the demand of both labour market and business start-ups in collaboration with the private sector.",""],[1,"170","5","Vocational Orientation in Secondary and High Schools","Providing vocational orientation at secondary and high school levels within the general education system",""],[1,"170","5","Awareness Campaign on Technical and Vocational Skills","further raising awareness on the importance and necessity of technical and vocational skills for building the future of youth, their families and the country",""],[1,"170","8","Teaching and Learning Methods Enhancement","Enhancing new teaching and learning methods, such as search rules and other rules, to ensure students have 21st century skills.",""],[1,"170","9","Life Skills, Career Counseling, and Youth Clubs Expansion","Expanding life skills education, career counseling, youth councils and clubs in Mathematics, Science, History and Khmer Literature.",""],[1,"170","11","Curriculum Framework Development for Industry 4.0","Developing a curriculum framework in response to the Industrial Revolution 4.",""],[1,"170","12","STEM and Creative Arts Skills Training","Training skills in science, technology, engineering, creative arts and mathematics.",""],[1,"170","15","Youth Business and Entrepreneurship Mainstreaming Programme","Mainstreaming the basic knowledge of business and entrepreneurship to youths in school and the community entrepreneurship development for out-of-school youth and integrating it into life skills curriculum.",""],[1,"170","18","Technical and Vocational Training Development and Scholarship Support","Continuing to develop technical and vocational trainings, consisting of quality and fluent skills aligned with labor market requirements, both internally and externally.",""],[1,"170","18","Youth Scholarship Access to Technical and Vocational Training","Continuing to provide scholarships and ease the access of youth to technical and vocational trainings.",""]],"23":[[1,"165","4","Higher Education Curriculum and Quality Reform","Preparing a comprehensive curriculum framework including the STEM and key social science subjects for higher education in accordance with the national qualification framework, regional and international standards; strengthening higher education quality accreditation mechanism; increasing the number of professors holding doctorates at the higher education level; increase investment in higher education and establishing the national policy framework to develop scholarship and loan funds for higher education students; enhancing capacity building and resources to support learning, teaching and research; establishing research funds and incentivizing achievement contest along with the establishment of the national policy framework for the governance and management of higher education.",""],[1,"166","2","Tertiary Education Reform Strategy","Tertiary Education Reform Strategy: (1) checking the ability to transform the public tertiary education institutions to the administrative public tertiary education institutions; (2) providing autonomy to the public tertiary education institutions in managing finance and human resource; (3) preparing the curriculum framework to respond to industry revolution; (4) encouraging the research and the creating an excellence research center at the public tertiary education institutions; and (5) evaluating the internal education quality and evaluating the education quality at the tertiary education institution.",""],[1,"167","10","Outcome-Based Investment in Priority Higher Education Programs","Increasing investments in priority higher education programs based on outcomes.",""],[1,"167","11","Higher Education Partnerships for Teaching, Learning, and Research","Improving teaching and learning capabilities and research through the establishment of higher education partnerships.",""],[1,"167","13","Higher Education Institutional Autonomy Strengthening","Strengthening the financial and human resources management system of higher education institutions toward full autonomy.",""]],"24":[[1,"153","2","Family and Traditional Religious Values Promotion","the Ministry of Cults and Religions (MCR) will continue to actively promote the role of family and adherence to the traditional religious values of the Kingdom.","Ministry of Cults and Religions (MCR)"],[1,"153","2","Buddhism Education Expansion and Dissemination","The MCR will continue to strengthen and expand Buddhism education at all levels, publish and disseminate the Buddhism bibles and strengthen the execution of Buddhism rules by cooperating with the two Samdech Preah Sangkareach.","Ministry of Cults and Religions (MCR)"],[1,"153","2","Support for Other Religions' Rights and Freedoms","In addition, the MCR supports the activities and promotes the rights and freedon in other religions to contribute to the social development.","Ministry of Cults and Religions (MCR)"],[1,"153","3","Promotion of State Religion and Religious Harmonization Policy","the MCR will introduce one priority policy \"Promotion of the state religion, value of the social ethics, and religion harmonization\" with the following key activities:",""],[1,"153","4","Buddhism Education Coordination and Training Programme","Continuing to coordinate the Buddhism education to train human resource among the monks from Buddhism rules level to tertiary education and higher.",""],[1,"153","6","Human Resources Training Across Education Levels","Continuing to train the human resources from primary to tertiary education in compliance with the national and international standard.",""],[1,"153","7","Expansion of Buddhim Education Schools","Continuing to expand the Buddhim Education Schools at the local level.",""],[1,"153","9","Country-wide Monk Congress and Dissemination Initiative","Organizing the country-wide monk congress and disseminating at all capital and provinces.",""],[1,"153","11","Buddhism Theory Education Dissemination Program","Continuing to disseminate the Buddhism theory educating at school through Buddhism context program in cooperation with line ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"153","12","Buddhist Texts and Ritual Rules Research and Compilation Initiative","Paying attention to cooperate with line ministries and agencies to promote the research and compilation of all Buddhism bibles, rules, wedding rules, and rules for other rituals and Buddhism rituals.",""],[1,"153","14","Religious Structures Management Law and Policy Development","Continuing to formulate laws and policies for the management and organization of all religious structures in the Kingdom of Cambodia.",""],[1,"153","16","Supervision of Religious Organizations","Continuing to guide and supervise religious organizations under the supervision of the Ministry, monasteries, religion research centers, and all religious organizations that carry out religious activities in accordance with State law.","the Ministry"],[1,"153","17","Religious Sector Inspection and Issue Resolution","Continuing to inspect the religious sector and facilitate the resolution of the issues.",""],[1,"153","18","Monastery Library Establishment Initiative","Continuing to promote the establishment of libraries in monasteries for the benefits of the public, including clergy in the Kingdom of Cambodia.",""],[1,"153","19","Religious Institutions as Education Centers Initiative","urging the monasteries and religious temples to become the education centers on mentality, ethics, culture and social affairs, maintaining the harmonization and freedom in all religious beliefs.",""]],"25":[[1,"171","9","Health Research Development Programme","enhancing health research development including research on communicable and non-communicable diseases;",""],[1,"175","3","Health Information Management Legal and Protocol Framework","Develop and implement legal tools and protocols for health information management.",""],[1,"175","4","Health Data Quality Improvement Initiative","Increase the quality, reliability and validity of health and health related data and information.",""],[1,"175","5","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Data Management","Improve institutional capacity on data management, especially at facilities and district level on data compilation, analysis, interpretation, reporting, dissemination and use.",""],[1,"175","7","Monitoring and Evaluation System Strengthening","Strengthen monitoring and evaluation system and promote health research.",""],[1,"175","7","Health Research Promotion","Strengthen monitoring and evaluation system and promote health research.",""]],"26":[[1,"172","7","Reproductive Health and Maternal-Child Mortality Reduction Programme","Improve reproductive health, and reduce maternal, newborn and child mortality and malnutrition among women and young children.",""],[1,"181","3","Public Awareness for Reproductive and Maternal Health","Increasing public awareness in promoting reproductive health, reducing maternal and child mortality, malnutrition among women and children, reducing the death by communicable diseases, non-communicable diseases and other public health problems.",""],[1,"182","5","Stage Sponsorship Program for Poor Households","Launching a Stage Sponsorship Program for Poor Households by adding midwifery support in the mid 2019.",""]],"27":[[1,"171","8","Universal Health Coverage Expansion","Pushing for universal health coverage in Cambodia by expanding the coverage of health equity fund, continuing to implement national social security on healthcare for civil servants, retirees and veterans, and healthcare scheme for workers-employees under the labor law, and organizing healthcare scheme for self-employed individuals.",""],[1,"172","5","Health Protection and Financial Risk Prevention Policy","the RGC will pay high attention on the strategic policy \"Promoting better Cambodian people's health and increasing the prevention from financial risks in receiving health protection services.\"",""],[1,"174","1","Health Service Coverage and Accessibility Expansion","Increase coverage of and accessibility to quality, safe and effective health services and information for the population, especially vulnerable people and in hard-to-reach areas.",""],[1,"174","6","Increase National Health Spending","Increase national health spending in accordance with economic growth and increased fiscal capacity.",""],[1,"177","20","Universal Health Coverage Expansion","Promoting the global health coverage in Cambodia, increasing the coverage of health equity funds, continuing to implement the Social Security Fund for the public officials, former civil servants, veterans, and health care for workers and developing health care for self-employed individuals.",""],[1,"179","1","Health Equity Fund","has put in place health equity fund",""],[1,"179","1","National Social Security for Healthcare and Occupational Risks","national social security on healthcare and occupational risks for workers-employees under the labor law",""],[1,"179","1","Civil Servants, Retirees and Veterans Health Insurance Scheme","healthcare insurance scheme for civil servants, retirees and veterans",""]],"28":[[1,"171","9","Disease Surveillance and Response System Strengthening","further strengthening systems for investigating, monitoring and responding to diseases in accordance with the international health regulatory requirements.",""],[1,"172","3","Communicable Disease Prevention and Awareness Campaign","Promoting the implementation of measures to prevent and reduce communicable diseases by cooperating with the community and stakeholders to raise awareness on hygiene, food safety, healthcare, effects of chemical products, alcohol and tobacco, and impact of climate change on human health.",""],[1,"175","6","National Disease Surveillance and Response System Enhancement","Enhance the national disease surveillance and response systems, including public health emergency and disease reporting system.",""]],"29":[[1,"152","1","Implementation of the 3-Year National Drug Control Plan","The National Authority for Combating Drugs (NACD), will continue to efficiently implement the five strategy plans of the 3-Year National Plan on Drug Control.","National Authority for Combating Drugs (NACD)"],[1,"152","2","Drug Abuse Prevention Education and Awareness Programme","Education, awareness raising, prevention and saying no to drugs: increasing public awareness of the harmful effects and the impact of illicit drugs upon society.",""],[1,"152","2","School Curriculum Integration on Drug and HIV/AIDS Prevention","Facilitate with relevant ministries and institutions to promote and integrate the program of education on illicit drug and HIV/AIDS from the abuse of drugs into the school curricula of both in formal and non-formal education systems.","relevant ministries and institutions"],[1,"152","2","Drug Abuse Prevention Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Promote and prepare mechanism for monitoring and evaluation of drug abuse prevention activities to ensure the future effectiveness.",""],[1,"152","3","Community-Based Drug Treatment and Reintegration Services","Community based treatment for drug users through drugs and health services of the Ministry of Health.","Ministry of Health"],[1,"152","3","Methadone Maintenance Treatment Programme","Methadone maintenance treatment program in Cambodia.",""],[1,"152","3","Drug Abuse Treatment, Rehabilitation and Reintegration Policy Development","Development of a drug abuse treatment, rehabilitation and reintegration draft policy.",""],[1,"152","3","Drug Treatment and Rehabilitation Center Establishment","The establishment of the structure of the center for drug treatment, rehabilitation and reintegration of drugs addicts.",""],[1,"152","3","Community-Level Drug Counseling Teams","The creation of a counseling team at the community level.",""],[1,"152","3","Capacity Expansion for Drug Treatment and Rehabilitation Centers","Increasing the capacities of drug treatment, rehabilitation centers.",""],[1,"152","4","Law Enforcement Strengthening for Drug Control","Strengthening the effectiveness of law enforcement agencies: intensify the effectiveness implementation of legislation affairs.",""],[1,"152","4","Border Liaison Office Expansion","Strengthening and expanding the Border Liaison Offices (BLO's).",""],[1,"152","4","NACD Laboratory Capacity Building","Strengthening the capacity of the NACD laboratory officials.",""],[1,"152","4","Computer-Based Training for Law Enforcement Officers","Continue using the mechanism of Computer-Based Training (CBT) to strengthen law enforcement officers.",""],[1,"152","4","Law Enforcement Support for Harm Reduction","Strengthening the law enforcement affairs to support Harm Reduction programme.",""],[1,"152","5","Precursor Chemicals Control Plan","Precursor chemicals control: strictly control of precursors chemical and psychotropic substances.",""],[1,"152","6","Green Villages and Communes Drug-Free Border Mechanism","Intensify the mechanism of green villages and communes' drug-free along the borders.",""],[1,"152","6","Border Liaison Office Strengthening","Strengthening the mechanism of Border Liaison Office (BLOs).",""],[1,"152","7","International Drug Control Cooperation and Convention Implementation","Strengthening and expansion of the implementation of all binding obligation stipulated in the agreements and international drugs control conventions and Promote international cooperation with other countries in order to seek the support and assistances in all drugs control activities.",""],[1,"153","1","Drug Control Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening mechanism of drug control at national and sub-national level: strengthening the structure of the NACD within national and sub-national level.",""]],"30":[[1,"97","7","Financial Risk Protection for Health Services","Financial risk prevention for access to health services aims to remove financial barriers to health care and to protect people, especially the poor and vulnerable people, from falling into poverty as a result of the cost of health care.",""],[1,"99","7","Public Financial Management Reform","The ongoing Public Financial Management Reform has provided opportunities for the MOH to improve the cost effectiveness.","MOH"],[1,"99","7","Performance-Based Health Service Delivery Mechanism","The effectiveness and responsiveness of public health providers has been promoted through a mechanism that combines the delivery of services to financial resources such as incentives for midwife, service delivery packages, and special agencies.",""],[1,"99","8","Primary Health Care Equity Financing Expansion","Access to health services and in health financing has been continuously promoted as a result of using resources that are targeted towards primary health care delivery in rural areas and the expansion of the coverage of equity fund, along with more health financing interventions.",""],[1,"99","9","Health Regulation Enforcement and Decentralization","Progress has been made in strengthening the enforcement of health rgulations, especially the elimination of illegal private services and counterfeit pharmaceutical products.",""],[1,"107","6","Health Care Services for Civil Servant Retirees and Invalid Civil Servants","As early as 2018, the NSSF for the Civil Servants cooperated with the NSSF to provide health care services to the retirees and invalid civil servants, who are being offered health care services in health facilities that have signed a contract with the NSSF from January 2018.",""]],"31":[[1,"34","7","Prison Health Services Strengthening","Prison health work related to technique, medicines, medical equipment and treatment was worked in the collaboration with the Ministry of Health and relevant stakeholders.","Ministry of Health"],[1,"172","4","Allowance Scheme for Pregnant Women and Children Under Two","Implementing allowance scheme for pregnant women and children under 2 of the poor families",""],[1,"172","4","Nutrition Enhancement Interventions","implementing interventions to enhance nutrition",""],[1,"172","4","Multi-Sectoral Nutrition Governance Mechanism","putting in place multi-sectoral mechanism with participation from the community and sub-national administration governing areas of insufficient nutrition",""],[1,"176","21","Feeding Practices Improvement Initiative","· Improve feeding practices.",""],[1,"177","11","Community-Led Nutrition and Food Security Programmes","Community-led nutrition and food security programmes with support for sub-national coordination and implementation.",""],[1,"177","13","Infant and Young Child Feeding Promotion","Promote the implementation of infant and young child feeding practices, especially breast-feeding and feeding.",""],[1,"177","14","Expand Coverage of Nutritional Supplements and Pills","Increase the coverage of nutritional supplements and pills by focusing attention in difficult areas.",""],[1,"177","15","Multidisciplinary Supplement Coverage Expansion","Increase the coverage of multidisciplinary supplements (Multi-micronutrient powder for children, fish sauce, soy sauce, iron and iodised salt).",""],[1,"177","16","Local and Community-Based Integration Services Strengthening","Strengthening local and community-based integration services, including child growth monitoring and nutrition counseling.",""],[1,"177","17","Severe Malnutrition Hospital Management Strengthening","Strengthen the management of severe malnutrition in the hospital.",""],[1,"177","18","Nutrition Law Enforcement and Advertising Restriction","Strengthen enforcement of nutrition laws such as restricting advertisements and promoting the use of dairy products.",""],[1,"177","21","Maternal and Child Nutrition Promotion for Poor Families","Implementing the promotion of pregnant women and children under 2 years old of poor families, organizing interventions to promote nutrition and develop multi-sectoral mechanisms, with the involvement of the communities and SNAs in the area which affected by high levels of malnutrition.",""],[1,"178","1","Micronutrient Nutrition Promotion Activities","the Ministry of Planning will promote the nutritional status of micronutrients into the following activities:","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"178","3","Micronutrient Fortification Expansion","Extending the fortification of micronutrients into other appropriate foods and ensure the required quality and quantity.",""],[1,"178","4","Micronutrient Standard List Integration","Promoting the incorporation of each level of micronutrients into the national standard list.",""],[1,"178","6","Micronutrient Fortification Promotion","Promoting the importance of the use of micronutrient (iodized salt, fish sauce, and soy sauce, and micronutrients-fortified rice).",""]],"32":[[1,"178","2","Micronutrient Food Fortification Policy and Enforcement Framework","Establishing national policies, technical guidelines, regulations, law on fortification of micronutrients into food, and promoting the effective enforcement of existing laws and regulations.",""],[1,"178","10","Policy Framework and Regulatory Promotion","Promoting policy frameworks and regulations.",""]],"33":[[1,"32","3","Gender Equity and Women’s Leadership Mainstreaming in SNA Management","principles for promoting gender, equity, social equity and strategies increase women in management positions were mainstreamed into work processes and the management system of SNA",""],[1,"179","4","Women's Leadership Capacity and Representation Promotion","Further promoting women's role in the society through enhancing their capacity and the proportion of women within the leadership roles at both national and sub-national levels, in ministries-institutions both in political and technical positions.",""],[1,"179","5","Gender Mainstreaming in Development Policies and Plans","Updating and implementing Neary Rattanak Strategic Plan by continuing to mainstream gender in development policies and plans in all sectors and at all levels",""],[1,"179","5","Women's Entrepreneurship Promotion through Education and Training","further promoting women's entrepreneurship through expanded education, technical and vocational training for women",""],[1,"179","8","Gender Equality Policy Development and Implementation","The RGC in the Sixth Mandate through the Ministry of Women's Affairs will develop and implement the Gender Equality Policy through mainstreaming gender and the implementation of the Convention on the Prevention of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women in all sectors and development programs to reduce poverty and vulnerability of women, especially women with disabilities, indigenous women minorities.","Ministry of Women's Affairs"],[1,"179","8","Women's Economic Empowerment and Participation Measures","In this context, the ministry will continue to pay special attention to economic empowerment of women, women's decision-making in the public sector and politics, preventing violence against women and girls, health and education for women and girls, and strengthening the mechanisms to mainstream gender in sectors and national programs, including the program of climate change and green development.","Ministry of Women's Affairs"],[1,"180","1","Gender Mainstreaming Coordination and Women's Economic Empowerment","The MOWA will continue to lead the coordination in mainstreaming gender in programs and education systems and promoting women's economic empowerment and improving the living conditions of the community through:","MOWA"],[1,"180","2","Women Development Centers Business Development Services Strengthening","Strengthening the creative, innovative, and inclusive entrepreneurial and business development services of the Women Development Centers.",""],[1,"180","3","Women’s Technical and Vocational Skills Development Programme","Increasing the opportunity, the friendly environment, the peace and the possibility of women getting the suitable jobs, the development of technical and vocational skills, including digital technology following the women's needs and market demand, in particular the standard techniques.",""],[1,"180","4","Private Sector Partnership for Entrepreneurship and Market Expansion","Expanding partnerships with the private sector and relevant partners in promoting entrepreneurship and potential development, experience and techniques to increase product productivity and reach national and regional markets.",""],[1,"180","6","Vocational Training and SME Support Initiative","Promoting vocational trainings, supporting small and medium enterprises, including the National Entrepreneurship Fund and the Center for Entrepreneurship Development responding to gender equality.",""],[1,"180","16","Women's Leadership Promotion Initiative","The MOWA will work with stakeholders to promote women's leadership in the public sector and politics through:","MOWA"],[1,"180","18","Gender Equality Awareness and Advocacy Campaign","Raising awareness and attention of the public and stakeholders about the value, the necessity of gender equality, women's participation in development and governance.",""],[1,"181","1","Gender Equality in Access to Health Services Initiative","The MOWA will continue to promote gender equality in accessing health services and related work to ensure healthy living of the people and improve the well-being of all people and all ages through:","MOWA"],[1,"181","2","Gender Mainstreaming in Programs and Health Strategic Plans","Mainstreaming gender into programs, policies and health-related strategic plans.",""],[1,"181","4","Gender Mainstreaming Mechanism and Capacity Strengthening","The MOWA will strengthen the mechanism and capacity in inclusively mainstreaming gender in policy, sectoral planning, reform programs through:","MOWA"],[1,"181","5","National Gender Equality Policy and Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","Designing National Policy on Gender Equality and the M&E Framework of the implemenaing of the national policies.",""],[1,"181","6","Gender Mainstreaming Capacity and Coordination Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity and mechanism capacity in mainstreaming gender including the Gender Mainstreaming Working Group and the Strategic Plan for Sector Gender Mainstreaming.",""],[1,"181","7","Strategy on Gender and Climate Change, Disaster Management and Green Development","Continuing to implement the Strategy on Gender and Climate Change, Disaster Management and Green Development.",""]],"34":[[1,"23","3","Poverty Reduction and Social Protection Policy Package","Achieving the poverty reduction target of below 10%, preventing the return of poverty by focusing on enhancing market participation, implementing social protection policy, lowering burden of daily life along with the provision of quality public services, and reducing social gaps.",""],[1,"24","3","Social Security and Healthcare System Strengthening","Reap the full benefits of the demographic dividend and low dependency ratio, to build social security and healthcare systems.",""]],"35":[[1,"89","13","Social Security Fund Implementation and Scheme Expansion","The implementation of social security fund as well as the expansion of the existing scheme to increase protection for all people is time-consuming, likewise, the need of resources to operate.",""],[1,"107","4","Support for the National Social Security Fund for Civil Servants","To support the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) for Civil Servants, the RGC has paid 18% of contributions and the civil servants pay 6% of the monthly salary, but currently, the RGC is responsible for a portion of the contribution instead of the civil servants.",""],[1,"107","4","Social Security System Adjustment","Along with the full support of the National Social Security Fund for Civil Servants, the RGC has also focused on adjusting the social security system in order to meet the economic growth and the affordability of the national budget.",""],[1,"108","6","Civil Servant Social Security Contribution Collection","The RGC continues to cover the support of former civil servants and people in burden.",""],[1,"109","5","Comprehensive Social Security System Development","The Ministry has been studying documents to develop a comprehensive social security system for the general people.","The Ministry"],[1,"126","15","Social Protection Reform","Social protection reform was implementing covering on main life cycles, a continuing effort to formalize job market",""],[1,"129","1","National Social Protection Policy Framework Implementation Support","Continuing to support the implementation of the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025 through implementing pension increasing policy for former civil servants and veterans including bridging the gap between old and new retirees.",""],[1,"130","4","Modern Social Security System Development","This work will coincide with the development of the modern social security system, facilitating savings through independent social insurance funds provided for formal sector workers and by providing social assistance for the poor and victims.",""],[1,"131","18","Social Security Scheme Expansion","Social insurance: Create a new Social Security scheme and expand coverage of existing schemes for pensions and health care and later for the unemployed.",""],[1,"134","5","Implementation of the National Social Protection Policy Framework","Support the implementation of the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016- 2025.",""],[1,"141","14","Social Security System Expansion for Veterans and Their Families","Preparing and increasing a social security system and veterans and families of veterans.",""]],"36":[[1,"179","5","Gender Equity Investment and Anti-Trafficking Partnership","uplifting social morality, the values of women and Cambodian family through investing in gender equity along with strengthened partnership between stakeholders prevent trafficking of and violence against women- children",""],[1,"180","7","Positive Child Raising Strategy Implementation","Continuing to implement the Strategy on Positive Child Raising that respond to the National Action Plan on the Prevention of Violence Against Women and Children.",""],[1,"180","8","Coordination of Violence Prevention and Anti-Trafficking Action Plans","The MOWA will coordinate the prevention of violence against women and children by updating and implementing the third National Action Plan on the Prevention of Violence against Women, implementing the Action Plan on Promotion of Social Morality, Value of Cambodia Women and Families, and implementing the Action Plan against Human Trafficking through:","MOWA"],[1,"180","9","Public Awareness and Enforcement of Violence Prevention Laws","Promoting public awareness of the culture of nonviolence, social morality, and strengthening the enforcement of the laws related to the prevention of violence against women.",""],[1,"180","10","Mixed Service Center for Women and Girls Facing Violence","Creating and improving social services, health services and legal services, especially, creating a mixed service center for women and girls suffering from all forms of violence.",""],[1,"180","11","Policy and Legal Review and Revision","Establishing and revising relevant policies and laws.",""],[1,"180","12","Capacity Development for Prevention of Violence and Discrimination Against Women and Children","Developing the capacity at national and sub-national level, including the prevention of violence against women and children, including eliminating all forms of discrimination against women with disabilities and women in vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"180","13","Implementation of the Fourth Mekong Sub-Region Plan","Continuing to implement the fourth Mekong Sub-Region Plan",""],[1,"180","13","National Cooperation Committee for Combating Human Trafficking","and the National Cooperation Committee of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking.",""],[1,"180","14","Third National Plan of Action Against Sexual Violence","Leading and coordinating the preparation and implementation of the third National Plan of Action against Sexual Violence in 2019-2023.",""],[1,"182","4","Protection Services for Victims of Human Trafficking and Sexual Assault","Providing protection for victims of human trafficking and sexual assault.",""],[1,"266","7","Mixed-Service Centres for Women and Girls Affected by Violence","Numbers of mixed-service centre for women and girls affected by all forms of violence in order to facilitate legal services, social services, health services, and other services to the victims",""]],"37":[[1,"126","10","Social Protection Expansion","and an annual improvement of the provided social protection.",""],[1,"131","19","Social Assistance Expansion for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","Social Assistance: Initial social assistance projects for the poor and vulnerable starting with childbirth beginning mid-2019 and later on scholarships and school feeding programs, vocational training, pensions for the elderly, healthcare for the disabled.",""],[1,"132","1","Integration of Social Protection with National Registration and Identification System","Link to the national registration and identification system, identify poor families, and provide operator registration to improve efficiency.",""],[1,"135","1","Human Resource Development and Social Protection Expansion","Over the next five years, with a peace, political stability and territorial integrity, the RGC in the sixth mandate of the National Assembly continues to focus on: 1) Human resource development, people's welfare, and social protection and other social benefits programs; 2) Institutional coordination and good governance.",""],[1,"138","3","Market Participation and Social Protection Measures","Achieving the poverty reduction target of below 10%, preventing the return of poverty by focusing on enhancing market participation, implementing social protection policy, lowering burden of daily life along with the provision of quality public services, and reducing social gap.",""],[1,"179","1","Social Protection Policy Framework Implementation","Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025\" which is comprehensive and respond to actual level of national development along with the reestablishment of its management institutions.",""],[1,"179","1","Food Reserve Program","the RGC is implementing the food reserve program",""],[1,"179","1","School Feeding Program","school feeding program",""],[1,"179","1","Scholarship Program","scholarship program",""],[1,"179","1","Cash Support for Pregnant Women and Poor Children","cash support to pregnant women and children of the poor families",""],[1,"179","6","Occupational Risk Scheme for Civil Servants","Pushing for the implementation of National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025 especially by putting in place the occupational risk scheme for civil servants",""],[1,"179","6","Pension Scheme for Workers Covered by Labor Law","Pushing for the implementation of National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025 especially by putting in place ... pension scheme for workers-employees covered by labor law",""],[1,"179","6","Civil Servants Pension Reform","reforming the pension scheme for civil servants",""],[1,"179","6","Integration of Social Security Operators into Social Protection Governance","integrating the social security operators into the social protection governance framework",""],[1,"179","6","Implementation of National Policy on Ageing 2017-2030","along with the implementation of National Policy on Ageing 2017-2030",""],[1,"179","7","Social Assistance Legal Framework and Coverage Expansion","Preparing the legal framework and supporting infrastructure in order to implement the new social assistance programs and widen the coverage of existing programs to provide better support to the poor and vulnerable group",""],[1,"179","7","New Social Security Schemes and Universal Social Protection Expansion","to put in place new social security schemes while expanding the coverage of existing ones to provide social protection service to every citizen",""],[1,"182","6","Identity Management System Integration for Social Protection","Linking the Identity Management System and the General Population Register, the Poor and Vulnerable Identity Management System, and the System of Operators to improve work efficiency, reduce time and expenditure, and increase people's awareness on social protection system.",""],[1,"182","20","Civil Servants Social Security Fund Service Development","Developing services to provide social security fund for civil servants efficiently",""],[1,"182","21","Civil Servants Social Security Fund","Providing social security fund for civil servants.",""],[1,"182","22","Veterans and Families Social Security Fund Service Efficiency Improvement","Increasing the efficiency of the services to provide social security fund for veterans and families",""],[1,"183","1","Social Security Fund Service Efficiency Improvement","Increasing the efficiency of the services to provide social security fund for veterans and families.",""]],"38":[[1,"106","10","Cambodia Ageing Day and International Ageing Day Commemoration","Organized Cambodia Ageing Day and Internaional Ageing Day on 01 October each year to promote the dignity and integrity of the elderly.",""],[1,"106","12","Elderly Association and Elderly Fund","The ministry has created an association of the elderly and is setting up an elderly fund to sustain protection for the elderly.",""],[1,"107","3","Social Protection and Welfare Expansion for Vulnerable Elderly People","The elderly people who experience financial insecurity and are inable to work need to be under the social protection and welfare project.",""],[1,"107","7","Retirement Pension Increase and Social Security Fund Payment Procedure","In the 5 years between 2014-2018, the RGC has raised the average retirement pension for unemployed and unqualified people every year, with a growth rate of around 42%.",""],[1,"179","6","Implementation of National Population Policy 2016-2030","along with the implementation of National Population Policy 2016-2030",""],[1,"182","15","Strengthening Elderly People Associations in Communes and Sangkats","Strengthening the activities of the elderly people associations in communes/Sangkats.",""],[1,"182","16","Elder Support Program Development Study","Studying and developing the Elder Support Program.",""],[1,"182","19","Veterans Association Coordination at Commune/Sangkat Level","Coordinating the work of Veterans Association at commune/Sangkat level.",""],[1,"183","12","National Institute of Social Affairs Capacity Expansion","Strengthening and expanding the capacity of the National Institute of Social Affairs.",""],[1,"185","18","National Population Policy Coordination and Implementation","The MOP's General Secretariat of Population and Development has the role of coordinating the NPP and strategies for the implementation, including the issues of the people at the relevant ministries and agencies responsible for supporting and promoting the NPP focusing on four priority areas: (1) infrastructure development and expansion, (2) migration management and urbanization, (3) expansion of agriculture and related activities, and (4) investment in social and human capital development.","MOP's General Secretariat of Population and Development | relevant ministries and agencies"],[1,"186","2","NPP Coordination and Monitoring Mechanism","the MOP's General Secretariat of Population and Development will play a role in coordinating with ministries, agencies and stakeholders to implement programs and projects of relevant ministries and agencies, based on the four priorities in the NPP through the implementation of the three-year action plan prepared in five phases until 2030.","MOP's General Secretariat of Population and Development"],[1,"186","4","Annual Progress Reporting and Action Plan Progress Reporting","Preparing Annual Progress Report and Progress Report of Action Plan 2019-2021.",""],[1,"186","5","Action Plan Phase 3 Implementation","Developing and implementing the Action Plan Phase 3 2022-2024.",""],[1,"186","6","Annual Progress Report Preparation","Preparing Annual Progress Report of Action Plan 2022-2024.",""],[1,"186","8","NPP Implementation within the Cambodia SDG Framework","Promoting the implementation of the NPP within the Cambodia's Sustainable Development Goals framework.",""]],"39":[[1,"30","13","Affirmative Recruitment for Women and Persons with Disabilities","Recruitment has been prioritized for female candidates with 20% to 50% of annual employment requirement, and 2% of disability staffs of total officials' number within Ministries and Institutions","Ministries and Institutions"],[1,"105","4","Implementation of the National Strategic Plan on Disability","To officially launched the implementation of the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2014-2018 through this plan, the MOSVY has prepared a mid-term evaluation report 2015 and a draft final report 2014-2018.","MOSVY"],[1,"105","8","Disability Recruitment Quota","Encouraged the ministries and agencies to recruit people with disability at the rate of 2%.",""],[1,"179","1","Persons With Disabilities Foundation","Persons with Disabilities Foundation",""],[1,"182","12","Disability Welfare Services Efficiency and Rights Promotion","Increasing the efficiency of providing welfare services for persons with disabilities and promoting the rights of persons with disabilities.",""],[1,"182","13","Disability Rights Implementation Strengthening","Strengthening the implementation of the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, National Strategic Plan on Disability and regulations.",""],[1,"183","4","Disability Rehabilitation Services","Providing all kinds of rehabilitation services to persons with disabilities.",""],[1,"183","5","Resource Mobilization for Disability Rehabilitation Services","Mobilizing resources for the sustainability in providing rehabilitation services to people with disabilities.",""],[1,"183","6","Supportive Policies for Persons with Disabilities","Providing supportive policies to people with disabilities.",""],[1,"183","7","Disability Rights Law Dissemination","Disseminating the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities.",""]],"40":[[1,"103","14","Child Rights Implementation and Monitoring Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening and expanding the child rights implementation and monitoring Mechanism at ministries, agencies and capital/provinces and issued a Guideline on the Implementation of the UN Recommendation on the Implementation of the Convention on the Child Rights.",""],[1,"104","1","National Action Plan for Child Development Implementation","Developed and disseminated the implementation of the National Action Plan for Child Development 2016-2018",""],[1,"104","1","Convention on the Rights of the Child Reporting","prepared the 4th, 5th and 6th National Report on the Implementation of the Convention on the Child Rights",""],[1,"104","3","Child Care Facility Regulation and Inspection","To strengthen the efficiency and quality of the child care center management and community child management, the RGC has issued three sub-decrees.","RGC | MOSVY"],[1,"182","7","Childcare Services Quality Improvement and Community-Based Expansion","Strengthening the quality of childcare services in the centers and expanding community-based childcare services.",""],[1,"182","8","Child Status Monitoring and Reporting System Strengthening","Strengthening the M&E system and reports on children's status.",""],[1,"182","9","Inter-country Child Adoption Framework","Implementing inter-country child adoption by ensuring the benefits and protecting basic rights of children.",""],[1,"182","10","Juvenile Rehabilitation Programme","Rehabilitating the juveniles who violate the law.",""],[1,"182","11","Drug Abuse Victim Rehabilitation","Rehabilitating the victims of drug abuse.",""]],"41":[[1,"126","10","Human Resource Development and Social Services Expansion","Human resource development: education, capacity enhancement of science and technology, the creation of technical training and an extensive possibility of access to technical training, access to public healthcare is enhanced, access to nutrition is improved with no hunger and an improvement to height to weight index, gender equity in the",""],[1,"126","15","Human Resource Development Budget Expansion","Increase budget allocation to human resource development sector (education more than 3% of GDP, health) and an initiative to prioritize resources (social protection, SMEs/Entrepreneurship)",""],[1,"134","7","Education and Health Promotion Policy Investment","Continue to invest in education and health promotion policies.",""],[1,"247","7","Basic Social Protection System Establishment","This approach specifically reflects new policy commitments for key priorities and policy changes (for example improved education and establishing a basic social protection system, and new spending to support improved administrative and technical capacities).",""],[1,"247","7","Improved Education Policy Commitment","This approach specifically reflects new policy commitments for key priorities and policy changes (for example improved education and establishing a basic social protection system, and new spending to support improved administrative and technical capacities).",""],[1,"247","7","Administrative and Technical Capacity Strengthening Spending","This approach specifically reflects new policy commitments for key priorities and policy changes (for example improved education and establishing a basic social protection system, and new spending to support improved administrative and technical capacities).",""]],"42":[[1,"61","5","Rural Roads Rehabilitation and Construction Programme","Rehabilitation and construction of rural roads - out of total 40,000 km",""],[1,"66","4","Road Infrastructure Connectivity and Standards Upgrading","Improved road infrastructure connectivity with countries in the region and strengthened and expanded the upgrading of the road standards.",""],[1,"66","6","ASEAN Roads Upgrading Programme","Constructing the upgrading of some ASEAN roads as standard 1 (4-lane, AC) such as National Road 5, to be completed by 2020.",""],[1,"187","19","Road Maintenance Program Application Process Strengthening","Strengthening the application process for participating in road maintenance programs.",""],[1,"188","1","Road Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Construction Programme","Continuing to rehabilitate and construct road infrastructure of at least 3,000 kilometers further.",""],[1,"188","2","National Roads Grade 1 Rehabilitation and Expansion","Continuing to rehabilitate, construct and expand the national roads Grade 1 from 2- lane paved road, to 4-lane AC linking to the development zones and key municipalities around 700 km.",""],[1,"188","3","National and Provincial Roads Rehabilitation and Construction","Continuing to rehabilitate and construct the national roads, provincial roads linking to the new development zones of industry, agriculture, agri-industry and tourism which were established and along the border.",""],[1,"188","4","Road Network Maintenance and Repair Programme","Continuing to strengthen the quality of maintenance, repair and construction work and ensure the flow of national budget on the routine maintenance and periodic maintenance of the network road network.",""],[1,"188","13","National Road Rehabilitation and Drainage Improvement Project Package","The Project for Rehabilitation of National Road N. 21, Phase I and II (Takhmao-Chrey Thom), National Road No. 2 (Takhmao - Dounkeo O Chambok), and National Road No. 22 (O Chambok-Ang Tasom/Takeo Province) National Road No. 48, Improvement of Siem Reap River Phase II, and construction of drainage system in Takhmao City.",""]],"43":[[1,"64","4","Amendment of the Traffic Law","Amendment of Article 40, 41, 47, 48, 75, 77, 82 and 90 of the Law on Traffic introduced in 2017.",""],[1,"88","15","Worker Safe Transportation Coordination and Traffic Law Enforcement","Continued to cooperate with relevant ministries to address the problems of safe transportation and commutation of workers, through adjusting means of transportation and strictly enforcing the Traffic Law.","relevant ministries"],[1,"188","5","Traffic Safety Signage and Speed Monitoring System","Increasing traffic safety signs on national roads and urban areas, and setting up cameras for monitoring the over-speeding vehicles along the national roads.",""],[1,"191","2","Road Traffic Safety Collaboration and Activity Expansion","Carrying out activities and expanding collaboration to achieve the UN's target on road traffic safety, reducing the death rate by 50% by 2020.",""],[1,"191","3","Traffic Law Public Dissemination","Continuing to disseminate the traffic laws to the public in all aspects.",""],[1,"191","4","Road Traffic Safety Implementation Collaboration","Continuing to collaborate with relevant institutions, the private sector, CSOs on the implementation of road traffic safety.",""],[1,"191","5","Private Sector Road Traffic Law Training","Continuing to promote the private sector to deliver road traffic law training to the company's workers.",""],[1,"191","6","Motorcyclist Safety Equipment Distribution","Continuing to distribute reflecing stickers and helmets to motorcyclists.",""],[1,"191","7","Hazardous Area Monitoring and Study Programme","Continuing to study and monitor the most frequent hazardous areas throughout the country.",""],[1,"191","8","Overweight Transport Regulation Awareness and Enforcement Capacity Building","Continuing to educate and promote the public awareness of laws and regulations related to overweight transport and build capacity and morality to the officials to put their heart at work to ensure the accuracy of the weight control tools.",""],[1,"191","9","Transport Overload and Vehicle Modification Enforcement","Continuing to eliminate overload transport and faulty vehicle modification and to restrict the offenses at the stations.",""]],"44":[[1,"187","6","Transport Sector Policy and Regulatory Framework Finalization","Continuing to finalize the necessary policies and regulatory frameworks for managing and developing transport sector and standards related to setting standards for road construction, land transportation and waterway transport.",""],[1,"187","7","Transport and Logistics Legal and Regulatory Reform Package","Identifying and developing draft Law on Ports, Law on Water and Maritime Transport, Law on Land Transport Business, Law on Multi-Transportation, Law on Logistics and Dry Ports, Law on Sewage Treatment, Law on Highways and huge bridges and related regulations, including the encouraging of approval, strengthening management, and enforcement.",""],[1,"187","8","Railway Law and Regulatory Development","Identifying and developing draft law and regulations related to railway.",""],[1,"187","9","Vehicle Identification and Plate Number Registration Sub-Decree","Finalizing Sub-Decree on Registration of Vehicle Identification and Plate Number.",""],[1,"187","10","Ship Registration Sub-Decree Development","Developing draft Sub-decree and Sub-decree on Registration of the Ships with Cambodian Nationality and reviewing draft Sub-Decree on Establishment of National System for the readiness to respond to spill oil and cooperation.",""],[1,"187","11","Priority Laws Organization and Dissemination","Continuing to organize and disseminate some priority laws, especially Traffic Law, Road Law, both at national and sub-national level.",""],[1,"187","12","Institutional Capacity Strengthening through Staff Training and Recruitment","Continuing to strengthen institutions through training human resources and recruiting the staff with quality and transparency.",""],[1,"187","13","Decentralization and Deconcentration Reform Implementation","Continuing to engage and promote the implementation of decentralization and deconcentration reform.",""],[1,"187","14","Road Traffic Regulatory Framework Development","Developing Sub-decree, Prakas, inter-ministerial Prakas and regulations required ss defined in the Law on Road Traffic.",""],[1,"189","15","Logistics Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","Formulating legal documents in logistics, European agreements related to international shipping of the hazadous items on road, warehouse management rules and service delivery rules and logistics operator management.",""],[1,"193","6","Legal Framework Development and Stakeholder Forum Coordination","Continuing to develop legal frameworks and organize forums to support the development and solve the problems effectively with development partners and the private sector.",""]],"45":[[1,"68","16","Airport Runway, Taxiway, Apron, and Safety Route Upgrading","Reinforced the runway and the end of safety route RESA 05 and RESA 23, constructing two new taxiways C and D, constructed a total of 21 airport aprons for 4D and installed a new airbag and continue providing maintenance.",""],[1,"68","19","Passenger Terminal Expansion and Maintenance","Expanded the passenger terminals which can accommodate more than 500 thousand passengers a year and installed a new airbag and continue providing maintenance.",""],[1,"69","2","Civil Aviation Capacity-Building Training Programme","Building the capacity of the officials through trainings focused on 3 skills: Safety Oversights Trainings, Aviation Security Oversights and Generic Trainin for officials in charge of safety oversights and security oversights, officials in charge of drafting regulations as well as public service providers in civil aviation.",""],[1,"69","3","Aviation Safety and Regulatory Framework Development","The SSCA developed and introduced safety regulations related to regulations and the additional revisions on the regulations, procedures, guidlines and other legal documents in accordance with the need and rcommendations of the International Civil Aviaiton Organization (ICAO) and developed drafts on National Safety Program, State Safety Program, Air Secuirity Program and has been preparing economic regulations and technical regulations to ensure the sustainability of business equipment in the air transport industry.",""]],"46":[[1,"229","5","Rural Roads Rehabilitation and Construction Programme","Rehabilitating and constructing rural roads (total length: 45,000km).",""],[1,"229","6","Climate-Resilient Rural Road Upgrading","Improving rural roads to DBST or concrete to be resilient with climate change.",""],[1,"229","7","Rural Road Maintenance Programme","Maintaining the rural road periodically.",""],[1,"229","8","Road Inventory and Rural Road Mapping","Preparing road inventory and rural road maps a well as putting up traffic signs.",""]],"47":[[1,"65","5","Phnom Penh-Poipet Northern Rail Section Restoration and Construction","The northern section (Phnom Penh-Poipet), restored and constructed, (national budget), is currently in the process of transporting passengers and connecting railroads of Cambodia-Thailand.",""],[1,"65","7","Cambodia-Thailand Railway Border Crossing Agreement","Preparing to sign the agreement on border crossings through Cambodia-Thailand railway.",""]],"48":[[1,"189","8","Cross-Border Rail Transport Agreement Implementation","Promoting the implementation of agreements on cross-border transport along the Cambodian-Thai Railways.",""],[1,"189","16","Public-Private Partnership Initiative","Promoting the implementation of a public-private partnership initiative.",""],[1,"189","18","ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan 2025 Coordination","Continuing to cooperate and coordinate with relevant institutions in implementing the ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan 2025.",""],[1,"190","11","Protocol Amendment Negotiation on Cambodia-Vietnam Land Transportation","Continuing to discuss the request for the amendment of the Protocol 2005 for the implementation of the agreement between Cambodia and Vietnam on land transportation.",""],[1,"190","12","Cross-Border Transport Negotiation Initiative","Continuing to negotiate with neighboring countries to promote efficiency and address the challenges of bilateral cross-border transport.",""],[1,"190","13","Implementation of Cross-Border Transport Agreements","Promoting the implementation of cross-border transport agreements in the Greater Mekong Sub-Region.",""],[1,"190","14","Legal Frameworks for ASEAN Transport Coordination Agreements","Establishing legal frameworks to implement the three agreements in the framework of the ASEAN Framework on Transport Coordination i.e. (1) ASEAN Framework Agreement on Facilitation of Commodity Transit, (2) Agreement within the ASEAN Framework for Inter-State Transport Coordination, and (3) ASEAN Framework Agreement on Multi-impage Transport Coordination.",""],[1,"190","15","ASEAN Passenger Carriage Agreement Ratification","Preparing for ratification from the National Assembly on an agreement within the ASEAN framework on facilitating the carriage of passengers by car.",""],[1,"191","10","Implementation of Cambodia-Vietnam Water Transport Agreement","Encouraging the more effective implementation of the agreement between Cambodia and Vietnam on water transport in 2009.",""]],"49":[[1,"191","11","Public Services Delivery and Ship Workshop Management Improvement","Strengthening the delivery of public services on logistics, inspection and technical checkups, boats, driving licenses and other related services, and promoting the development and management of ship workshops.",""],[1,"191","12","Ship Management and Registration Strengthening","Strengthening ship management and registration as well as relevant work at the Department of Public Works and Transport.","Department of Public Works and Transport"],[1,"191","14","Ship Registration and Technical Inspection Service Strengthening","Strengthening public service delivery of ship registration, ship technical checks, ship business permit, and other related services, and promoting the development and management of ship workshops.",""],[1,"191","16","Coastal Ship Development Cooperation","Continuing the cooperation to develop coastal ships of Cambodia, Thailand and Vietnam.",""],[1,"191","19","Ship and Crew Management Strengthening","Strengthening ship and crew management and related work.",""],[1,"191","22","Marine Transport Technology Coordination Cooperation","Cooperating with the Marine Transport Technology Coordination Center to gain knowledge of regulations and management of ships and crew.",""],[1,"192","4","Public Passenger Boat and Small Port Development Projects","Studying and designing projects on public passenger boats, construction of small- scale ports and docks in some districts and areas of the Mekong River.",""],[1,"192","5","Tourist Port Construction in Kep and Coastal Areas","Constructing the tourist port in Kep and coastal areas.",""],[1,"192","6","Navigation Signage and Waterway Rehabilitation","Studying and developing the navigation signs boats and rehabilitating the navigation, Vaico River, Angkor Borey canel and other parts of the Mekong River.",""],[1,"192","8","Waterway Classification for Navigation Study and Production","Studying and producing the waterway classification for navigation.",""]],"50":[[1,"190","17","Public Transport Policy and Legal Framework Development","Promoting the formulation of national policies, master plans and legal documents related to public transport.",""],[1,"190","18","Smart Transportation Systems and Traffic Management","Promoting the use of smart transportation systems and traffic management.",""],[1,"190","19","Urban Street Development Programme","Continuing to develop the city's streets to avoid heavy transport across the city.",""],[1,"190","20","Phnom Penh Traffic Congestion Study and Mitigation","Continuing to study and solve the traffic jams in Phnom Penh.",""],[1,"190","21","Urban Rail Feasibility Studies","Continuing to study the feasibility of building an automatic train system, and the study of the feasibility of constructing tramway, monorail, subway in Phnom Penh.",""]],"51":[[1,"65","11","Integrated Development Plan and Transport and Logistics Master Plan Implementation","The RGC has introduced the IDP 2015-2025, including planning and implementation of the Transport and Logistics Master Plan, linked to major economic corridors.",""],[1,"65","14","National Transport and Logistics Master Plan","Preparing the national transport and logistics master plan.",""],[1,"66","11","ASEAN Customs Transit System Pilot Project","Implementing a pilot project of the ASEAN Customs Transit System, Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, and Vietnam, which is the East-West Corridor of ASEAN after implementing the pilot projects in Singapore, Thailand and Malaysia, the North-South Corridor of ASEAN under technical assistance from European Commission on Customs Transit System.",""],[1,"66","13","Temporary Inland Transportation Agreement under the GMS","Within the GMS, began implementing a temporary inland transportation agreement for 500 commercial vehicles.",""],[1,"186","12","Master Plan for Multimodal Transport and Logistics","Approving and implementing the Master Plan for Multi- modal Transport and Logistics to accelerate integration by linking key economic poles and major economic corridors to be more competitive in the region and the world.",""],[1,"187","1","Physical Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Expansion Investment Programme","Increasing investment budget and mobilizing financing to rehabilitate, build and develop physical infrastructure, including roads and expressways, bridges, railways, waterways, and airways to respond to the demand of national development in terms of quantity, quality, safety and sustainability aspects along with the improvement in inter-institutional coordination mechanism.",""],[1,"187","4","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Investment Project Management","Strengthening institutional capacity to plan, prepare budget, implement, monitor and evaluate investment projects.",""],[1,"188","9","Highway and Major Bridge Construction Studies","Promoting the study of the construction of highways and major bridges with development partners, in particular Phnom Penh-Bavet and Phnom Penh-Poipet- Siem Reap according to the Master Plan of Highway Development in Cambodia.",""],[1,"188","11","Road and Bridge Construction Programme","construction of Saang bridge, National Road No. 43, National Road No. 378 ( Dong Krolor - Siempang - O Chum-Banlung), National Road No. 294 (Chhep- Tonle Lapov), National Road No. 72 (Trapaing Thlong-Thraeng-Kampong Thmor), National Road No. 92 (Sam Ang - Kampong Srolao 1 and 2 - Three angles), National Road No. 78-5 ( Banlong-dragon tail), Chumkiri Road",""],[1,"188","12","Japanese Financing Bridge and Road Rehabilitation Projects","Japanese Financing: Project for Rehabilitation of Chroy Changvar Bridge, National Road No. 5 (Battambang-Sisophon, Prek Kkdam-Thlea Maom, Thlea Maom- Battambang and Sisophon-Poipet); and Reconstruction Projects of 7 Bridges (National Road No. 73 and 11).",""],[1,"189","3","Stung Bot Bridge and Border Post Road Link Construction","Thai Financing: Construction of Stung Bot Bridge, International Boundary Gateway Building and Road Link (border posts linked to National Road No. 5).",""],[1,"189","4","Railway Line Rehabilitation and Station Upgrading","Seeking fund to rehabilitate the railway lines from Phnom Penh to Poipet to 20 tons of weight and to construct and repair the stations, install the safety signs and repair the bypass roads.",""],[1,"189","5","Railway Connection to New Phnom Penh Autonomous Port","Seeking fund to connect railway from Phnom Penh to the new Phnom Penh Autonomous Port.",""],[1,"189","6","Railway Freight Connectivity to Industrial Sites","Promoting the connection of railways to factories, enterprises, special economic zones, such as Touk Meas station to cement factories from Touk Meas station to Chakrey Ting cement factory and from the Veal Rinh station to the Keo Phos Port.",""],[1,"189","7","Stung Bot Railway Container Terminal Construction","Constructing a railway container terminal in Stung Bot.",""],[1,"189","9","Railway Integration and Connectivity Projects","Seeking fund to implement railway integration and connectivity projects and to neighboring countries through new construction under the master plan for Cambodia railway development studied by Republic of Korea, especially Phnom Penh-Bavet- Ho Chi Minh railway.",""],[1,"189","10","Singapore-Kunming Railway Network Development Partnership","Continuing to seek development partners and the private sector to build the Singapore-Kunming Railway network.",""],[1,"189","12","Logistics Master Plan Implementation","Implementing the logistics master plan.",""],[1,"189","14","Logistics Infrastructure Investment Promotion","Promoting investment in logistics centers, warehouse, container terminal and dry port.",""],[1,"189","17","National Transport and Logistics Master Plan","Introducing a new concept of transforming Cambodia into a regional exchange of goods and logistics into a national master plan on transport and logistics to take advantage of trade flows between Vietnam and Thailand.",""],[1,"193","7","Private Sector Feasibility Studies for Transport Infrastructure Investment","Continuing to encourage the private sector to study the feasibility of investing in roads, bridges, railways, and port projects, especially the highways as the priority stated in the Master Plan.",""],[1,"193","9","Transport Policy and Strategic Plan Collaboration","Continuing to collaborate to implement transport policies and strategic plans and initiatives in the region and the world.",""]],"52":[[1,"193","11","Civil Aviation Airworthiness and Environmental Protection Regulatory Framework","Prepare and compile regulations, standards, procedures, requirements, instructions, guidelines and legal documents related to examination of airworthiness and environmental protection according to the laws and regulations of Cambodian Civil Aviation regulations and in accordance with ICAO's standards and recommendations.",""],[1,"193","12","Aircraft Lifespan Regulatory Framework Development","Cooperate in formulating the regulations, legal frameworks and procedures on the lifespan of aircrafts used in the Kingdom of Cambodia.",""],[1,"193","13","Review of Flight Operation Permit Suspension, Revocation, and Renewal Procedures","Review and evaluate the technique of suspending, revoking and renewing the flight operation permit in the Kingdom of Cambodia (inbound and outbound and across).",""],[1,"193","14","Foreign Aircraft Operations Inspection","Examine the operation of all foreign aircrafts flying in the Kingdom of Cambodia (inbound and outbound and across).",""],[1,"193","15","Aircraft Incident and Accident Research and Evaluation","Research and evaluate incidents or accidents related to aircrafts inside and outside the Kingdom of Cambodia.",""],[1,"193","16","Aviation Certification Review and Evaluation","Review and evaluate techniques for issuing, suspending, revoking and renewing aircraft registration certificates, airworthiness certificates, engineer capacity and aircraft skill certificates, audio certificates, radio licenses, aircraft lease certificates, aircraft oil stations, aircraft repair and maintenance units, and aircraft maintenance programs.",""],[1,"193","17","Aircraft Airworthiness Inspection","Examine the airworthiness for aircrafts registered in the Kingdom of Cambodia.",""],[1,"193","18","Aircraft Incident and Accident Research and Evaluation Cooperation","Cooperate in researching and evaluating incidents or accidents related to aircrafts inside and outside the Kingdom of Cambodia.",""],[1,"193","19","Civil Aviation Security Strengthening","Strengthening civil aviation security is to provide national and international trust guaranteed through thorough implementation according to the national and international standards on civil aviation security intended to prevent and combat any law violations such as terrorism, destruction, life- threatening threats and property damage and so on.",""],[1,"193","20","Air Transport Hazardous Goods Regulatory Framework","Prepare and compile legal provisions, procedures, standards, requirements, guidelines and legal documents relating to the security measures and the air transport of hazardous goods according to the laws and regulations of Cambodia Civil Aviation and the standards and recommendations of the International Civil Aviation Organization.",""],[1,"193","21","Civil Aviation Security Training Program","Plan training program and train security and security officers in cooperation with other departments and with ministries and agencies and competent authorities to take action to prevent the violation and destruction of civil aviation sector.",""],[1,"194","1","State Safety and Civil Aviation Security Program Management","Implement and manage state safety programs and national civil aviation security programs by analyzing and reporting on the security and safety control systems of operators, air transport enterprises and service providers.",""],[1,"194","2","Civil Aviation Controller Certification Review and Renewal Reform","Review and evaluate techniques for the suspension, revocation and renewal of civil aviation controller certificates.",""],[1,"194","3","Aviation Inspection Programme","Conduct inspection of: (1) Airport and helicopter, (2) Air transport enterprises and operators, (3) airports, and (4) air routing services.",""],[1,"194","4","Civil Aviation Cooperation and Connectivity Strengthening","Strengthening international cooperation and flight connections is to continue efforts to strengthen civil aviation cooperation in order to create and harmonize policies and roadmaps to develop the civil aviation sector in the sub-region, the region and the whole world.",""],[1,"194","5","Security and Safety Audit Program Coordination","Cooperate and coordinate with the International Civil Aviation Organization to determine the standards and recommendations to carry out the Security and Safety Audit Program.",""],[1,"194","6","Civil Aviation Regulatory Review and Amendment","Prepare drafts of regulations and legal documents, study and amend and modify regulations and provisions pertaining to the national and international civil aviation sector.",""],[1,"194","7","Air Transport Policy and Regulatory Compilation","Prepare and compile Air Transport policies and regulations in accordance with the objectives and vision of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the International Civil Aviation Organization.",""],[1,"194","8","Air Transport Services Negotiation and Legal Agreements","Conduct negotiation and establish memorandums of understanding, agreements and legal documents on air transport services.",""],[1,"194","9","Air Transport Liberalization Participation","Participate in managing and handling essential aviation jobs such as liberalization of air transport with ASEAN and other organizations at regional and international levels, in collaboration with the International Relations and Legislation Department.","International Relations and Legislation Department"],[1,"194","10","Review and Evaluate Air Transport Licensing and Certification Procedures","Review and evaluate the techniques of providing air transport licenses or certificates in cooperation with the Department of Flight Safety and Standard and the Department of Airworthiness.",""],[1,"194","11","Review of Hazardous Air Transport Permit Issuance","Review and evaluate the technique of issuing the permits of air transport of hazardous goods in coordination with the Department of Flight Safety and Standard and the Department of Civil Aviation Security.",""],[1,"194","12","Civil Aviation Flight Services and Data Compilation","Prepare and provide program and off-program flight services and compile civil aviation data in cooperation with relevant departments and institutions.",""],[1,"194","13","Air Routing Services and Infrastructure Development","Enhancing air routing services ensure that air routes for aircrafts and air traffic services are secure, ensuring the reliability of delivering services in accordance with international standards as well as the development of routing infrastructures.",""],[1,"194","14","Air Routing Safety and Standards Regulatory Framework","Prepare and compile regulations, procedures, standards, requirements, guidelines, and legal instruments relating to air routing safety and standards, and air routing services for aircrafts operating its flight in and out of the Kingdom of Cambodia.",""],[1,"194","16","Aviation Information Publication","Prepare and publish a book on aviation information related to Cambodia's airspace and the air space reserved for Cambodia under the cooperation and international and national agreements recognized or permitted by the International Civil Aviation Organization.",""],[1,"194","17","Monitoring and Control of Electronic Radio Signals","Collaborate with relevant ministries and institutions in monitoring and controlling electronic radio signals to avoid interrupting air routing services.","relevant ministries and institutions"],[1,"194","18","Aviation Frequency Management","Manage the aviation frequency with the authority of the telecommunications authority in accordance with the instructions of the International Telecommunication Union.",""],[1,"195","1","Air Routing Service Contracting Arrangement","Prepare contracts with relevant authorities in the provision of air routing services, such as the weather services and telecommunication services, etc.",""],[1,"195","2","Air Routing Services Administration","Administer and provide air routing services in and out of the airspace of the Kingdom of Cambodia in accordance with Cambodian Civil Aviation Regulations and the International Civil Aviation Organization's standards and recommendations.",""],[1,"195","4","Airport Infrastructure Development","The airport infrastructure development must be consistent with the growth of air passengers and make the civil aviation industry best responsive to the needs of consumers, including air passengers, efficient airport landings, civil airport development and the promotion of development in the field of safe, reliable and economic air transport.",""],[1,"195","5","Airport Safety and Environmental Compliance Regulatory Framework","Prepare and compile regulations, procedures, standards, requirements, instructions, manuals, and legal documents related to airport safety standards, airport safety management systems, water and electricity supply and environmental protection at the airport in the Kingdom of Cambodia in accordance with the laws and regulations of Cambodian Civil Aviation and the standards and recommendations of the International Civil Aviation Organization.",""],[1,"195","6","Airport Construction Standards and Oversight","Oversee the implementation and standards for existing and new airport construction projects, study the location and process (including materials and equipment), engineering work and maintenance.",""],[1,"195","7","New Airport Licensing Technical Study and Evaluation","Conduct technical study and evaluation of application for licenses for the construction of a new airport.",""],[1,"195","8","Airport Certification Study and Evaluation","Study and evaluate the technique of issuing airport certificates.",""],[1,"195","9","Airport Registration and Aircraft Operation Certification Study","Study and evaluate the technique of issuing airport registration and aircraft operation certificates.",""],[1,"195","10","Airport Barrier Management and Signage Compliance","Provide advice and guidance on any barriers that interfere both inside and outside the airport and comply with the standards and guidelines about the signs and interrupting lights.",""],[1,"195","11","Human Resources and Institutional Capacity Development for Civil Aviation Security","Develop human resources and strengthen institutional capability: To ensure security and safety meets the requirements.",""]],"53":[[1,"23","12","Productivity and Competitiveness Enhancement Measures","Capitalizing on and maintaining growth momentum in the Cambodian economy (flourishing domestic business activity and investment, and high and rising FDI flows, on the back of bullish demand and trade) by addressing productivity and competitiveness bottlenecks.",""],[1,"23","12","Economic Diversification and Value-Addition Promotion","This has many dimensions, including: diversifying the economy; boosting value added in industry and service sectors;",""],[1,"47","1","Economic Base Diversification and Productivity Enhancement","Cambodia intends to diversify its economic base and increase productivity to compete in regional and global markets efficiently.",""],[1,"126","10","Economic Diversification and Connectivity Improvement","Economic diversification: improvement on transportation, energy, and digital connectivity, scouting a new source of",""],[1,"126","15","Productivity and Structural Transformation Programme","A higher productivity (a yearly increase in all sectors) a structural transformation through a transfer investment and acquire technology and build skill/vocational and technical training",""],[1,"126","15","Industrial Development Policy Implementation","Industrial Development Policy was implemented, maintain a strong flow of FDI, a push to implement the 4th industrial revolution.",""],[1,"132","9","Consolidation-to-Acceleration Economic Growth Measure","The new measure begins with the phase of convergence to acceleration, a measure implemented by the government to promote economic growth, to achieve the long-term goal of achieving higher middle-income country status in 2030.",""],[1,"134","8","Industrial Development Policy Implementation Support","Support the implementation of the Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025.",""],[1,"134","11","Agriculture-to-Manufacturing Linkage Support","Support the linking of agriculture to manufacturing (agro- industry) to increase value added.",""],[1,"134","12","Cross-Sector Connectivity Support","Support connectivity among the three sectors: physical infrastructure, energy, and digital.",""],[1,"138","1","Economic Diversification and Macroeconomic Stability Measures","Ensuring a sustainable economic growth of around 7% per annum which is resilient to crises through diversifying into new growth sources to widen the growth base and enhance competitiveness while maintaining the macro-economic stability through containing inflation, ensuring a stable exchange rate for Riel, increasing the international reserve on regular basis and managing public debt vigilantly.",""]],"54":[[1,"76","5","Certificate of Origin and Export Permit Automation and Registration","Has been issuing certificate of origin, export-import licenses and export-import of unprocessed gemstones, (2) cooperated to connect the automation system of certificate of origin (C/O Form D) to the ASYCUDA system of national single system platform, and is trying to connect with the ASEAN member states in order to reach full implementation, and (3) has been registering for export permits under the generalized system preferential of trade.",""],[1,"76","6","Agricultural and Agro-Industry Product Promotion","Promoting agricultural and agro-industry products, which has in turn promoted the use of Khmer products as a substitute for imported products and eventually will increase export to international market.",""],[1,"76","10","Facilitation of Cambodian Agro-Product Trade for Export Expansion","Facilitating trade of Cambodian agro-products for faster exports with reduced cost.",""],[1,"77","1","ASEAN Economic Community Integration Measures","Cambodia has worked closely with other member countries to implement four basic principles: (1) removal of customs clearance and non-tariff barriers for special goods and services, (2) removal of tariff and non-tariff barriers for all goods and services; (3) the Joint Policy on Customs for External Imports and (4) the free flow of labor and capital.",""],[1,"77","1","ASEAN Single Window Trade Facilitation Upgrade","Cambodia has been working to improve its One Window Service to be able to integrate into an ASEAN single window in order to ensure trade facilitation for the \"ASEAN Economic Community\".",""],[1,"77","5","Trade Partnership and Overseas Market Expansion","Strengthened trade partnerships and explored overseas markets to attract foreign investors and businesses in Cambodia.",""],[1,"77","6","Trade and Investment Partnership Cooperation","Cooperated with Center of ASEAN - Japan, ASEAN-China, ASEAN - Korea, ASEAN - Indonesia, ASEAN - USA, ASEAN - Russia, ASEAN - Hong Kong in order to strengthen trade and investment partnerships, and to promote Cambodian Products in Foreign Markets.",""],[1,"77","8","Export Market Expansion Cooperation","Cooperating with Europe, the Middle-East, Africa, Timor-Leste and other countries in the Americas to expand markets for the Cambodian products.",""],[1,"78","2","Cambodia Trade Integration Strategy Update Implementation","Implementing the Cambodia Trade Integration Strategy Update (CTISU) and the Trade SWAP Road Map 2019-2023.",""],[1,"78","5","International Product Quality and Trade Policy Cooperation","Cooperating in the bilateral, multilateral framework on strengthening the quality and safety of products and trade policies with the goal of promoting and protecting the reputation of Cambodian products in international markets.",""],[1,"83","10","Import and Export Permitting for Artistic Souvenirs","Checking and permitting the import and export of artistic souvenirs",""],[1,"126","15","ASEAN Integration and LDC Graduation Preparation","Business enlargement through a complete integration into ASEAN, a preparation to leave the LDC status",""]],"55":[[1,"197","6","Special Economic Zone Operations Improvement","Further improving the operation of SEZs to attract more investment and create industrial bases that include agro- processing, assembly, furniture manufacturing, and household appliances as well as souvenir products for tourists.",""],[1,"198","4","Preah Sihanouk Multi-Purpose Special Economic Zone Master Plan Formulation","Studying and engaging in the formulation of the master plan or the concept notes related to transforming Preah Sihanouk province into a multi-purpose special economic zone.",""],[1,"198","8","Special Economic Zone Investment Promotion and Industrial Base Development","the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC) will implement the following key activities:","Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC)"],[1,"198","9","SEZ Incentive Framework Review","Leading and coordinating in reviewing the incentive framework for companies located in the SEZs, both foreign, local, and small and medium enterprises.",""],[1,"198","10","Private Sector and Regional Developer Participation in SEZ Infrastructure Development","Promoting more active involvement from the private sector/regional developers in the development of infrastructure at the sites of the SEZs to ensure the attractiveness and interest of investors.",""],[1,"198","11","Special Economic Zones Law and Industrial Park Development Support","Continuing to promote the establishment of major industry and industrial parks by adopting \"Special Economic Zones Law\" to develop those areas to international standards in all aspects as well as encouragement and other practical support measures to promote investment in the SEZs.",""],[1,"198","12","Provincial Industrial Zones Development Support","Continuing to cooperate in the development of the provincial industrial zones, which are the focus of small and medium enterprises aimed at promoting the competitiveness of these enterprises, especially through the prioritization of access to electricity and water supply, transport links and logistics as well as other facilitations and motivations.",""],[1,"198","13","SEZ Performance Indicator Development for Incentives","Promoting competitiveness between SEZs by studying the development of core indicators for measuring the performance of those economic zones as criteria for providing incentives and promoting best practices.",""],[1,"198","14","Physical Infrastructure Development Around SEZs","Participating and cooperating with relevant ministries and agencies to continue to develop physical infrastructure, especially around the SEZs.",""],[1,"198","15","SEZ Governance Reform and Capacity Strengthening","Continuing to reform the governance structures and strengthen the capacity of officials in the SEZs to provide more efficient services to investors.",""],[1,"198","16","Feasibility Review for Major High-Quality SEZ Promotion","Reviewing the feasibility of promoting major and high-quality SEZs using the public private partnership mechanism.",""],[1,"199","2","Industrial Cluster and Special Economic Zone Development","Promoting and encouraging investment to create industrial clusters, industrial parks and the establishment of SEZs as well as investment in infrastructure development and the connection of both software and hardware supporting all industrial production activities.",""],[1,"207","7","Industrial Diversification and Production Capacity Expansion","Diversifying the industry and expanding the industrial production capacity, increasing productivity, with a particular emphasis on the implementation of the IDP 2015-2025.",""],[1,"207","8","Industrial Cluster and Special Economic Zone Development","Encouraging investments to create industrial clusters, industrial parks and the establishment of Special Economic Zones as well as investment in infrastructure development and linking both software and hardware supporting all industrial production activities.",""]],"56":[[1,"149","14","Corporate Governance Policy Framework Studies","In the sixth Legislature of the National Assembly, the RGC will focus on (1) Initiating studies to assist in the formulation of a policy framework aimed at enhancing corporate governance and good practices in the private sector",""],[1,"149","14","Corporate Social and Environmental Responsibility Policy Studies","Undertaking studies aimed at supporting the preparation of a policy framework to promote the Corporate Social and Environmental Responsibility of the private sector in terms of addressing social and environmental protection issues, inculcating social morality in national culture, enhancing consumer rights protection and consumer safety with the enactment of a Law on Consumer Protection",""],[1,"149","14","Public-Private Dialogue Mechanism","Continuing the practices of promoting policy dialogues through the public-private dialogue mechanism, at the policy, technical, national and sub-national levels, through a joint engagement with the Chamber of Commerce",""],[1,"149","14","Private Sector Human Capital and Innovation Incentives","Encouraging the private sector to reinvest in human capital development and innovation",""],[1,"149","16","Government-Private Sector Forum Mechanism","Continuing to implement the Government-Private Sector Forum mechanism to continue addressing the various concerns of the private sector and to further strengthen the private sector to become more productive.",""],[1,"149","17","Entrepreneurship Promotion and SME Support","Promoting entrepreneurship, including one for small and medium enterprises, especially among Cambodians, to do business and investment by providing incentives, capital and technical consulting.",""],[1,"149","17","Government-Private Sector Forum Mechanism Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen the Government-Private Sector Forum Mechanism in the direction of promoting these mechanisms into the Cambodian Development Forum, a mechanism for stakeholders to discuss issues of development.",""],[1,"154","5","Investment Law Amendment and Enforcement","Pushing for the amendment of the law on investment, and the effective enforcement of this law as well as the law on special economic zones.",""],[1,"154","7","Business Start-Up Facilitation and Public Service Reform","Preparing and implementing mechanisms to facilitate new business start-up by cutting time for registration, license application and other relevant procedure as well as reforming the public service for business.",""],[1,"154","12","Business Expenditure Reduction Reform","Accelerating reform and strengthening of institutional capacities through (1) reducing business expenditure, taking into account the issues, procedures, procedures, and public service costs, in order to effectively promote the transport and logistics systems in Cambodia;",""],[1,"154","12","Human Resources and Skills Improvement for Public Service Delivery","(2) improving the quality of human resources and medium and high- level skills to increase the effectiveness of public services delivery.",""],[1,"155","15","Investment Law and Special Economic Zone Law Preparation","Preparing a new Investment Law and Special Economic Zone Law.",""],[1,"155","16","Private Investment Promotion and Coordination","Continuing to strengthen and expand the private sector through more effective management and coordination of private investment, as well as the promoting, the attracting and supporting the private investment.",""],[1,"155","17","Investment Monitoring and Control Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening and enhancing the effectiveness of the investment monitoring and control mechanism to ensure compliance with the principles and conditions of investment contracts and compliance with existing Cambodian laws.",""],[1,"155","18","Investment Facilitation Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening investment mechanism based on global initiative to promote the effectiveness of investment facilitation and addressing investors' challenges at all stages of the implementation of the investment projects.",""],[1,"155","19","Targeted Investment Promotion and Attraction Strategy","Developing and implementing concrete strategies and measures to enhance the promotion and attracting investment by focusing on a number of targeted countries and identifying specific types of priority industries.",""],[1,"155","20","One-Window Business and Investment Facilitation Mechanism","Creating a favorable environment for both domestic and international investments, including facilitating registration, licensing and permits, especially through the one window service mechanism to accelerate all business and investment transactions as well as the reduction of the informal expenses.",""],[1,"155","22","Automated Business Registration System Expansion and Strengthening","Expand and strengthen services through competitive Automated Registration System in ASEAN countries",""],[1,"159","6","International Investment Attraction Mechanisms","Continuing to strengthen international cooperation and creating new mechanisms to further attract investment, from both private sector and official development institutions, as well as developing commerce sector and promoting industrial and agriculture diversification into high value-added activities.",""]],"57":[[1,"199","16","Salt Field Development and Management Policy Formulation","Promoting the policy formulation for the development and management of salt fields.",""],[1,"199","17","Food Safety Promotion and Training Programme","Organizing promotions and training on food safety and promoting compliance with national and international standards.",""],[1,"199","18","Local Handicraft Processing Promotion","Encouraging and promoting local processing handicraft activities such as rattan, bamboo.",""],[1,"200","1","National SME and Handicraft Statistics Management and Strategic Planning","Continuing to promote the management of basic statistics on SMEs and handicraft in the entire country in the formulation of a strategic plan to promote and support the development of SMEs and handicrafts.",""],[1,"200","2","SME and Handicraft Development Cooperation with Development Partners","Continuing to promote cooperation with development partners in promoting the development of SMEs and handicraft.",""],[1,"200","3","One Village One Product Movement","Encouraging, supporting and promoting a One Village One Product Movement, organizing training courses on financial management and handicraft management in collaboration with development partners.",""],[1,"200","4","Domestic Product Promotion and Exhibition Programme","Increasing promotion activities and organizing competition program, the exhibitions of domestic and foreign products to promote domestic products.",""],[1,"200","5","SME Development Policy Implementation Plan","Promoting the formal inclusion of SME Development Policy and the five-year implementation plan and implementing the activities set out in this policy",""],[1,"207","16","National SME Statistics Management and Strategic Planning Support","Continuing to promote the management of SMEs statistics across the country in the formulation of a strategic plan to promote and support the SME development and handicrafts.",""],[1,"207","17","SME and Handicrafts Development Cooperation with Development Partners","Continuing to promote cooperation with development partners in promoting SME development and handicrafts.",""],[1,"207","18","One Village One Product Promotion and Training Programme","Promoting, supporting and enhancing the movement of One Village One Product, creating training courses on financial control and handicraft, enterprise management in collaboration with development partners.",""],[1,"208","5","One Village One Product Policy Implementation","the General Secretariat for Promotion of the One Village One Product Movement will continue to implement the key activities of the National Policy on Promotion of the One Village One Product Movement 2016-2026 as follows:",""],[1,"208","6","Development of Legal Frameworks and Mechanisms","Development of legal frameworks and mechanisms.",""],[1,"208","8","One Village One Product Institutional and Human Resource Development","Promotion of institutional and human resource development related to the promotion of the One Village One Product movement.",""],[1,"208","11","One Village One Product Program Participation Enhancement","Enhancement of the participation from all relevant parties to promote the One Village One Product program.",""],[1,"208","12","One Village One Product Research and Development Capacity Development","Develop the One Village One Product research and development capacity.",""],[1,"208","13","Capacity Building for Agricultural, Industrial, Handicraft, and Services Production","Build the capacity in making the agricultural, industrial, handicraft products and services.",""],[1,"208","14","One Village One Product Quality Upgrade","Promote the product quality to meet the One Village One Product standards.",""],[1,"208","17","One Village One Product Promotion Association/Community","Create, compile or strengthen or extend the One Village One Product promotion association/community.",""],[1,"208","18","Youth and Women Participation in One Village One Product Promotion","Promote the participation of the youth and women in the promotion of One Village One Product.",""],[1,"208","19","One Village One Product Participation Promotion","Promote the participation from the skilled, experienced and local people in the promotion of One Village One Product movement.",""],[1,"213","8","SME Development and Modernization Support","The RGC's strategic goal is to continue strengthening the development and modernization of small and medium enterprises, promoting entrepreneurship and the creation of new enterprises substitute imports with domestic production, connecting small and medium enterprises with FDI, and enhancing the export of products with high potential especially in agriculture, food processing and agro- industry sectors.",""],[1,"213","11","SMEs Development Policy Finalization and Implementation","Finalizing the preparation of the \"SMEs Development Policy\" and promoting subsequently its effective implementation.",""],[1,"213","12","Market Support and Technology Dissemination Mechanism","Strengthening the supporting mechanism to facilitate registration, service coordination, the widely and timely dissemination of market information, and the dissemination and mainstreaming of new technologies in an effort to open up markets for Cambodian products.",""],[1,"214","1","SMEs Bank Establishment","Establishing a \"SMEs Bank\" to provide financing to SMEs and promoting the development and implementation of other financing arrangements/options including the Collective Investment Scheme.",""],[1,"214","2","National Entrepreneurship Fund","Establishing a \"National Entrepreneurship Fund\" ... in collaboration with the private sector",""],[1,"214","2","Entrepreneurship Development Center","and \"Entrepreneurship Development Center\" in collaboration with the private sector",""],[1,"214","3","Support Infrastructure Investment and SME Cluster Promotion","Strengthening and expanding additional investment on supporting infrastructure such as a national laboratory and, improved trade facilitation and logistics system as well as promoting investment in the creation of SMEs clusters.",""],[1,"214","4","SME Productivity Enhancement and Standards Compliance Programme","Enhancing productivity for SMEs through stricter compliance with sanitary and phytosanitary requirements, technical standards and products innovation through the protection of intellectual property and patents.",""],[1,"214","6","Private Sector Support Strategy Review","Reviewing the strategy or action plan supporting the private sector on production, increasing the competitiveness of SMEs and handicrafts, and expanding the Cambodia market.",""],[1,"214","7","Inclusive Business and Social Enterprise Promotion","Promoting and encouraging the implementation of an inclusive business model or business activities, as well as social enterprise initiatives to create a new dynamics for a systematic solution that will accelerate the innovative business of the private sector that can help to solve problems for poor and low income people in Cambodia.",""],[1,"214","8","Wide Cross-Sector Coordination Meetings","Implementing wide cross-sector meetings linking systematic relationships between producers, suppliers and marketers by requiring close participation and collaboration with relevant ministries and agencies and private sectors such as Chamber of Commerce, Chamber of Employment, associations or unions, and enterprises.",""],[1,"214","9","Business Development Advisory Center","Continuing to establish a Business Development Advisory Center and cooperate with private business development advisory bodies.",""],[1,"214","10","Business Environment Improvement for Enterprise Registration and One-Window Services","Creating a business environment in order to increase registration, authorization, establishment of a small-scale manufacturing enterprise and handicraft, and to improve One Window Service Office.",""],[1,"214","11","Local Handicraft Enterprise Processing and Digitalization Support","Improving the processing capacity of local handicraft enterprises and the use of digital systems in businesses, especially innovative and social businesses providing such as social enterprises in contribution to local job creation.",""],[1,"214","12","Salt Field Development and Management Policy Formulation","Promoting the policy formulation for the development and management of salt fields.",""],[1,"214","13","Food Safety Promotion and Training Programme","Organizing promotions and training on food safety and promoting compliance with national and international standards.",""],[1,"214","14","Local Handicraft Processing Promotion","Encouraging and promoting local processing handicraft activities, using materials such as rattan, bamboo.",""],[1,"214","15","National SME and Handicrafts Statistics Management","Continuing to promote the management of basic statistics on SMEs and handicrafts in the entire country for the formulation of a strategic plan to promote and support the development of SMEs and handicrafts.",""],[1,"214","16","SME and Handicrafts Development Cooperation with Development Partners","Continuing to promote cooperation with development partners in promoting the development of SMEs and handicrafts.",""],[1,"214","17","One Village One Product Movement","Encouraging, supporting and promoting a One Village One Product Movement, organizing training courses on financial management and handicraft management in collaboration with development partners.",""],[1,"214","18","Domestic Product Promotion Campaign","Increasing promotion activities and organizing competition programs, and exhibitions of domestic and foreign products to promote domestic products.",""],[1,"214","19","SME Development Policy Implementation","Promoting the formal inclusion of SME Development Policy and the five-year implementation plan and implementing the activities set out in this policy which focus",""],[1,"215","2","SME Cluster Investment Attraction Activities","the Council for the Development of Cambodia will implement the following key activities:","Council for the Development of Cambodia"],[1,"215","3","SME Industrial Park Promotion Policy Consultation","Participating in the consultation on the policy of encouraging industrial parks for small and medium enterprises to promote linkages between foreign enterprises and local enterprises.",""],[1,"215","4","Industrial Park Design Study Tours for SMEs","Organizing or participating in study tours to explore the design of industrial parks for small and medium enterprises that promote linkages between foreign enterprises and local enterprises, in particular the participation in the value chains and the production chain in the context of regional integration with Thailand or Vietnam, or any other country in a region that has similar situation.",""],[1,"215","6","Trade Policy Dissemination and Business E-Learning Promotion","Disseminate new trade policies and promote business-related subjects in e-learning",""],[1,"215","6","Entrepreneurship and SME Development Training Programme","training on entrepreneurship and the development of SMEs in terms of business and project management, e- commerce, opportunities and challenges.",""],[1,"215","7","Trade Activities Development Programme","2. Develop of Trade Activities in Capital and Provinces: (1) Develop business management, and (2) Develop business skills.",""],[1,"215","8","Gender Equity Promotion in Trade and Public Service","Promote gender equity in the field of trade as well as public service",""],[1,"215","8","Women in SMEs Support and Gender Equity Expansion","strengthen and expand the concept of gender, gender equity and women in SMEs sector",""],[1,"215","8","Gender Mainstreaming in Cross-Sector Initiatives","gender mainstreaming in cross-sector initiatives for short-term strategies (vocational training and skills) and long-term strategies",""],[1,"218","3","Medium-Term SME Development Planning Framework","Encouraging medium-term planning for SME development by identifying potential business opportunities for export, new product development, value chain linkages and regional production network, and developing a necessary and realistic activity framework for developing those enterprises.",""],[1,"218","4","SME Training and Production Modernization Support","Examining the ability to provide support to SMEs on trainings and investment in machinery or production equipment and other incentives linking with the conditions of local raw material production, improving product quality and modernizing the production chain aimed at linking multinational corporations.",""],[1,"218","5","Single-Window SME Registration Mechanism","Strengthening the single-window mechanism for SME registration, by using the licenses and accounting records for the evaluation basis and conditions for providing incentives and support from the RGC.",""],[1,"218","7","Industry Registration Efficiency Improvement Measures","Improving the efficiency of industry registration by implementing cooperation procedures, granting registration authority to partner agencies, and facilitating the registration of business agents on behalf of applicants, including taking into account the automation of industrial property registration.",""],[1,"218","9","Technology Transfer Promotion in Manufacturing and Handicrafts","Promoting and encouraging the transfer of new technologies in manufacturing and handicrafts.",""],[1,"232","4","One Village One Product Institutional and Human Resource Development","Promotion of institutional and human resource development related to the promotion of the One Village One Product movement.",""],[1,"232","7","One Village One Product Program Participation Enhancement","Enhancement of participation from all relevant parties to promote the One Village One Product program.",""],[1,"232","8","One Village One Product Research and Development Capacity Development","Developing the One Village One Product research and development capacity.",""],[1,"232","9","Capacity Building for Agricultural, Industrial, Handicraft, and Service Production","Building the capacity in producing the agricultural, industrial, handicraft products and services.",""],[1,"232","10","One Village One Product Quality Improvement Initiative","Promoting the product quality to meet the One Village One Product standards.",""],[1,"232","13","One Village One Product Promotion Associations and Communities","Createing, organizing, strengthening or extending One Village One Product promotion associations/communities.",""],[1,"232","14","Youth and Women Participation in One Village One Product","Promoting the participation from youth and women in of One Village One Product.",""],[1,"232","15","One Village One Product Participation Promotion","Promoting the participation from skilled, experienced and local people in the promotion of One Village One Product movement.",""]],"58":[[1,"76","4","Intellectual Property Rights Regulatory and Registration Measures","Intellectual Property Rights: (1) Registered as a member of international trademark, the Lisbon Agreement on name of Origin of Goods and Geographical Indication, and International Geographical Indication Network Organization, (2) issued statements on exclusive goods, trademark protection, international trademark registration, protection of geographical indication goods, online trademark registration, draft Prakas on establishment of council of complaints and procedures for dispute resolution, and listing of licenses and franchises.",""],[1,"76","13","Trade and Business Legal Framework Reform","Creating legal documents and trade-related laws to ensure legality and effectiveness in carrying out business operations.",""],[1,"78","4","Border and Domestic Market Goods Inspection","Inspecting export-import of goods at all border gates and at domestic markets in order to prevent the flow of goods which is not accordance with technical regulations.",""],[1,"86","16","Product Quality and Safety Certification System","Set up a system for certification of product quality and safety and efficiency of the management system of the factory and SMEs in accordance with national, regional and international standards",""],[1,"86","17","Product Quality and Management System Certification","The system certifies product quality standards and certifies standard management systems (ISO 9001, ISO 14001, ISO 22000, GMP, etc.).",""],[1,"86","18","Organized Product Registration System","Organized product registration system in accordance with international principles and mutual recognition coordination in ASEAN to ensure safety for consumers.",""],[1,"87","8","Metrology Law Enforcement and Regulatory Promotion","Promoted the activities related to the legislation and promoted the enforcement of the Law on Metrology and regulations as a basis for the metrological performance.",""]],"60":[[1,"197","9","Oil Production Site Launch and Revenue Management Reform","Promoting the developing oil and gas industry, especially the launching of the first- ever oil production site as soon as possible while strengthening the management of revenues from those resources in an efficient, transparent and accountable manner.",""],[1,"199","3","Factory Regulation Enforcement and Registration Drive","Continuing to strengthen the implementation of laws and regulations on factory management and attract all enterprises and factories to register for the factory establishment, factory license and the factory's signboard.",""],[1,"199","5","Scientific, Technological and Innovation Cooperation Promotion","Strengthening the scientific, technological and innovative cooperation and promoting research activities and encouraging new creativity in the business, services and products that are appropriate in national and digital contexts or the 4th industry revolutions.",""],[1,"199","6","Industrial Waste Management Guidelines","Developing guidelines on industrial waste management.",""],[1,"199","7","Patent Registration and Protection Cooperation","Strengthening procedures and cooperation with domestic and international partners in strengthening and facilitating the registration, protection, and provision of patent licenses in the industrial sector.",""],[1,"199","8","National Standards and Meteorology Implementation Strengthening","Strengthening the implementation of national standards and meteorology in protecting public welfare, increasing regional and global competitiveness.",""],[1,"199","9","Business Development Service Capacity Building and Institutional Support","Boosting capacity building in business development service delivery and institutional support capability, especially the National Institute of Standards, the National Institute of Meteorology, the National Productivity Center, the Industrial Laboratory of Cambodia, and other relevant institutions to promote investment and efficiency of public service delivery.",""]],"61":[[1,"197","4","Cambodia Industrial Development Policy Implementation and Mid-Term Review","Further implementing the \"Cambodia Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025\", especially transforming Sihanoukville Province into a multi-purpose Special Economic Zone (MPSEZ), along with the conduct of the Policy's mid-term review.",""],[1,"197","5","Garment and Footwear Sector Development Strategy","Formulating and implementing the garment and footwear sector development strategy to improve competitiveness, create value-addition, establish supporting industries and develop the industry's value chains.",""],[1,"197","8","Creative Industries Development and Domestic Product Promotion","Promoting the development of the entertainment service sector, literature, arts, cartoons and movies, which are the creative industries with high potentials for creating value-addition and jobs, while encouraging the production and consumption of domestic products, both traditional products and those with a Geographical Indications (GI).",""],[1,"197","10","Industry Development Policy Implementation Promotion","the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC) will continue its task of promoting the implementation of the Industry Development Policy (IDP) 2015-2025 through the following activities:","Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC)"],[1,"197","11","Capacity Building for Planning and Policy Officials","Building the capacity of officials involved in planning, evaluation, scientific research and analysis, and policy recommendations.",""],[1,"197","12","IDP Implementation Facilitation and Monitoring","Facilitating, promoting and monitoring the progress of the implementation of the IDP of relevant ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"197","13","Implementation of IDP Policy Measures and Action Plans","Continuing to implement the policy measures, policies and action plans as set out in the IDP related to the responsibilities of the CDC, particularly relevant policy measures under the key strategy of \"promoting investment attraction\".",""],[1,"197","14","Policy Implementation Progress Reporting System","Collecting, analyzing synthesizing, and compiling the timely progress reports on policy implementation.",""],[1,"197","15","IDP Implementation Coordination Meetings","Organizing technical working group meetings and inter-ministerial meetings related to promoting the implementation of the IDP.",""],[1,"198","1","Policy Dissemination Workshop","Organizing dissemination workshop on policies and progress reports on policy implementation.",""],[1,"198","2","Priority Topic Memorandum Update Process","Continuing to update memos related to the four priority topics, including agro- industrial development, promotion of SME development, promotion of skills training and human resource, and promotion of transport system and logistics development.",""],[1,"198","3","Industry Development Memos and Concept Notes","Continuing to develop memos, and concept notes related to global experience and expertise in industry development.",""],[1,"198","5","Development Partner Collaboration for Priority Investment Identification and Resource Mobilization","Continuing to collaborate with development partners to study and identify priority investment sectors and mobilize resources to support the implementation of the IDP.",""],[1,"198","6","Garment and Footwear Industry Development Strategy Coordination","Co-organizing strategic documents related to the maintenance of investment and develop concept notes related to strategies promoting the development of the garment and footwear industry to increase value-added and promote the development of clusters of supporting industries.",""],[1,"198","7","Mid-Term Review of IDP Implementation","Facilitating Mid-Term Review of the Implementation of the IDP.",""],[1,"198","18","Industrial Diversification and Production Capacity Expansion","Diversifying industry and expanding industrial production capacity, increasing productivity, with particular emphasis on the implementation of the IDP 2015-2025.",""],[1,"199","1","Technical and Financial Support Mobilization under UNIDO Coordination","Outlining the action plan to attract technical and financial support from the country partnership program under UNIDO coordination and strengthening cooperation with international organizations and development partners.",""],[1,"199","4","Statistical Data Monitoring and Management","Monitoring, collecting, managing and compiling better statistical data.",""],[1,"199","10","Private Sector Support Strategy Review","Reviewing the strategy or action plan supporting the private sector on production, increasing the competitiveness of SMEs and handicrafts, and expanding the Cambodia market.",""],[1,"199","12","Wide Cross-Sector Coordination Meetings","Implementing the wide cross-sector meetings linking systematic relationships between producers, suppliers and marketers by requiring close participation and collaboration with relevant ministries and agencies and private sectors such as Chamber of Commerce, Chamber of Employment, associations or unions, enterprises.","relevant ministries and agencies"]],"62":[[1,"126","15","Capital Investment in Infrastructure","Prioritize capital investment especially infrastructure which supports growth",""],[1,"126","16","Public-Private Partnership Expansion in Main Sectors","Increase the utilization of PPP in main sectors",""],[1,"128","7","Public Infrastructure Investment Expansion","Continuing to sustain medium and long-term economic growth through increasing public investment spending on expanding and strengthening the quality of physical infrastructure such as roads, railways, ports, irrigation, electricity and telecommunications.",""],[1,"128","8","Public Investment Expansion for Infrastructure and Productivity","Increasing additional investment in public investment spending to improve competitiveness and economic productivity by investing in \"hard\", \"social\" and \"soft\" infrastructure.",""],[1,"129","3","Debt Management Strategy 2019-2023","Debt Management Strategy 2019-2023 will continue to focus on borrowing principles that can support economic productivity, ensure macroeconomic stability, and sustain public financial sustainability.",""],[1,"129","3","Reserve Building for Crisis Protection","At the same time, the RGC is building strong reserves to provide effective protection against crises.",""],[1,"129","4","Public Investment Financing Framework Strengthening","Strengthening public investment spending both in form of state and development partner financing framework and through public-private partnership mechanisms",""],[1,"129","4","Development Partner Cooperation Financing Project Procedures Update","Update of joint procedures to implement a development partner cooperation financing project",""],[1,"129","4","Public-Private Partnership Legal Standards for Public Investment Projects","Formulate legal standards to managing public investment projects through Public-Private Partnership mechanism.",""],[1,"129","5","Diversified Financing Mobilization through PPPs and Securities Markets","Diversifying funding sources by continuing to mobilize financing from development partners and the private sector under the framework of public-private partnerships and securities markets.",""],[1,"129","6","Debt Risk Management Framework Implementation and Monitoring","Strengthening the implementation of the Debt Risk Management Framework and monitoring the risk of potential debt obligations resulting from: (1) A state guarantee on PPP projects (2) Banking and financial sector (3) Ministries, institutions, public entities equivalent, public institutions, public enterprises and sub-national administration.",""],[1,"135","3","Integrated Public Investment for Infrastructure, Energy, and Digital Connectivity","In the next five years, the RGC will focus on connecting three sectors: physical infrastructure, energy and digital through increasing public investment to boost economic productivity and economic competitiveness.",""]],"63":[[1,"126","15","Savings, Investment, and Financial Inclusion Strengthening","Increase level of saving and investment on current level (a yearly increase) strengthen financial and banking sector, a better financial inclusion and internationalization",""],[1,"129","9","Credit Supply Facilitation Mechanism","The RGC will facilitate the supply of credit to the economy to achieve its ambitious growth goals.",""],[1,"129","10","Household Savings Mobilization into the Banking System","During the planning cycle, the RGC will try to maintain an annual savings rate of 30%.",""],[1,"129","10","Banking System Inclusion Effort","The key is the effort to bring people who have kept their assets in the form of gold, cash or other assets into the banking system as they are not yet using the banking system.",""],[1,"130","1","Facilitate Remittance Access for Overseas Workers","promote easier access to financial services for Cambodians working abroad to remit income to family members who reside in Cambodia.",""],[1,"130","2","Secure and Diversified Financial System Development","The RGC will make financial inter-mediation between depositors and lenders easier and more convenient through the efforts to build a secure and diversified financial system which is accessible to citizens and businesses for either saving and loan needs and access to financial products.",""],[1,"130","2","Inclusive Financial System Development","Efforts will be made to develop a diversified and inclusive financial system and to note the importance of MFIs and its products.",""],[1,"130","2","Financial Inclusion Outreach for Unbanked People","Meanwhile, on the demand side, building a customer base through enhancing trust and more financial inclusions through initiatives to assist people who has yet to use the banking system to access banking services.",""],[1,"131","7","Microfinance Strategy Update","Update the microfinance strategy",""],[1,"131","7","Financial Inclusion Strategy Development","develop a new strategy for financial inclusion",""],[1,"131","10","Financial Literacy Promotion Campaigns","Promote financial literacy through public awareness campaigns, especially in the countryside, including financial literacy programs in the national curriculum and promoting through the media.",""],[1,"131","19","Budget Arrangements for Financial Inclusion","Determine budget arrangements to ensure financial inclusion.",""]],"64":[[1,"130","4","Domestic Insurance Market Development","The RGC will also continue to explore the development of the domestic insurance market so that businesses and people can protect against risks.",""],[1,"131","14","Insurance Product Awareness and Market Management Measures","Take measure to increase knowledge/confidence in insurance products by disseminating information and awareness and taking steps to manage the market.",""],[1,"131","15","Electronic and Telecommunications Insurance Broker Regulatory Frameworks","Strengthening the management of electronic/telecommunications insurance (brokers) through the establishment of regulatory and other regulatory frameworks.",""],[1,"131","16","Insurance Broker Establishment and Accreditation Programme","Promote the establishment of insurance brokers, inspections and licensing potential of brokers/certificates, and launch training and accreditation programs.",""]],"65":[[1,"119","13","Khmer Riel Confidence and Usage Promotion","Moreover, the government and the National Bank of Cambodia is the first to build trust of the Khmer Riel and encourages the use Khmer riel in all financing process by implementing in other activities like: (1) requiring all operations by the","National Bank of Cambodia"],[1,"129","7","Riel Promotion and Dollarization Reduction Policy","the government continues to encourage the use of the riel to replace dollar in the long run",""],[1,"129","8","Financial Policy Instruments for Growth and Price Stability","many financial policy instruments have been put in place and the RGC will use these tools to contribute to growth to ensure price stability and provide sufficient liquidity to support business needs",""],[1,"129","8","Riel Currency Supply Support","the government will continue to supply further through the riel printing",""],[1,"129","8","Exchange Rate Stabilization Policy","The NBC is committed to keeping the exchange rate at around 4,000 riel per dollar",""],[1,"130","7","Foreign Exchange Reserve Protection and Establishment","Protecting and establishing USD reserves in line with economic activities, ensuring that financing and capital requirements are always provided.",""],[1,"130","8","National Riel Promotion Policy Development","Promote the use of the riel through the development of national policies set up by various working groups based on market options, new services and tools.",""],[1,"130","8","Riel Investment Promotion in Treasury Bills and Bonds","The NBC will focus specifically on riel investments such as treasury bills and bonds.","NBC"]],"66":[[1,"90","2","Onsite and Off-site Banking Supervision Strengthening","the NBC has been continuing to strengthen the onsite and off-site supervision for the banking and financial institutions with great caution and attention",""],[1,"90","3","Banking Supervision and Prudential Regulation Framework","the National Bank of Cambodia issued new prakas such as: (i) prakas on liquidity risk management framework for banks and other financial institutions (ii) prakas on minimum registered capital of banking and financial institutions, (iii) prakas on capital buffer in banking and financial institutions, (iv) prakas on credit risk grading and impairment provisioning, (v) prakas on auditing of banking and financial institutions.","National Bank of Cambodia"],[1,"90","3","Cross-Border Banking Supervisory Cooperation Mechanism","the National Bank of Cambodia has continued cooperating with other supervisory colleges that have established their branches and subsidiaries in Cambodia to strengthen cooperations by sharing information and any systematic risks and concerns in order to jointly solve the possible crisis and to prevent cross border systematic risks.","National Bank of Cambodia"],[1,"90","4","Banking and Financial Sector Compliance and Audit Oversight","the National Bank of Cambodia has issued a prakas on auditing companies for banking and financial institutions and has urged the financial and banking institutions to pay more attention to the compliance with the Basel Core Principles the compliance, the preparations of financial statements in accordance with international financial reporting standards (IFRS), the implementation of consumer protection policies; and the compliance with the foreign account tax compliance act (FATCA).","National Bank of Cambodia"],[1,"90","6","Liquidity Risk Management Prakas Preparation","NBC is preparing a number of Prakas related to liquidity risk management for the banks and financial insitutitions",""],[1,"90","6","Liquidity Provision Prakas for Banks and Financial Institutions","strengthened its role as the final borrower through the implementation of Prakas on liquidity provision for banks and financial institutions to be protected in advance for the systematic risks.",""],[1,"91","1","Financial Sector Crisis Management Mechanism","NBC, MEF, and SECC have established a working group to formulate a crisis management mechanism for Cambodia's financial sector.","NBC | MEF | SECC"],[1,"92","4","Risk-Based and Forward-Looking Supervision","The NBC remains committed to risk-based and forward- looking supervision as demonstrated by the recent issuance by NBC of the Prakas on the implementation of Risk-Based and Forward-looking Supervision.",""],[1,"92","4","Regular Monitoring of Laws and Regulations","Likewise, laws and regulations are required to be regularly monitored in order to catch up with the market progress.",""],[1,"130","3","Banking System Security and Financial Market Regulation","the RGC will continue to improve the security of the banking system (building firmness through enhancing monitoring and regulations) through adequate guarantees of international reserves to cope with stress and crisis.","NBC"],[1,"130","9","Strengthen NBC Financial Monitoring and Advance Notification System","Strengthen the capacity of the NBC's financial monitoring unit and advance notification system and require financial institutions to provide the necessary information in a timely manner.",""],[1,"130","10","National Committee on Financial Stability","Establish a National Committee on Financial Stability to provide a comprehensive institutional framework for monitoring financial stability.",""],[1,"130","13","Special Settlement Scheme for Bank Weaknesses","Establishing a special settlement scheme by offering NBC a low-cost alternative to dealing with weaknesses of banks.",""],[1,"130","14","Basel II Compliance and Bank Supervision Strengthening","Compliance with Basel II standards by moving in full compliance with 29 core principles on effective bank supervision with a focus on overall risk management and management processes.",""],[1,"131","1","Savings Index Regulation Review and Corrective Action","Review the regulation on savings index and immediate corrective action.",""],[1,"131","2","Risk Monitoring and Staff Capability Improvement","Improve its monitoring approach to risk and look forward and improve staff capability (through care and information technology).",""],[1,"131","3","Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing Scrutiny Enhancement","Improve the scrutiny of money laundering and terrorism financing and NBC and CAFIU, raising awareness among banks and MFI.",""],[1,"131","12","Shadow Banking Reduction Measures","Reduce shadow banking activities by strengthening data and information collection and taking legal action.",""]],"67":[[1,"132","2","Stock Market Development through National Listing and Public Stock Issuance","Continue to develop the stock market through promotion of national listing and issuance of public stock.",""],[1,"132","3","Financial Development Center Establishment","Assess the progress of the future of the commodity market, evaluate business conditions and cases, and find partners to establish a Financial Development Center.",""],[1,"132","4","National Committee for Financial and Institutional Statistics for Credit Assessment","Establish a national committee for financial and institutional statistics for credit assessment in establishing key risk management mechanisms/tools.",""],[1,"132","5","Corporate Affairs, Governance and Responsibility Law","Develop a new law on corporate affairs, governance and responsibility.",""],[1,"132","6","Regulation on Technology Use in Securities Trading and Financial Statements","Develop regulations on the use of technology in securities trading and other financial statements.",""],[1,"132","7","SME Bank Working Group Establishment","Establish a working group to establish the SME Bank/ Supervise the draft articles of Association of Business Planning, Selection technical assistance.",""]],"68":[[1,"24","2","Financial Sector Functionality Improvement","Improve the functionality the financial sector, including easing the supply/ reducing the cost of credit, so relieving a key constraint for enterprises of all sizes.",""],[1,"208","21","Financial Sector Development and Diversification","To date, the RGC's achievements include the development of policies and regulations, especially by strengthening control and monitoring mechanisms in the financial and banking sector, developing financial infrastructure, providing favorable conditions to people through imposing an interest rate ceiling of 18% per annum for loans from MFIs, further developing an insurance sector and securities market, which include primary market and equity-finance market, and establishing of derivatives market and raising awareness of advantages of listing on the stock market to facilitate SMEs' registration.",""],[1,"209","2","Payment Gateway Infrastructure Development","developing the payment gateway infrastructure",""],[1,"209","2","Fintech-Based Payment System Promotion","promoting the development of payment system using financial technologies (Fintech)",""],[1,"209","2","Financial Sector Policy and Regulatory Coordination","coordinating policy and regulatory frameworks",""],[1,"209","2","Financial and Banking Sector Capacity Strengthening","strengthening institutional capacity and human resources related to financial and banking sector in line with Cambodia's economic progress and in response to the needs of integrating Cambodia's financial system into the region and internationally",""],[1,"209","3","Financial Sector Supervision Strengthening","Further ensuring financial stability, especially through strengthening the management and supervision mechanisms of the financial and banking sector by adopting a risk- based and forward looking approach; speeding up the establishment of financial stability committee as well as developing a crisis prevention and resolution mechanism, including an early warning system, financing options and enacting a Law on Deposit Protection.",""],[1,"209","4","Banking Sector Domestic Financing Mobilization","Strengthening the roles of the banking sector to mobilize domestic financing; conducting studies and preparing policies and mechanisms to expand the financial service coverage and the principles of financial consumer protection to promote people's living standards and economic development.",""],[1,"209","5","Securities Market Development and Trading Mechanism Reform","Further developing the securities market by encouraging enterprises and companies to issue public securities; enhancing trading mechanism by establishing institutional investors; establishing future market operators; and exploring the possibility of developing a digital asset trading management mechanism.",""],[1,"209","6","Government Bond Market Development","Exploring the development of a government bond market to serve as the foundation for setting the base interest rate; mobilizing financing for public investment and strengthening monetary policy.",""],[1,"209","7","FinTech Development and Adoption in Banking Sector","Encouraging the development and use of Financial Technology (FinTech) in financial and banking sector aimed at modernizing and increasing the cost-effectiveness and safety of banking operations.",""],[1,"209","8","Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing Oversight Strengthening","Enhancing, analyzing and monitoring the competency and oversight on money laundering activities and terrorist financing.",""],[1,"209","9","National Riel Promotion Policy","Encouraging a wider use of the Riel by developing a national-level policy aimed at increasing participation from stakeholders; raising people's financial literacy aimed at increasing the efficiency and contributing to the economic growth.",""],[1,"209","10","Insurance Product Expansion and Regulatory Strengthening","Further strengthening and expanding new insurance products, especially life insurance and micro insurance by improving the regulatory framework; strengthening insurance operator's capacity and consumer protection.",""],[1,"209","12","Financial Stability Monitoring Capacity Strengthening","Maintaining the financial stability by strengthening the capacity and capabilities of the financial stability monitoring unit.",""],[1,"209","12","Early Warning System for Financial Sector Soundness","Early Warning System is one of the tools used to signal the potential for deterioration in the soundness of the financial institutions.",""],[1,"209","12","National Financial Stability Committee Establishment","The government plans to establish a national financial stability committee, which created a comprehensive institution framework in order to monitor and maintain the financial stability.",""],[1,"210","1","Crisis Preparedness Cooperation Framework and Contingency Planning","Preparing for crisis, which supervisory agencies will adopt a cooperation framework and procedures in crisis preparedness.",""],[1,"210","2","Depositor Protection Scheme","Studying the possibility of implementing a depositor protection scheme to increase public confidence in the banking system, especially for small depositors.","NBC | MEF"],[1,"210","2","Special Bank Resolution Regime","there is a need to establish a special resolution regime (i.e. a law providing NBC with more alternatives to resolve problem banking promptly with low cost).","NBC"],[1,"210","3","Banking Supervision Compliance Improvement","NBC will improve the status of compliance especially on risk management processes such as sovereign and transfer risk, operational risk, interest rate risk, and consolidated supervision.",""],[1,"210","4","Solvency and Prompt Corrective Action Regulatory Review","Reviewing regulation on solvency ratio and prompt corrective actions.",""],[1,"210","4","Banking Supervision Staffing and Capacity Building","NBC will also recruit and train additional staff in banking supervision and undertake other targeted capacity building program.","NBC"],[1,"210","4","Risk-Based and Forward-Looking Supervisory Reform","NBC will enhance its supervisory approach toward being risk based and forward-looking.","NBC"],[1,"210","4","Information Technology Upgrade for Banking Supervision","This process requires capacity building and undated information technology.",""],[1,"210","5","National Policy to Promote Use of the Riel","Further promoting the use of Riel currency by setting up a national policy on promoting the use of Riel.",""],[1,"210","6","Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Supervision and Awareness","Supervising anti money laundering and combating the financing of terrorism, an item in supervision and monitoring of banks.",""],[1,"210","7","Real Estate Registration and Ownership Title Reform","Improving the effectiveness in issuing ownership tittles as well as reducing its cost.",""],[1,"210","7","Fragmented Ownership and Co-owned Property Registration Resolution","the government plans to solve problems related to the issuance of fragmented ownership on co-owned building and real estate registration at Department of Collateral Registration.",""],[1,"210","7","Mandatory Real Estate Registration for Bank Borrowing","the government will enforce the process of real estate registration to be used when borrowing from banks and financial institutions.",""],[1,"210","8","Consumer Protection Regulatory Enhancement","Reviewing the desirability of expanding consumer protection principles in existing regulations by setting out more specific requirements on lending products, advertising and promotional materials, complaint procedures, fees, interest rate calculations, and collection practices.",""],[1,"210","10","Updated National Microfinance Strategy","Adopt the updated national strategy for microfinance sector and a new strategy for financial inclusion.",""],[1,"210","10","Financial Inclusion Strategy","Adopt the updated national strategy for microfinance sector and a new strategy for financial inclusion.",""],[1,"210","11","Microfinance Supervision and Basel Compliance Enhancement","Supervise the microfinance sectors and plan to enhance compliance with the Basel committee's Core principles for Effective Banking Supervision for microfinance activities.",""],[1,"211","1","Microfinance Institution Supervision Regulations","regulations following international standards for supervising microfinance institutions.",""],[1,"211","2","Enforcement Against Illegal Microfinance Operators","Strengthen enforcement of laws by taking strict actions against unregistered microfinance operators and those who continue to operate illegally.",""],[1,"211","3","Financial Literacy Public Awareness Campaigns","Enhance for Financial Literacy by continuing to conduct its public awareness campaigns, particularly for people in rural areas, in order to enhance further understanding about financial literacy and promoting financial inclusion, clearly clarifying with the public that microfinance institutions are neither state-owned and nor charitable organizations.",""],[1,"211","4","Interest Rate Reduction Study and Market-Based Financing Measures","Seek low funding sources, to study the factors that contribute to high cost of funds, and to find ways to reduce interest rates with market mechanism.",""],[1,"211","5","Shadow Banking Risk Reduction Measures","Reduce shadow banking activities by strengthening data and information gathering and taking action to reduce shadow banking activities that can create risks to financial stability.",""]],"69":[[1,"248","9","Development Financing Diversification Strategy","Five channels are reviewed: (1) better management/ coordination of grant in aid from (traditional) donors and accessing new partners; (2) additional concessional loans from multilateral institutions, and increasingly bilateral partners; (3) new revenue sources-fees and charges, additional taxes, or improved collection performance; (4) greater use of Public Private Partnership (PPP) arrangements/modalities; and (5) new borrowing from domestic sources.",""],[1,"249","3","Capital Investment Mobilization Efforts","the RGC will widen its capital investment mobilization efforts to address new opportunities (see below), but within ODA will seek: (1) to maximize the quality of donor assistance via better coordination and management; (2) to maximize the quality of grant aid by encouraging donors to move to budget support arrangements; and (3) by seeking increases in concessional finance by broadening those DPs engaged in concessional lending, and prioritizing high rates of return, typically focusing on infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"249","4","Strengthening Sectoral Technical Working Groups","The RGC will therefore work with partners to strengthen the TWG mechanism to enhance efficiency, build technical cooperation and human and institutional capacities.",""],[1,"249","5","Restructuring of Technical Working Groups","Reshaping the TWGs to cover sector or thematic issues (potentially to complement improved oversight as set out in the CSDG Framework Report);",""],[1,"249","6","Technical and Policy Support Focus for TWGs","Adopting greater focus within the TWGs on technical and policy support.",""],[1,"249","7","TWG Administrative Professionalization","Further developing the professionalism of TWG administration, including ensuring agendas are better prepared (with specific items), their advanced circulation with fixed deadlines, and keeping and circulating official minutes.",""],[1,"249","8","Budget Support Modalities for ODA Delivery","the government will also encourage development partners to adopt 'budget support' modalities for delivery of remaining, particularly capital investment related ODA flows.",""],[1,"250","2","Diversification of Development Lending Partners","the RGC will seek a wider arrange of development lending partners to support public capital investment, especially infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"250","2","Enhanced Financial and Socioeconomic Review of Borrowing Proposals","any new borrowings will be subject to high levels of financial scrutiny of financing proposals, alongside rigorous socioeconomic and environmental review of projects.",""],[1,"250","2","Prioritization of High-Return Infrastructure Projects","This will be combined (as noted) with a stronger prioritization placed on high rate of return projects.",""],[1,"250","2","Public Investment Program and Capital Budgeting Procedures","These will also be facilitated by new procedures within the three-year rolling Public Investment Program and capital budgeting within the Budget Strategic Framework.",""]],"70":[[1,"250","3","Resource Mobilization Strategy 2019-2023","via adoption of its new Resource Mobilization Strategy 2019-2023 (RMS), will boost additional non-tax revenues in key sectors.",""],[1,"250","3","National Revenue Management Information System Roll-out Completion","This will specifically include: measures to complete the roll-out of the National Revenue Management Information System (NRMIS);",""],[1,"250","3","Capacity Building for Fee and License Authorities","build capacity in ministries and agencies responsible for setting and collecting fees and issuing licenses;",""],[1,"250","3","Additional Revenue Regulations and Laws","and the enactment of any additional regulations and laws.",""],[1,"250","4","Tax Base Expansion Support","the Government will continue to support growth in the overall tax base",""],[1,"250","6","Tax Administration and Capacity-Building Measures","A series of supportive administrative and capacity building proposals will be set out in the final RMS.",""],[1,"250","6","Tax Policy Measures to Influence Consumer and Producer Behavior","The RGC is also seeking to use tax as a policy instrument to influence consumer and producer behaviors.",""],[1,"250","6","Tobacco Tax Increase and Demand Reduction Measures","Examples include raising the price and reducing demand/ use of tobacco and potentially other harmful products;",""],[1,"250","6","VAT and Excise Incentives for New Technology Adoption","and conversely, boosting the adoption of new technologies, by reducing the effective rate of VAT and/or excise on qualifying imports.",""],[1,"251","2","Development of Domestic Borrowing Sources through Riel-Denominated Bonds","the RGC is currently actively researching, and will bring forward proposals on the development of domestic sources of borrowing through the issuance of Riel dominated bonds.",""]],"71":[[1,"219","7","Agricultural Processing Industry Upgrading and Crop-Specific Strategies","Upgrading the processing industry through the promotion of private investment in agricultural products with high potentials such as rice, cassava, mango, cashew nuts, banana, rubber, vegetables, etc and through the formulation of specific strategy for each crop.",""],[1,"219","8","Farming Diversification for Import Substitution","Further promoting farming diversification aimed at substituting imports, and establishing clean and hygienic wholesale vegetable markets.",""],[1,"219","8","Clean and Hygienic Wholesale Vegetable Markets","Further promoting farming diversification aimed at substituting imports, and establishing clean and hygienic wholesale vegetable markets.",""],[1,"219","9","Agricultural Commercialization and SPS Strengthening","Promoting the commercialization of agriculture through better application of the Sanitary and Phytosanitary system, improved trade facilitation, additional investment in a quality laboratory for export and promoting the production and consumption of domestic agricultural products.",""],[1,"220","2","Private Investment Promotion for Agro-Processing","the CDC will undertake the following key activities:",""],[1,"220","3","Agricultural Processing Areas Feasibility Review and Incentive Scheme","Reviewing the feasibility for establishing the agricultural processing areas and provide incentives to companies located in those areas.",""],[1,"220","4","Business and Investment Forum for Agro-processing Investment Attraction","Co-organizing business and investment forum to attract more investors in agro- processing industry.",""],[1,"220","5","Review and Discussion of Agro-processing Investment Incentive Policies","Participating in the review and discussion of incentive policies for companies investing in the agro-processing industry.",""],[1,"220","6","Private Sector Export Agricultural Processing Areas","Cooperating with relevant ministries and agencies to promote and encourage the private sector to establish export agricultural processing areas.","relevant ministries and agencies"],[1,"220","9","Accelerating Inclusive Markets for Smallholders (AIMS) Program","continuing to implement the program of Accelerating Inclusive Markets for Smallholders (AIMS): The project covers 17 provinces and five types of products: fragrant rice, vegetables, chicken, cassava, and silk",""],[1,"220","9","Agricultural Product Promotion and Agro-industry Export Support","continuing to promote agricultural products and agro-industry to promote these Cambodian products, substituting for import and leading to the export of which to foreign markets",""],[1,"220","9","Cambodian Products Buy-Local Campaign and Trade Fair Participation","continuing to campaign for buying Cambodian products at the national in all provinces in Cambodia and participating in international trade fairs within the bilateral, regional and global framework",""],[1,"220","9","Chamber of Commerce and Business Association Expansion","strengthening private sector institutions through the establishment of chamber of commerce and business associations throughout the country",""],[1,"220","10","Strategic Food Inventory Maintenance and Expansion","continuing to strengthen and maintain strategic food inventory ready-to-use for helping intervention to victims of flood, storm and any damages",""],[1,"220","10","Rice Price Stabilization in Local Markets","continuing to strengthen the stability price of rice in local market in order to maintain the benefit for the people and prevent them from the market from being taken into chaos",""],[1,"220","10","Rice Trade and Market Operations","continuing to buy and sell rice",""],[1,"220","10","Bilateral Rice Trade Agreement Negotiation","continuing to negotiate bilateral trade agreement, with the existing rice markets",""],[1,"221","1","Household Rubber Farming Expansion and Processing Investment","Strengthening and enlarging household rubber farming to stimulate opportunities for farmer to benefit from cultivating, harvesting, and processing rubber and to enhance famers' bargaining power when selling their produce.",""],[1,"221","1","Rubber Processing Investment Promotion","Investment in rubber processing will be promoted to add value to the commodities and create job opportunities which will contribute to rural poverty alleviation.",""],[1,"221","2","Agricultural Product Diversification and Value-Addition Programme","Promoting diversification of agricultural products with higher added value in the crops, livestock, aquaculture, and timber farming sub-sectors as well as investment in main crops processing",""],[1,"221","2","Agricultural Quality, Packaging, and Standards Inspection Improvement","continuing to improve the quality and safety of the agricultural commodities, including packaging and enhancing the capacity for quality standards inspection",""],[1,"221","2","Crop Protection and SPS Control Strengthening","strengthening the crop protection measures, and SPS control",""],[1,"221","10","Agricultural Modernization and Crop Diversification Programme","To promote the production of all crops with around 5% growth per year and to increase the export of agricultural products by 7% per year through agricultural modernization, increased productivity, diversification of crops with high potential and strong competition in markets.",""]],"72":[[1,"233","8","Fisheries Resource Preservation and Management Programme","Continuing to promote the preservation and management of fisheries resource through combatting fisheries crimes, improving the fishing community, and increasing the aquaculture.",""],[1,"234","7","Sustainable Fisheries Resource Management and Conservation","Continuing to strengthen sustainable fisheries resource management and conservation in line with the Strategic Planning Framework for Fisheries 2015-2024 and the statements on national policy for fisheries, particularly through fighting all forms of crimes related to fisheries.",""],[1,"234","8","Aquaculture Expansion and Fisheries Protection Enforcement","Increasing aquaculture to increase the supply to fish farms, including techniques, fish varieties, credit, markets and the implementation and enforcement of laws through the continued use of existing mechanisms which is the priority in fisheries protection.",""]],"73":[[1,"231","20","Implementation of the National Policy on Promotion of the Agricultural Sector","the CARD will continue to implement the National Policy on Promotion of the",""],[1,"232","2","Legal Framework and Mechanism Development","Development of the legal framework and mechanism.",""]],"74":[[1,"23","12","Rural Productivity Improvement Initiative","and a specific focus on productivity in rural areas (encompassing farm and non-farm production).",""],[1,"48","2","Integrated Agricultural Modernization Measures","the RGC has taken some effective and efficient integrated measures to build and rehabilitate major infrastructure including improvement of agricultural production chains and the increase in market competitiveness, such as roads, water supply system, power supply distribution, technical assistant and agricultural inputs, land management reform and investment financing, mechanisms to increase the market access, agricultural community establishment and development, and the strengthening of institutional coordination machanisms.",""],[1,"48","3","Agricultural Extension Policy","The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries (MAFF) has recently introduced the Agricultural Extention Policy to ensure that farmers an their communities are able to acquire a better agricultural knowledge/skill and technology.","Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries (MAFF)"],[1,"48","4","Agricultural Support Services Expansion and Intensification Programme","The expansion and strengthening of the support services including research and dissermination of modern technology in all sub-sectors based on the potential geographical areas, the distribution of seed, fertilizers, agricultural materials, and the provision of rural credit, have been taken into serious consideration and set as priority by the government in order to elevate agricultural productivity in the respond to the market demand focusing on quantity, quality, safety and international standard.",""],[1,"51","16","Agricultural Training and Market Access Support","The use of the land is not maximized, requiring further support and trainings in the techniques of cultivating, livestocks and especially helping to find markets for the sale of collected products.",""],[1,"219","4","Agriculture Sector Master Plan and Strategic Development Plan Implementation","Promoting the development and implementation of the \"Master Plan for Agriculture Sector Development towards 2030\" and the \"Agriculture Sector Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023\".",""],[1,"219","5","Plant Protection and Sanitary and Phytosanitary Law Reform","Accelerating the process to prepare, enact and enforce the \"Law on Plants Protection and Sanitary and Phytosanitary\"",""],[1,"219","5","Contract Farming Law Reform","and the \"Law on Contract Farming\".",""],[1,"219","6","Agricultural Research and Innovation Investment Programme","increasing investments in R&D for high value-added crops, livestock and aquaculture",""],[1,"219","6","Model Farm Development Initiative","promoting a Model Farm development",""],[1,"219","6","Agricultural Extension Service Strengthening","boosting agricultural extension service",""],[1,"219","6","Farmer Cooperative Management Strengthening","strengthening farmer cooperative management",""],[1,"219","6","Contract Farming Production Mechanism","preparing contract farming production mechanism",""],[1,"219","6","Agricultural Input Cost Reduction and Quality Improvement","reducing costs and improving quality of agricultural inputs",""],[1,"219","6","Agricultural Insurance Services Study","conducting studies related to the establishment of agricultural insurance services",""],[1,"219","6","Agricultural Finance Product Development","developing financial products in support of agricultural production",""],[1,"219","6","Digital and Smart Agriculture Promotion","promoting the use of digital and smart technology in agriculture",""],[1,"220","12","Agricultural Research and Technology Development Enhancement","Continuing to enhance research into modern agricultural techniques and technology development in order to sustainably increase product quantity, quality and diversification while improving nutrition and adapting to climate change and local, regional and international market demand.",""],[1,"220","13","Agricultural and Livestock Cooperative Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of registered agricultural and animal raising cooperatives through promoting the performance of appropriate technology, the practice of water- saving techniques and contract-farming, and promoting private sector investment in agricultural value chains at all levels.",""],[1,"221","13","Agricultural Extension Services and Cooperative Development","Promoting agricultural extension services and agricultural cooperative development.",""],[1,"221","17","Cross-Sectoral Policy Project Implementation","Building and implementing projects related to cross-sectoral policies.",""],[1,"222","19","Institutional Management Support and Capacity Building for Sustainable Agriculture","To Optimize the effectiveness of institutional management, provide the supporting services and capacity building and education for the sustainable agriculture sector development with the following key priority activities:",""],[1,"222","20","Agricultural Institutional Management and Programme Budget Computerization","Optimizing the effectiveness of institutional management, providing the supporting services and human resource development in agriculture sector through strengthening and using the computerized system for planning, activity management, monitoring and evaluation of the Programme Budget",""],[1,"222","20","International Agricultural Cooperation and Education Quality Improvement","improving international cooperation and promoting the quality of agricultural education",""],[1,"222","21","Agricultural Private Investment and ICT Access Support","Promoting the appropriate environment for private investment in agriculture production chains, increasing technology usage (ICTs) to easily access production techniques, market information, value chain data and other agriculture information.",""],[1,"222","22","Agricultural Legal and Policy Framework Development","Preparing laws, legal instruments and the supporting agricultural policies.",""],[1,"222","24","Cambodian Academic Institution of Agricultural Sciences","Establishing and operating the Cambodian Academic Institution of Agricultural Sciences to optimize the effectiveness of agricultural research in Cambodia.",""]],"75":[[1,"221","5","Fishery Community Capacity Strengthening","7. Strengthening the capacity of existing fishery communities in both freshwater and marine territories such as free of illegal fishing.",""],[1,"221","7","Illegal Fishing and Flooded Forest Protection Enforcement","Continuing to use all means to detect, investigate and combat illegal fishing activities and flooded forest exploitation and encroachment with local authorities, armed forces and related institutions including prosecutors and the courts, and to demarcate flooded forest boundaries and to prevent and mitigate intrusion into flooded forest and forest lands as far as possible.",""],[1,"222","7","Fisheries Resource Management Strengthening","To improve fisheries resource management to be more effective and sustainable through strengthening the enforcement of Law on Fisheries, maintaining a natural fish catch of around 600,000 tons per year, increasing aquaculture yields by 20% per year and providing fishing communities with better livelihoods with the following key priority activities:",""],[1,"222","9","Freshwater and Maritime Aquaculture Development","Developing fresh water and maritime aquaculture.",""],[1,"222","10","Fisheries Value Chain Development and Management","Developing and managing fisheries value chain.",""],[1,"222","12","Fisheries Capacity and Human Resources Development","Strengthening the capacity of the units and developing human resources in fisheries.",""]],"76":[[1,"219","10","Livestock and Aquaculture Development Framework Implementation","Fostering livestock and aquaculture through continued implementation of the \"Law on Animal Health and Production\", the \"Strategic Planning Framework for Livestock Development 2016-2025\", and the \"National Aquaculture Development Strategy 2016-2030\".",""],[1,"221","3","Commercial Animal Husbandry Promotion","Promoting animal husbandry for commercial purposes in order to increase household profits and to encourage highly productive small, medium and large-scale animal farms that implement good quality, and safety measures as well as provide economic benefits to supply local demand and to increase export competitiveness.",""],[1,"221","4","Border Quarantine Control Stations for Agricultural Biosecurity","Establishing crop, animal and fish quarantine control stations at the main border gates to hinder the transmission of zoonosis as well as pest, animal and fish diseases and to restrict the import and export of poor-quality agricultural products which have negative effects on public health and damage both local and international markets.",""],[1,"221","18","Livestock Management and Development Programme","To achieve an animal production growth rate of 3% annually through the management and development of livestock, to reduce the risk of infectious diseases, and to reinforce the sanitary inspection of animal and animal products with the following key priority activities:",""],[1,"221","19","Animal Production Strengthening Programme","Strengthening animal production, including the promotion of animal management and breeding.",""],[1,"222","1","Legal Dissemination and Enforcement of Policy Implementation","Promoting the dissemination of the law and enforcing laws and policy implementation.",""],[1,"222","2","Animal Health and Production Research and Development","Promoting the research and development on animal health and production.",""],[1,"222","4","Public-Private Partnership Promotion","Promoting public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"222","5","Animal Health, Production, and Market Development Extension Services","Strengthening extension services on animal health, animal production and market development.",""],[1,"222","6","Animal Health and Production Cooperation Strengthening","Strengthening national and international economic and technical cooperation for the animal health and production sub-sector.",""],[1,"222","23","Local Human Resource Development and Capacity Building for Village Animal Health Workers","Increasing the investment in local human resource development through promotion of technical knowledge, and continuing to prepare the supporting structure through capacity building of village animal health workers to become agricultural promotion workers under the management of District Agriculture Office, to achieve sustainable development goals.",""]],"77":[[1,"50","2","Animal Waste Management and Biodigester Construction","With the development in sub sector on animal production, the animal waste management has been taken into high consideration through the provision of education and extension on animal husbandry best practice, the construction of bio-digester in animal farm and family animal raising.",""],[1,"50","5","Animal Product Sanitary Standards and Hygiene Measures","Formulation of legal standards and implementation of sanitary standards for animal products with the implementation of animal hygiene measures to prevent and combat public health disease through the prevention of human-to-human transmission and Modern slaughterhouse to protect public health and facilitate trade and respond to shifts International commitments.",""]],"78":[[1,"201","8","National Culture Development and Conservation Policy Implementation","the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts (MOCFA) will continue to implement its key priority policies including the national culture development and conservation","Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts (MOCFA)"],[1,"201","9","National Cultural Heritage Conservation and Cultural Industry Development Policies","Therefore, the RGC will put in place the policies that will help to create a suitable condition, which is an opportunity to \"develop national culture\" through encouraging creativity in the arts and culture as well as expanding the cultural industry.",""],[1,"201","10","National Cultural Heritage Database System","Updating the inventory of national cultural heritage by creating a national \"database system\"",""],[1,"201","11","Cultural Heritage Legal and Work Plan Development","Developing legal documents and work plans that respond to the specific situation in managing cultural heritage.",""],[1,"201","12","National Cultural Heritage Maintenance and Repair Measures","Putting in place the measures for the maintenance and repairing of national cultural heritage.",""],[1,"201","13","Illegal and Stolen Artifacts Reinstatement Mechanism","Strengthening the mechanism for the reinstatement of illegal and stolen artifacts both inside and outside the country.",""],[1,"201","14","National Cultural Heritage Awareness and Public Participation Initiative","Promoting the awareness and engaging the public participation in the preservation of national cultural heritage.",""],[1,"201","16","Cultural Knowledge and Professional Skills Development","Strengthening and expanding the development of knowledge and professional skills in the field of culture.",""],[1,"201","17","Traditional Knowledge Transfer Promotion","Maintaining and promoting the transfer of traditional knowledge.",""],[1,"201","18","Public Awareness and Participation Training on Education for Culture, Culture for Education","Increasing the awareness, attention and participation of the public, especially youths and children, by training on the principle of \"Education for Culture, Culture for Education\".",""],[1,"202","1","National Cultural Dissemination Expansion","Strengthening and expanding the scope of the national cultural dissemination through performance, conference, exhibitions, etc.",""],[1,"202","2","Museum and Cultural Center Strengthening and Expansion","Strengthening and expanding the roles of museums and cultural centers.",""],[1,"202","3","National Cultural Heritage Research and Promotion","Researching and promoting national cultural heritage.",""],[1,"202","4","UNESCO Heritage File Preparation and Registration Initiative","Preparing a compilation of Cambodia's outstanding and luxurious heritage files to register in the UNESCO's list.",""],[1,"202","5","Legal Support Framework for the Culture Sector","Developing legal documents and mechanisms to support artists, producers, associations, and entrepreneurs who are engaged in the culture sector.",""],[1,"202","6","Cultural Product and Labor Market Development","Cooperating with relevant ministries and agencies to promote the creation of cultural product market and labor markets in the culture and arts sector.",""],[1,"202","7","Cultural Markets and Products Expansion","Expanding cultural markets and products by providing a wide range of opportunities for artists, producers and artists in the culture and arts sector.",""],[1,"202","9","Promotion of Creativity in Arts, Culture and Industry","Promoting the exhibition of creativity in arts, culture and industry.",""],[1,"202","12","Foreign Film Production Promotion Initiative","Increasing the promotion in all forms to attract foreign filmmakers in Cambodia to become a welcoming land for foreign film productions.",""],[1,"202","13","One-Window Film Permit Facilitation Mechanism","Increasing the facilitation mechanism in applying for filming through one window service office.",""],[1,"202","14","Golden Hour Policy for Domestic Films","Continuing the policy \"Golden Hour\" for domestic movies.",""],[1,"202","17","Database on Cultural Organizations, Associations and Enterprises","Establishing a database on cultural organizations, associations and enterprises",""],[1,"202","18","Culture Identification and One Village One Product Initiative","Identifying culture and one village one product.",""],[1,"202","19","Technology Equipment Import Facilitation Mechanism for Cultural Entrepreneurs","Setting up mechanisms to facilitate the import of standard and legal technology equipment to entrepreneurs in the culture sector.",""]],"79":[[1,"82","1","Ancient Buildings Protection and Preservation Programme","The Ministry has been protecting and preserving ancient buildings at risk by repairing temples in the provinces and managing ancient stations facing losses by setting standards and the boundaries of ancient stations in the capital and in some provinces.","The Ministry"],[1,"82","9","Temple Conservation and Repair Programme","Conserve and repair Bantey Chmar and Bantey Tob temples",""],[1,"82","10","Temple and Bridge Conservation and Repair","Conserve and repair Trapaing Prasat temple and Tob bridge",""],[1,"82","11","Temple Conservation and Repair Programme","Conserve and repair Banon temple, the north corridor of Baset temple, Ek Phnom temple and Steong temple",""],[1,"82","12","Temple Conservation and Repair Programme","Conserve and repair Preah Steong temple and Bakan temple",""],[1,"82","13","Sambo Preykuk Temple Restoration","Repair Sambo Preykuk temples",""],[1,"82","14","Cultural Heritage Conservation and Repair Works","Conserve and repair Phnom Trob temple, Mohaleap pagoda, the north entrance gate of Nokor Bachey temple, Svay Sach Phnom pagoda, Hannchey temple, centers of Hannchey temple",""],[1,"82","15","Temple Conservation and Repair Programme","Conserve and repair Preah Theat Toch temple, Cheong Ong Temple",""],[1,"82","16","Temple Conservation and Repair Programme","Conserve and repair Kachroleong temple, Srey Krubleak temple",""],[1,"82","17","Temple Conservation and Repair Programme","Conserve and repair Phnom Chiso temple, Neang Khmov temple, Tmor Dos temple, Tamao temple, Taprum temple (Tonle Bati)",""],[1,"82","18","Preah Samdey Temple Conservation and Repair","Conserve and repair Preah Samdey temple",""],[1,"82","20","World Heritage Cultural Heritage Documentation","Collecting and compiling books on cultural heritages that have been listed as World Heritage List until 2017.",""],[1,"84","1","Cultural Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","In addition to enforcing the existing laws and regulations, the ministry has drafted royal- decrees, sub-decrees, and important Prakas that are fundamental to preserving and developing the culture.",""],[1,"84","13","Cultural Crimes Cooperation and Protection Measures","Continued cultural crimes that requires cooperation and protection from relevant ministries and agencies because of the wide range of cultural works across the country, including tangible and intangible heritage.",""],[1,"233","10","Cultural Heritage Preservation and Development Programme","Continuing to preserve and develop the cultural heritage by encouraging their additional inscription, strengthening the management, research, studies, and compilation as well as generating value from the cultural heritage.",""],[1,"235","17","Cultural Heritage Management Strengthening","Strengthening the cultural heritage management in collaboration with culturally responsible institutions, concerned units and development partners.",""],[1,"236","1","Natural-Cultural Heritage Capacity Building and Public Awareness Programme","Enhancing the capacity of the organizations and disseminate information and education on the value of comprehensive natural-cultural heritage to the public.",""],[1,"237","11","National Cultural Heritage Inventory Database Update","Updating the National Cultural Heritage Inventory by creating a national database that is easy to identify cultural heritage risk regularly.",""],[1,"237","12","Cultural Heritage Management Mechanisms and Regulations","Establishing mechanisms, regulations and work plans that address the real situation of cultural heritage management.",""],[1,"237","13","National Cultural Heritage Safeguarding and Restoration Measures","Taking appropriate measures in time to safeguard, preserve and restore national cultural heritage which is at risk or loss.",""],[1,"237","14","Cambodian Artifact Recovery Mechanism","Strengthening mechanisms for recovering Cambodian artifacts that were illegally stolen and held locally and abroad.",""],[1,"237","15","National Cultural Heritage Awareness and Public Participation Initiative","Raising awareness and encouraging the public participation in the preservation of national cultural heritage.",""],[1,"237","18","Traditional Knowledge Transfer Promotion","Maintaining and promoting the transfer of traditional knowledge.",""],[1,"237","19","Public Awareness and Participation Training on Education for Culture","Increasing the awareness, attention and participation of the public, especially youth and children, through the training of \"Education for Culture, Culture for Education\".",""],[1,"237","22","National Cultural Promotion Expansion","Strengthening and expanding the scope of national cultural promotion through performances, festivals, exhibitions, etc.",""],[1,"237","23","Museum and Cultural Center Strengthening and Expansion","Strengthening and expanding the roles of museums and cultural centers.",""],[1,"237","24","National Cultural Heritage Research and Dissemination","Researching and disseminating national cultural heritage.",""],[1,"237","25","UNESCO Heritage Registration Initiative","Compiling the documents to register Cambodia's most valuable and valuable heritage items and sites in UNESCO's list.",""]],"80":[[1,"187","2","Electricity Rate Reduction and Grid Expansion","Reducing further the electricity rates, expanding supply coverage and enhancing electricity reliability through the construction of additional sub-stations closer to economic development poles and areas with high economic potentials.",""],[1,"195","12","Power Sector Development and Electricity Supply Improvement","the MME will continue its priority activities in managing and promoting the power sector development to achieve an adequate, reliable, quality, and affordable electricity supply for all types of users","MME"],[1,"195","12","Energy Efficiency and Energy Saving Promotion","to manage and promote the development of energy efficiency and energy saving","MME"],[1,"195","13","Energy Sector and Electricity Connectivity Expansion","Promoting the development of the energy sector and electricity by enhancing the connectivity to people with quality, stable and affordable electricity in a variety of sources, including hydropower, combustion, and solar power.",""],[1,"195","14","Building Energy Efficiency and Electricity Standards Strengthening","Strengthening the energy techniques and electricity standard in buildings and housings.",""]],"82":[[1,"55","11","Technical Safety Management Regulation for Fuel and LPG Service Stations","Prakas on the procedure of technical safety management of the installation fuel service station, LPG station, and joint fuel and LPG service station.",""],[1,"55","12","Safety Circular for Fuel and LPG Service Stations","Circular on the safety of the installation fuel service station, LPG station, and joint fuel and LPG service station.",""],[1,"55","15","Petroleum Production Well Development for Block A","Signed petroleum MOU with KrisEnergy Corporation for the petroleum production well development Block A.",""],[1,"202","20","Mining Sector Development and Resource Value Chain Expansion","the MME has a big mission in maximizing the development of mining through the exploration, production development, treatment, transport, inventory, oil and gas trade","MME"],[1,"202","21","National Petroleum Policy 2020-2030","the MME will formulate the National Petroleum Policy 2020- 2030 and introduce the action plan for the implementation in 2020.","MME"],[1,"202","22","Legal and Regulatory Development","Developing laws and regulations.",""],[1,"202","23","Institutional Capacity Building and Strengthening Initiative","Building capacity and strengthening the institutions both upstream and downstream.",""]],"83":[[1,"195","12","Civil Nuclear Energy Research and Development","The MME also aims to manage and promote the research, development and use of civil nuclear energy, including radiation and nuclear energy techniques for the purpose of peace, safety and security","MME"],[1,"195","15","Civil Nuclear Science and Technology Strengthening","Strengthening the science and technology of civil nuclear energy, including radiation and nuclear energy techniques.",""],[1,"196","9","Nuclear and Radiological Safety Regulations Development","Development of technical specifications and regulations related to the management, safety, security, and safety protection of the nuclear and radiative substance.",""]],"84":[[1,"53","3","Forest Sub-sector Reform Implementation","The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries (MAFF) has focused mainly on the implementation of forest sub-sector reform.","Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries (MAFF)"],[1,"57","1","National Strategic Planning for Protected Area Management and REDD+","the MOE has prepared a number of necessary documents, especially the National Strategic Plan for the Management of the Protected Areas 2017-2031, and the National REDD+ Strategy 2017- 2026, which is important to mobilize funds from other sources for managing, preserving and conserving sustainable forest resources in Cambodia.","MOE"],[1,"57","1","REDD+ Project Implementation in Key Wildlife Sanctuaries and National Park","three REDD+ projects are at the \"Keo Seima\" wildlife sanctuary, \"Prey Lang\" wildlife sanctuary and \"Tatai\" sildlife sanctuary and the Southern Cardamom Mountains National Park",""],[1,"57","1","Technical Procedure Development for Valuation Validity","has been cooperating the development of technical procedures for validity valuation between the General Department of Nature Conservation and Protection and some core partners.",""],[1,"57","2","Decentralized Protected Areas and REDD+ Management Delegation","to implement the Decentralization and Deconcentration Policy, the MOE has been delegating the functions of the administration for Nature Conservation and Protection to the capital and provincial Departments of the Environment on the implementation of the management of protected areas and the implementation of REDD + activities at the sub-national level","MOE"],[1,"157","16","Natural Protected Areas Boundary Identification and Registration","Identifying the boundaries, the management area and registration of the natural protected areas as the state public properties.",""],[1,"157","18","Delegation of Protected Area Management to SNAs","Promoting the delegation of management of the natural protected areas to SNAs, identifying the new protected areas.",""],[1,"157","19","Protected Area Habitat Rights and Land Dispute Resolution","Determining the habitat rights of the protected areas and addressing land disputes in protected areas, including in the economic land concession project areas.",""],[1,"157","20","Forest Cover Regeneration and Protected Area Conservation Strategy","Developing a strategy to regenerate forest cover through reforestation and enhancing the conservation and rehabilitation of genetic resources of the plants, forests and wildlife in protected areas.",""],[1,"158","1","REDD+ Implementation Efficiency and Forest Carbon Management","Promoting the efficiency of REDD+ implementation, reducing greenhouse gas emissions from deforestation, conserving forest carbon stocks, sustainable forest management, and increasing forest carbon inventory.",""],[1,"158","2","Conservation Innovation and Sustainable Ecotourism Financing Mechanisms","Developing innovations in conservation and development, including creating opportunities for sustainable ecotourism and financing mechanisms.",""],[1,"158","3","Environmental Education and Public Participation Expansion","Strengthening and expanding environmental education activities, enhancing the dissemination of the environmental information, updating the environmental statistics, promoting the participation of environment-friendly activities in order to achieve better public participation in environmental protection, biodiversity conservation and the sustainable use of natural resources.",""],[1,"158","4","Community Forestry Studies in Newly Created Protected Areas","Continuing community forestry studies in newly-created protected areas to develop more protected communities.",""],[1,"158","5","Protected Areas Community Network Establishment","Cooperating with SNAs and relevant ministries and agencies in the establishment of protected areas community networks, including national, regional and the protected area committee.",""],[1,"158","6","Community Employment Expansion for Local Livelihoods","Improving the community livelihoods by expanding/increasing employment for local communities located in the East of the Mekong, North and South Tonle Sap Lake are established and managed",""],[1,"158","7","Integration of Community Management Activities into Commune Investment Plans","Integrating all activities in the community management plan into each commune investment plan",""],[1,"158","8","Eco-Tourism Promotion and Access Facilitation","Cooperating and partnering with relevant ministries and agencies, especially tourism and eco-tourism companies and agencies to promote eco-tourism in an effective and easy way to access ecotourism sites and the eco-tourism community.","relevant ministries and agencies"],[1,"158","9","Cultural and Natural Heritage Management Strengthening","Strengthening the cultural heritage management in collaboration with institutions responsible for culture, relevant institutions, and development partners and strengthening the management of natural heritage.",""],[1,"158","10","Natural and Cultural Heritage Capacity and Public Awareness Programme","Strengthening the capacity of the organization and disseminating information and education on the value of natural and cultural heritage to the public.",""],[1,"233","7","Forest Cover Maintenance and Wildlife Protection Programme","Continuing to manage the forest and wildlife resource by maintaining the forest cover more than 60% of the country land area, promoting the forest and wildlife preservation, preventing the forest encroachment and clearing for private ownership purpose, promoting the contribution of community in forest prevention and restoration as well as combatting the forest crime and wildlife trafficking.",""],[1,"234","10","Forest and Wildlife Research and Development Enhancement","Enhancing the research and development on forests and wildlife.",""],[1,"234","12","Strengthening Enforcement of Forest Law","Strenghthenig the enforcement of Law on Forest.",""],[1,"234","15","Protected Area Management System Strengthening","Improving the effectiveness of the protected area management system through strengthening the management capacity of the organization and through good governance.",""],[1,"234","16","Protected Areas Demarcation and Management Planning","Demarcating, identifying management areas, registering protected areas as the state public property, while having a clear plan for protected areas management.",""],[1,"234","17","Law Enforcement Modernization and Skills Training","Increasing law enforcement efficiency and reducing threats with modern equipment and training on law enforcement and related skills as needed in each area.",""],[1,"234","18","Delegation of Protected Area Management to SNAs","Encouraging the delegation of the management function of protected areas to SNAs",""],[1,"234","19","Protected Area Land Rights and Conflict Resolution","Determining land rights in protected areas and resolving land conflicts in protected areas, including in the areas of economic land consession projects.",""],[1,"234","20","Creation of New Protected Areas","Creating new protected areas.",""],[1,"234","21","Forest Reforestation and Biodiversity Conservation Strategy","Developing strategies to increase forest cover through reforestation and promoting conservation and restoration of genetic resources, plants, forests and wildlife in protected areas.",""],[1,"235","1","REDD+ Programme Effectiveness Improvement","Improving the effectiveness of REDD+ programs by reducing greenhouse gas emissions from deforestation and degradation, conserving carbon stocks, sustainable forest management, and increasing forest carbon inventory.",""],[1,"235","5","Environmental Data Organization and Mapping Services","Organizing the environmental data, providing environmental mapping services such as biodiversity conservation maps, maps used for protected areas management, managment area maps in protected areas, community protected area maps, and ecotourism corridor maps.",""],[1,"235","7","Community Protected Areas Review and Management Plan Update","Continuing to review and update community protected areas and management plans",""],[1,"235","8","Forest Community Study for Community Protected Area Development","Studying forest communities in newly established protected areas to further develop community protected areas.",""],[1,"235","11","Co-management and Community Participation in Protected Areas","Selecting and implementing the concept of \"co-management and community participation\" in several protected area communities located in the eastern part of the Mekong River and north and south parts of the Tonle Sap.",""],[1,"241","15","Implementation of Green Growth and Climate Strategy Frameworks","Continuing to implement the \"National Strategic Plan on Green Growth 2013-2030\", \"Cambodia Climate Change Strategic Plan 2014-2023\", \"National Environment Strategy and Action Plan 2016-2023\", \"National REDD+ Strategy\"; and use social and environmental funds effectively to ensure economic development with low-carbon emission and resilience to climate change.",""],[1,"241","16","Protected Areas and Biodiversity Conservation Strengthening","Further strengthening the management of protected areas, biodiversity conservation, natural resource conservation, especially the ecosystems of Tonle Sap lake, Mekong river and the coastline areas.",""],[1,"242","14","Delegation of Functions and Resources to SNAs","Delegating functions and resources to SNAs to strengthen responsibility and ownership to ensure the sustainability of environmental and natural resources.",""],[1,"243","2","Ecosystem Services Payment Mechanisms","including the implementation of ecosystem services payment mechanisms.",""],[1,"243","3","Ecosystem Services Payment Policy Framework","Developing a policy framework for ecosystem services payment.",""]],"85":[[1,"221","6","National Forestry Program Update","Updating the national forestry program in the context of the current reform for stable, long term forestry development.",""],[1,"222","13","Forest Law Enforcement and Replantation Programme","To manage sustainably the forest resource and wildlife though strengthening the enforcement of Law on Forest, by promoting forest replantation, increasing research and development on forests and wildlife, and building the the capacity of forest communities to have a better living condition with the following key priority activities:",""],[1,"222","15","Forest and Wildlife Research and Development Enhancement","Enhancing the research and development on forests and wildlife.",""]],"86":[[1,"156","5","Comprehensive Environmental Management Approach","the Ministry of Environment and National Council for Sustainable Development will maintain the comprehensive approach for the environment management in Cambodia through:","Ministry of Environment | National Council for Sustainable Development"],[1,"156","8","Renewable Energy Policy and Regulatory Reform","Improving policies and regulations to increase the contribution of renewable energy in Cambodia's diverse energy sector.",""],[1,"156","10","Strategic Environmental Assessment Integration","Promoting the inclusion of strategic environmental assessments into decision-making process, policies, plans and regulations to ensure the sustainability of the environment and natural resources.",""],[1,"157","1","Green City Strategic Plan Implementation","Implementing the Green City Strategic Plan in urban areas.",""],[1,"157","2","Decentralization of Environmental and Natural Resource Management Functions and Resources","Decentralization of functions and resources to sub-national levels to strengthen ownership in order to ensure the sustainability of environmental and natural resources",""],[1,"157","4","Nationally Determined Contributions Implementation Roadmap","Developing a roadmap for implementing the National Determined Contributions (NDC) for the implementation of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change.",""],[1,"157","6","Ecosystem Service Charges Policy Framework","Establishing a policy framework for ecosystem service charges.",""],[1,"157","8","Policy and Regulatory Reform Package","Establishing key policies and regulaiton, including 7 sub-decrees, amendment of 4 sub-decrees, 4 inter-ministerial Prakas, 4 Prakas, a Joint Prakas on the Delivery of Public Services and Transitional Fines, drafting of an inter-ministerial circular on the implementation of Sub-decree on Plastic Bag Management, and two technical guidelines.",""],[1,"157","9","Environmental Quality Monitoring","Continuing to monitor the environmental quality at the targets in the capital and provinces.",""],[1,"157","10","Public Water Monitoring and Sampling Expansion","Expanding the targets for monitoring and sampling public water in areas that are threatened by environmental pollution.",""],[1,"157","12","Environmental Protection Regulation Enforcement","Continuing to enforce legal regulations related to environmental protection at factories, enterprises, companies and investment projects throughout the country.",""],[1,"157","13","Automatic Pollution Source Monitoring and Reporting System","Promoting the implementation of automatically regulating and reporting system for critical pollution sources and equip the automatic tool for monitoring the waste release.",""],[1,"157","14","Database of Toxic Substances Release Implementation","Promoting the implementation of the database of toxic substances released in the environment.",""],[1,"157","17","Enforcement Modernization and Training Programme","Increasing efficiency of enforcement and mitigating threats by equipping modern tools and training on enforcement of relevant laws and skills in each area.",""]],"87":[[1,"22","25","Natural Resource Protection and Climate Change Action","Three themes underpin the approach are accountability - a stakeholder system of responsiveness, adherence to mandate and to cross government cooperation, is coupled with emphasis on efficiency - building human resources, facilitating structural change and harnessing technology notably industrial revolution 4.0; improved opportunities for all, particularly the vulnerable groups, improved public services, as well as protecting natural resources and combating climate change.",""],[1,"42","2","Community Resource Protection and Management Initiative","The RGC is working with communities to restore environmental losses through promoting sustainable protection and management of community resources.",""],[1,"42","5","Cross-Sector Environmental Coordination and Cooperation","The RGC will continue to focus on reforestation to restore forest cover.",""],[1,"42","5","Reforestation for Forest Cover Restoration","The RGC will continue to focus on reforestation to restore forest cover.",""],[1,"56","2","Development Partner Collaboration for Budget Mobilization","Collaborated with development partners in formulating proposals to mobilize budget for implementation of climate change programs, management of biodiversity resources and biosafety, sustainable city, sustainable energy, and scientific and technological researches.",""],[1,"56","3","Increased Budget Allocations for Cambodia Climate Change Projects and Programs","The RGC has increased its budget allocations for the implementation of the Cambodia climate change projects and programs.",""]],"88":[[1,"191","17","Marine Pollution Prevention from Ships Project","Continuing to implement the IMO/NORAD project on the prevention of marine pollution from ships.",""],[1,"191","18","National Emergency Plan for Oil Spill Response","Reviewing the draft of the National Emergency Plan for combating oil spills.",""]],"89":[[1,"235","3","Environmental Education Policy and Practice Promotion","Promoting the transformation of environmental knowledge into environmental practices through the development of environmental education policies, environmental education strategies, environmental events, and environmental education activities such as the improvement of the national environmental education program, the continued implementation of environment-friendly schools, the implementation of environment-friendly pagodas, the promotion of green community movement, and environment-friendly houses.",""],[1,"235","4","Environmental Information Dissemination and Public Awareness Campaign","Promoting environmental information dissemination activities in all forms and means by continuing to cooperate with relevant stakeholders to change people's attitude towards environment.",""],[1,"235","6","Green Awards and Certification Scheme","Promoting environment-friendly competitions through awards, and green certifications to environmental-friendly operators, technology discovery service providers, and green product manufacturers.",""]],"90":[[1,"71","1","Mekong River Commission Procedures Implementation","Continued implementing the Mekong River Commission's procedures for sharing of data and information, water usage monitoring, notification, prior consultation and agreement, maintenance of water on the main river and water quality.",""],[1,"71","4","Equal-Proportion Financial Contributions to the Mekong River Commission","Approved the formulation of financial contributions in equal proportion by 2030, which highlights the high commitment of the governments of the four countries to the Mekong River Commission.",""],[1,"71","5","Dialogue Partner Cooperation and Joint Research Mechanism","Continued to strengthen cooperation with dialogue partners: China and Myanmar and shared data and information, joint technical conferences and exchange visits, and joint research on key issues and collaboration with Lancang-Mekong Water Resources Operation Center.",""],[1,"71","10","Strengthening Mekong River Basin Regional Cooperation Mechanisms","The role of the Mekong River Commission in regional cooperation is limited, which is necessary to continue and promote regional cooperation and relations with existing regional mechanisms and new mechanisms related to the development and management of water resources and retated resources in the Mekong Basin.",""]],"91":[[1,"178","11","Urban Water Supply Legal Framework Development","Developing a legal framework for the urban water supply sector.",""],[1,"178","12","Urban Water Supply Decentralization and Deconcentration","Promoting decentralization and deconcentration in the urban water supply sector.",""],[1,"178","13","Water Resource Protection and Regulatory Strengthening","Increasing the protection of water resources and strengthening the regulation.",""],[1,"178","15","Clean Water Awareness and Participation Campaign","Promoting awareness of the benefits of clean water and participation to implement \"clean water for all\".",""],[1,"188","11","Provincial Water Treatment System Project","Water Treatment System Project in some provinces, especially Preah Sihanouk province.",""],[1,"230","21","Clean Water Policy Implementation for Urban Water Access","To implement the RGC's priority policies in the Sixth Legislature of the National Assembly in implementing the Clean Water Policy so that 100% of urban people have access to clean water services by 2025 and ensuring four preconditions: quality, safety, sustainability and affordability, the MIH has the following priority activities:","MIH"],[1,"230","22","Sector Development Strategy and Financing Plan Development","Developing sector development strategies, including long-term financing and investment plans.",""],[1,"230","23","Public Entity Five-Year Business Planning Requirement","Ensuring all public entities formulate their 5-year business plans well by 2023.",""],[1,"230","24","Restoration of Production Facilities and Distribution Networks","Restoring existing production facilities and distribution networks using the RGC's organizational resources and financing from development partners.",""],[1,"231","1","Provincial Public Water Supply Capacity Expansion","Providing full autonomy to public entities by building public water supply capacity in the provinces to promote the autonomy as the economic public enterprise.",""],[1,"231","2","Approval of Entities as Economic Public Entities","Following the model and experience of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority (PPWSA), in which all entities will be approved as economic public entities by 2023.",""],[1,"231","3","Public Water Supply Service Improvement and Cost Recovery Reform","Striving to push the public water supply authorities to provide quality services, affordable prices, ensured full payment of costs and resources for re-investment.",""],[1,"231","4","Water Quality Monitoring System Development","Developing an effective water quality monitoring system to ensure that drinking water supply complies with national drinking water quality standards.",""],[1,"231","5","Development Partner Financing for Supply Capacity Rehabilitation and Expansion","Continuing good cooperation with development partners to obtain financing for rehabilitation and expansion of supply capacity in line with development plans.",""],[1,"231","6","Private Sector Finance Access Support","Studying and promoting access to receive finance for the private sector through working with the RGC's institutions, development partners, NGOs and local and international banks to support the private sector in accessing favorable loans.",""],[1,"231","7","Private Sector Investment Promotion Framework","Encouraging the investment from the private sector by establishing policies, legal frameworks, as well as facilitating an investment environment conducive to private-public partnerships, and private investment.",""],[1,"231","8","Water Supply Improvement Coordination","Collaborating with relevant institutions to ensure the achievement of the goal of improved water supply.",""],[1,"231","9","Partnership with Cambodia Water Suppliers Association","Strengthening the partnership with the \"Cambodia Water Suppliers Association\" to jointly achieve Cambodia's Water Sector Development Strategy.",""],[1,"231","10","Climate Change Preparedness and Disaster Risk Cooperation for the Clean Water Sector","Cooperating with the National Committee for Disaster Management in preparing for climate change as well as participating in all activities to reduce the impact on the clean water sector.",""],[1,"231","11","Urban Water Supply Legal Framework","Establissing a legal framework for the urban water supply.",""],[1,"231","12","Urban Water Supply Decentralization and Deconcentration","Promoting decentralization and deconcentration in urban water supply sector.",""],[1,"231","13","Water Source Protection and Regulatory Strengthening","Increasing the protection of water sources and strengthening regulations.",""],[1,"231","17","Clean Water for All Subsidy Program","Implementing 'Clean Water for All' program, with a focus on providing subsidies on networking fees to the poorest and most vulnerable families.",""],[1,"231","18","Water Quality Service Quality Indicator System","Creating a competitive environment by introducing key water quality service quality indicators as a measure of the organization's capacity and transparent monitoring system.",""],[1,"231","19","Clean Water Education and Information Dissemination Program","Conducting educational programs and disseminating information on clean water to people of all levels for development cooperation.",""]],"92":[[1,"188","6","Sewage Treatment Station Construction","Continuing to build sewage treatment stations in key provinces.",""],[1,"188","7","Wastewater and Drainage Infrastructure Investment Cooperation","Continuing to cooperate with development partners, organizations and private companies in investing in wastwater (drainage, flood protection system, wastwater treatment and garbage).",""],[1,"188","8","Wastewater Treatment Station Master Plan Finalization and Implementation","Promoting the finalization and implementation of the Master Plan for WastWater Treatment Station throughout the country.",""]],"93":[[1,"69","10","Water Resources Development and Management Strategic Plan Implementation","Hence the implementation of the MOWRAM's strategic plan on water resources development and management, the Rectangular Strategy Phase III for the Fifth Mandate of the National Assemble and National Strategic Development Plan 2014-2018 aims at increasing the ability and potential of irrigation in addition to the existing irrigation capacity to increase agricultural production, flood and drought mitigation, and sea water intrusion prevention.","Ministry of Water Resource and Meteorology (MOWRAM)"],[1,"70","4","Hydrological Station Network Expansion","Set up 25 hydrological stations along Mekong, Tonle Sap and Basac River.",""],[1,"70","7","Automatic Stream Monitoring Equipment Installation","Set up 08automatic equipment along stream in Kampong Speu province.",""],[1,"70","8","Meteorological Station Expansion and Repair","Set up 44meteorological stations and repaired 14 stations in the provinces.",""],[1,"130","11","National Disaster Preparedness Framework and Plans","Improve preparedness for crises including the establishment of a national institutional framework, a national disaster prevention plan along with agency preparedness plans.",""]],"94":[[1,"226","10","Flood Control and Water Drainage Development","Promoting and encouraging the study and construction of flood controls and water drainage with the aim of minimizing natural disasters caused by water.",""],[1,"226","11","Flood Mitigation and Community Awareness Programme","Taking actions to mitigate flood in all areas which provide high economic potential by providing education to communities and public information through media.",""],[1,"226","12","Urgent Disaster Response for Water-Related Damage","Responding urgently to areas serverely affected by drought, flood and other destructions caused by water.",""],[1,"226","13","Flood Mitigation Participation and Awareness Actions","Continuing to encourage people and all institutions to participate in flood mitigation actions such as preparing safety hills, supplying materials and machinary, educating, and participating in national and international events on flood risk reduction.",""],[1,"226","14","Pumping Station and Water Pump Repair Programme","Setting up pumping stations and repairing pumping stations and water pumps.",""],[1,"226","15","Emergency Rice Rescue Intervention for Water Shortages","Being ready to intervene to rescue dry season rice and rainy season rice for people in all provinces in case of water shortage, especially in areas near water resources that are not irrigated by irrigation schemes.",""],[1,"227","3","Protection of Agricultural Land, Public Property, and National Physical Infrastructure","Sustain and expand protection over agricultural area, public property and national physical infrastructure",""],[1,"227","5","Agricultural Area and Crop Protection Programme","Sustain and expand protection over agricultural area and all kind of crops",""],[1,"227","7","Pumping Station Installation","Set up pumping stations",""],[1,"228","15","Flood Alleviation and Capacity Building","Flood alleviation and capacity building to ensure protecting from floods caused by rainwater and sea water.",""]],"95":[[1,"228","4","Water Resources Management Law Enforcement and Project Screening","Strengthening and encouraging the enforcement of Water Resources Management Law and other related provisions to monitor and prevent all rehabilitation and construction projects which might have adverse impact on water resources and eco- systems.",""],[1,"228","5","River and Lake Water Level Maintenance","Maintaining water discharge and minimum water level in river, and lake for sustainable ecological systems and waterway transport.",""],[1,"228","6","Land Filling and Excavation Prohibition and Waterbody Protection Enforcement","Prohibiting and taking urgent action to prevent the invasion of land filling or excavation or the invasion of water in rivers, lakes, ponds, and canals as well as regular inundated or coastal areas without any permission which in turn impacts water resources, eco-system and environment.",""],[1,"228","7","River Basin and Natural Lake Conservation","Strengthening river basin and natural lake conservation which could store water to help reduce flood and maintain ecosystems.",""],[1,"228","8","Sub-decree on Irrigation System Geographic Mapping and Reservoir Protection","Preparing a sub-decree to define the geographical map of irrigation systems, and the reservoir to avoid possible invasion in irrigation system area.",""],[1,"228","10","Irrigation Expansion for Agricultural Water Management","Maximizing the usage of irrigation potential to deal with water problems in the agricultural sector.",""],[1,"228","11","Irrigation Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Management","Strengthening the rehabilitation, construction, maintenance, and irrigation infrastructure management involving: river basins, drainage, canals, flood control systems, polders, and pumping stations to increase irrigation capacity and agricultural productivity.",""],[1,"228","12","Irrigation Management Capacity Building","Improving the management and increasing the effectiveness of irrigation through capacity building.",""],[1,"228","17","Mekong River Basin Cooperation and Agreement Implementation","the Cambodia National Mekong Committee (CNMC) will continue to fully cooperate with other Mekong Member Countries under the Mekong River Commission (MRC) framework to ensure the prosperous and sustainable development of the Mekong River Basin, implement more effectively the Agreement on Cooperation for the Sustainable Development of the Mekong River Basin, and ensure mutually beneficial cooperation towards the optimal and sustainable development of the Mekong River Basin.","Cambodia National Mekong Committee (CNMC)"],[1,"229","2","Basin Development Strategy Implementation","the implementation of the Basin Development Strategy (BDS)",""],[1,"229","2","MRC Product Dissemination and Uptake Improvement","continuing to improve the dissemination, uptake, and use of the MRC products by relevant line agencies and organizations",""],[1,"229","2","Mekong Regional Cooperation Expansion","identifying opportunities for further cooperation with Dialogue Partners, Development Partners and other concrete cooperation mechanisms such as ASEAN, Mekong-Lancang Cooperation, and Greater Mekong Sub-region",""]],"96":[[1,"229","10","Water Infrastructure Construction and Repair Programme","Continuing to build and repair all types of wells, community ponds, rainwater ponds, community water distribution systems, and small scale irrigation systems.",""],[1,"229","11","Water Purifier Container Supply","Continuing to supply water purifier containers.",""],[1,"229","12","Water Quality Laboratory Establishment and Operation","Continuing to establish and run water quality laboratories.",""],[1,"229","13","Rural Water Supply System Inventory","Continuing to organize rural water supply system inventory.",""],[1,"229","14","Water Safety Plan Awareness Raising","Continuing to raise awareness of water safety plans.",""],[1,"229","15","Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Development","Continuing to develop rural water supply and sanitation with funding from national and subnational sources and support from development partners and NGOS.",""],[1,"229","16","National Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Monitoring System","Establishing a national monitoring system for rural water supply and sanitation.",""],[1,"229","17","Village-Level Water Supply Operation and Management Support Programme","Developing programs for supporting water supply operation and management at the village level.",""],[1,"229","18","Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Programmes","Establishing rural water supply and sanitation programs with support from development partners and NGOS.",""],[1,"229","19","National Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Monitoring System","Establishing a national monitoring system for rural water supply and sanitation.",""],[1,"229","20","Sanitation Financing Strategy for Poor and Vulnerable Households","Developing a sanitation financing strategy with a particular focus on poor and vulnerable households.",""],[1,"229","21","Subnational Rural Sanitation Delivery and Capacity-Building Programme","Establishing the role of subnational institutions (commune/Sangkat, district/Khan) in delivering rural sanitation programs according to guidelines and capacity building programs.",""],[1,"229","22","Rural Sanitation Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening national and subnational capacity in promoting rural sanitation.",""],[1,"230","1","Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Monitoring and Evaluation System","Establishing a monitoring and evaluation system for rural water supply and sanitation programs.",""],[1,"230","2","Rural Hygiene Promotion and Behavior Change Initiative","Promoting hygiene practices in rural communities and changing hygienic practice behavior.",""],[1,"230","3","National Strategy on Changing Habits and Communication","Developing a national strategy on changing habits and communication.",""],[1,"230","4","Rural Sanitation Awareness Communication Campaign","Increasing awareness of rural sanitation through communication.",""],[1,"230","5","National Sanitation Financing Strategy","Developing and implementing national strategy on financing for sanitation programs for poor and vulnerable households.",""],[1,"230","6","Village Sanitation Coordination Team Network and Capacity Building","Establishing networks and building capacity for the Village Sanitation Coordination Team.",""],[1,"230","7","Rural School Sanitation and Handwashing Facilities Programme","Building latrines and hand washing facilities at schools in rural areas.",""]],"97":[[1,"71","15","Kampot Provincial Water Supply Capacity Expansion Project","Kampot Provincial Water Supply Capacity Expansion Project (being implemented by Japanese companies, consultants and construction contractors).",""],[1,"72","3","Clean Water Infrastructure Expansion and Training","Continued to train and carry out plans to expand clean water infrastructure to achieve autonomy as an economic enterprise.",""]],"98":[[1,"227","10","Meteorological and Hydrological System Strengthening and Expansion","Strengthening and expanding meteorological and hydrological system including data collecting and broadcasting.",""],[1,"227","11","Drought, Flood and Storm Forecasting and Early Warning System","Conducting regular forecast and alert on droughts, floods and storms for short, medium and long periods of time.",""],[1,"227","12","Meteorological and Hydrological Monitoring Infrastructure Expansion","Improving and installing meteorological and hydrological stations, rain gauges, and water staff gauges at important locations and rivers for data collection and dissemination.",""],[1,"227","13","Hydrological Observation Systems Installation","Installing hydrological observation systems to provide accurate water level and water discharge data for flood forecasting.",""],[1,"227","14","Meteorological Observation System Installation","Installing meteorological observation system to receive accurate weather data for weather forecasting.",""],[1,"227","15","Public Weather Risk Information and Preparedness Education","Informing the public of weather forecast information as well as education to prepare themselves for weather risks and climate change adaptation, including storms, lightning, tsunamis, and flood.",""],[1,"227","16","Irrigation and Water Resources Mapping Inventory","Preparing inventory for and geographical maps of irrigation systems, flood control systems, polders, river basins, inundated land and water resources management based on sufficient data.",""],[1,"227","18","Hydrological Station Establishment","Set up hydrological stations",""],[1,"228","1","Meteorology Station Establishment","Set up meteorology stations",""],[1,"229","2","Mekong Basin Flood and Drought Monitoring and Forecasting Systems","strengthening the MRC basin-wide monitoring networks and forecasting systems for floods and droughts, as well as data and information management systems",""]],"99":[[1,"139","7","Armed Forces Reform and Capability Enhancement","Continuing to reform the armed forces with the following measures: 1) strengthening of oversight, management and networking; 2) improving human resource development and enhancing armed forces' capabilities through better skills training, more utilization of technology and building up of a next generation of fighting forces; 3) reinforcing the capacity to maintain security, encouraging armed forces personnel and their families to resettle in areas along the borders, combatting and removing terrorism threat so as to ensure peace, national safety and development; 4) strengthening international cooperation, especially within the UN peacekeeping framework; and 5) creating a supportive environment for infrastructure development, environmental and natural resource protection, and building better capacity for interventions during national disasters, humanitarian operations and support during crop harvesting seasons.",""],[1,"141","24","Armed Forces Continuation and Strengthening","the Ministry of National Defense will continue implementing all kinds of armed forces to ensure the effective protection of sovereignty, territorial integrity, security, security and public order.","Ministry of National Defense"],[1,"141","25","Armed Forces Professionalization and Security Police Strategic Plan Implementation","Promoting the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces' professional ability through the continued implementation of Stratety 3, and 10 Operation Activities and Development as well as the updating and promoting of the implementation of the Security Police Strategic Plan in order to promote the effectiveness of the armed forces especially strengthening the enforcement of laws and regulations.",""],[1,"142","1","Armed Forces Modernization and Training Capacity Development","Developing human resources and increase the capacity of the armed forces through modernization of equiments to improve the quality of training, especially the training of professional soldiers.",""],[1,"142","2","Armed Forces Management Strengthening","Strengthening the assignment in the armed forces, especially the army, at all levels to ensure effective management.",""],[1,"142","3","Army Technical Equipment and Welfare Support","Providing technical equipment and promoting welfare of the army, especially the efficiency of financial logistics management for units stationed at the front line and island defense forces.",""],[1,"142","4","Veterans and Families Support Programme","Continuing to pay attention to veterans and crippled soldiers, families of the dead soldiers and families of the army and development projects for the community of families along the border and the rural areas.",""],[1,"142","6","International Cooperation for Armed Forces Development","Strengthening and expanding the international cooperation relations for the development of armed forces in all areas, including the continued participation in the UN peacekeeping mission.",""],[1,"142","7","RCAF Human Resources Development for Agricultural and Processing Skills","Developing human resources in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) on the professional skills of the agricultural sector, processing production and other skills that can create a personal career that allows for the unit and the military community to earn a living and to promote welfare in the military community.",""],[1,"142","8","Expansion of Women's Military Units in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces","Promoting gender equality in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces by encouraging the growth of women's military units within the leadership of the unit.",""],[1,"142","9","Investment Partnership Development Strategy for Military Community Land","Establishing investment partnership development strategies on agriculture, industry and resource processing, especially the land of the military community to maximize the use and potential of RCAF resources to improve the livelihoods of the army through job creation and employment for the military community.",""],[1,"142","10","Green Energy Projects for Community-Based Energy Sector","Implementing the green energy projects, especially the community-based energy sector, to facilitate development work, which is the RGC's policy.",""]],"100":[[1,"79","18","Tourism Service Quality Evaluation and Promotion System for the Chinese Market","Tourism service quality evaluation system for the Chinese market, promotion, education, awareness raising and cooperation.",""],[1,"80","7","Community Tour Guide Uniform and Korean Translator Support","Managed community tour guide uniform and Korean translators continuing from the Korean language guides.",""],[1,"80","10","Clean Restaurant Campaign Implementation Guidance","Guidance on the implementation of the campaign \"Clean Restaurant: Non-Paper Trash Restaurant\".",""],[1,"200","7","Tourism Development Strategy and Priority Actions","preparing development strategies and priority actions on tourism development",""],[1,"200","7","Tourism Product Diversification Initiative","diversifying new tourism products in addition to Angkor area",""],[1,"200","7","Tourism Investment Promotion","promoting attraction and investment in tourism",""],[1,"200","7","Licensed Tourism Investment Company Review and Promotion","reviewing, evaluating and promoting investment companies licensed by the RGC",""],[1,"200","7","Sacred Tourist Site Development","promoting the establishment of sacred tourist sites",""],[1,"200","8","Tourism Market Research and Promotion Expansion","Studying tourism market and promotion: (1) enhancing the promotion of \"Cambodia, Kingdom of Wonders\", (2) promoting market study and expanding tourism promotion to other priority market targets; (3) encouraging and expanding overseas tourism promotion through the Cambodia Board of Marketing and Tourism Promotion, and (4) promoting market research and developing tourism statistics.",""],[1,"200","9","Tourism Product and Service Quality Improvement Programme","Strengthening and improving the quality of tourism products and services: (1) strengthening the quality of tourism products and services; (2) strengthening the quality and effectiveness of public service delivery through the creation and promotion of public service standards; (3) implementing the national tourism standard; (4) encouraging the competition movement of \"Clean City, Clean Resort, Good Service and Good Hospitality\" \"Clean Cambodia\"; and (5) strengthening the tourism industry quality with a \"One Service, One Standard\".",""],[1,"200","10","Tourism Sector Skills Development and Internship Programme","Strengthening the quality of education, training and human resource development in the tourism sector: (1) training and building tourism professional skills and (2) sending officials to internships for experiences and study abroad.",""],[1,"200","11","Tourism Travel and Transport Coordination","Coordinating the tourism travel and transport: (1) promoting the development of relevant infrastructures of relevant ministries and agencies; (2) encouraging and facilitating tourism travel; and (3) collaborating with relevant ministries and agencies in reducing unnecessary barriers and jobs through gateways and international border gates.",""],[1,"200","12","Private Sector and Public-Private Partnership Strengthening","Strengthening the private sector and the public private partnership: (1) promoting international, multilateral, trilateral, and bilateral cooperation in the sub-regional and global context; (2) promoting active participation from the private sector; and (3) promoting partnership between the public private partnership.",""],[1,"200","13","Tourism Human Resource Capacity Development","developing the capacity to improve the management and development of human resources, in particular the ability to manage and assign tasks according to organization's needs",""],[1,"200","13","Tourism Workforce Skills Improvement Initiative","strengthening the human resource quality in the tourism industry with the concept \"One Staff, One Skill\"",""],[1,"200","13","Decentralization to Sub-national Administrative Authorities","promoting the decentralization to SNAs in accordance with the National Program for Sub-national Democratic Development",""],[1,"201","1","Tourist Safety and Security Strengthening Measures","Strengthening the safety and security of tourists: (1) promoting the roles of women, child safety, and disabled persons; (2) preventing the spread of HIV/AIDS in tourism; and (3) combating drugs in tourism.",""],[1,"201","3","Cultural and Natural Heritage Tourism Site Conservation and Development","Conserving, protecting, improving and sustainably developing the appropriate places that are rich in culture, history and natural resources, which are the tourism destinations of the potential nation.",""],[1,"202","15","Cultural Heritage Tourism Attraction Development","Turning cultural heritage sites into targeted attractions for filming, performance and investment in tourism.",""]],"102":[[1,"154","8","National Single Window Completion and Trade Facilitation Reform","Further trade facilitation by completing the preparation of the National Single Window, minimizing cross-border control mechanism and cutting unnecessary procedures that hinder trade.",""],[1,"155","9","Yeal Khov Trademark Development","Developing Yeal Khov trademark.",""],[1,"156","2","Export Certificate of Origin Decentralization","Strengthening of decentralization of the issuance of Certificate of Origin Form D to Departments of Commerce in the provinces along the border",""],[1,"156","2","ASEAN Self-Certification Invoice-Based Origin Verification","strengthening and expanding the implementation of using invoice for the self- certification of origin in ASEAN",""],[1,"156","2","Certificate of Origin Automation System Upgrade","strengthen the maintaining, upgrading certification of origin automation system, and linking C/O Form D in the national single system of Cambodia and organizing additional C/O forms according to the rules of origin of importing countries",""],[1,"156","2","Exporter Training and EU Registration Information Campaign","organize the training and publishing the information of registration for exporters to the European Union",""],[1,"160","3","Export Market Diversification through Permanent Free Trade Agreements","moving forward, Cambodia not only strives to maintain its existing export markets, but open new markets to expand the export base by relying on permanent FTAs (rather than bilateral favorable treatment which can be lost easily)",""],[1,"160","5","Trade Integration and Connectivity Enhancement","Continuing to fulfil remaining obligations under WTO, ASEAN Economic Community and bilateral frameworks especially physical and soft infrastructure connectivity, and improvement in regulatory framework as well as institutional and human capacity to fully capitalize on integration and enhance trade and investment flows in the region and the world.",""],[1,"160","6","Bilateral and Multilateral Free Trade Agreement Promotion","Promoting the establishment of bilateral free trade areas with major partner countries and the establishment of multilateral free trade areas with major regions such as Eurasia, European Union, as well as Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) and other free trade agreements.",""],[1,"160","7","Business Networking and Export Diversification Forums","Further strengthening business networking by organizing forums, business visits or trade fairs aimed at promoting business partnership and clear understanding of market demand as well as export market diversification.",""],[1,"161","2","Trade Sector Development and Market Diversification Initiative","Promote the trade sector development through market diversification and facilitation in trade negotiations in order to accelerate integration into the key free trade frameworks in the region and the world",""],[1,"161","2","Trade Barrier Research and Export Facilitation Study","do research on trade barriers that affect the export of products of the country in mission",""],[1,"161","2","Expansion of Trade Agreements","strengthen and expand trade agreements in Asia Pacific, Europe, Middle-East and Africa, the United States and other countries",""],[1,"161","3","Trade Fair Promotion and Participation Programme","Continue to conduct trade fair for Cambodian products at the campaigns to buy Cambodian products in the cities and provinces, (2) continue to participate in world and international trade fair",""],[1,"161","3","Private Sector Trade Partnership Promotion","promote trade partnership between private sector and private sector in the country and international countries on commodity exchanges, business perspectives and other development projects that can lead to supply in domestic market instead of import overload",""],[1,"161","3","Company Exhibition Organization Support","encourage the company to organize its exhibitions properly",""],[1,"161","4","Business and Market Consulting Support","Provide business and market consulting to business people",""],[1,"161","4","Product Exhibition, Promotion, and Branding Initiative","exhibition, Promotion, Consulting and Promote of Cambodian products Branding",""],[1,"161","4","Cambodia Business Center and Overseas Chamber Office Expansion","strengthen and create more Cambodia business centers and representative office of chamber of commerce in abroad",""],[1,"161","4","Export Market Expansion and Trade Facilitation Measures","take measures to strengthen and expand Cambodia's export markets, in particular through open market negotiations with countries in the region and outside the region, promoting transportation infrastructure and logistic system including information technology and communication system to facilitate flow of goods and services, including financial services, as well as reducing non-tariff barriers such as improving the sanitary and phytosanitary",""],[1,"161","5","Trade Sector Integration Roadmap","Develop a roadmap for clear process of trade sector integration.",""],[1,"161","6","Trade Information Center Development and Expansion","Develop Trade Information Center: 1) Continue to update trade information need assessment, 2) strengthen and expand the production of trade information in accordance with the social context, 3) strengthen and expand the dissemination of trade information, 4) Monitor and evaluate the process of Trade Information Center.",""],[1,"161","7","Legal Framework Development for Business and Investment Environment","Continue to develop legal frameworks to improve the business and investment environment.",""],[1,"162","5","Free Trade Zone and Free Trade Agreement Implementation Activities","the Council of the Development of Cambodia (CDC) will implement the following activities:","Council of the Development of Cambodia (CDC)"],[1,"162","6","Active Participation in Free Trade Agreement Negotiations","Continuing to more actively participate in agreement negotiation or investment chapters in the free trade agreement framework such as RCEP and other free trade agreements to enhance the Cambodia's integration into the regional and the world economy.",""],[1,"163","5","Economic and Cultural Diplomacy Implementation","Implementation of economy and culture diplomacy to strengthen the national economy",""],[1,"163","7","Economic, Cultural, and Tourism Diplomacy Activities","Continuing to implement the economic, cultural, and tourism diplomatic activities in order to promote export policies, strengthen and promote national culture, and attract foreign tourists.",""]],"103":[[1,"202","27","Cambodia Product Branding and Export Promotion Initiative","Study and establish a branding of potential products of Cambodia to enhance its reputation and expand exports to international markets",""],[1,"202","27","Permanent Product Centers and Trade Promotion Centers","continue to set up and manage Cambodia's permanent product centers and the international and domestic trade promotion centers",""],[1,"202","27","International and Domestic Trade Cooperation for Cambodian Products","cooperate with trade partners and overseas trade centers to promote Cambodian products into regional and global markets",""],[1,"202","28","Export Promotion Policy Development","Prepare export promotion policies",""],[1,"202","28","Trade Policy Monitoring and Evaluation System","develop a system of monitoring and evaluation of trade policy and strengthen the effectiveness of implementation of trade policy",""],[1,"202","28","International Trade Expansion","strengthen and expand international",""],[1,"203","1","Trade Research, Monitoring, and Analysis Programme","continue to do research, monitor and analyze the trend of economic and trade, trade barriers and trade strategies of implemented countries",""],[1,"203","1","Trade Facilitation Improvement in Export Operations","improve trade facilitation in all export operations",""],[1,"203","1","Expansion of Bilateral and Multilateral Trade Agreements","strengthening and expanding trade agreements in bilateral and multilateral frameworks",""],[1,"216","7","Special Economic Zones and Border Market Development","Continuing to encourage and promote the development of SEZs, export processing areas, free trade zones and border market development with the participation of the private sector.",""],[1,"216","15","Private Sector Institutional Strengthening and Export Promotion","Strengthening and expanding the development of private institutions through the establishment of business associations and chambers of commerce, (2) evaluating the needs of trade facilitation among business-related institutions, (3) carrying out dialogue and discussion, and regularly deal with challenges faced by businesses with relevant institutions, (4) promoting export and",""],[1,"217","1","Fuel Retail Price Monitoring and Price Index Adjustment","continuing to monitor fuel retail prices at in domestic and international markets and adjust the price index",""],[1,"217","1","Value Addition Study for Potential Products","studying value addition of potential products",""],[1,"217","1","Government and Private Sector Training Expansion and Research Programme","expanding training activities to relevant government officials and private sector staffs and establishing a research program supported by development fund agencies",""],[1,"217","2","Trade Facilitation Strengthening and Expansion","Strengthening and Expanding Trade Facilitation: (1) Continuing to develop administrative procedures and strengthening trade facilitation, (2) strengthening collaboration between state institutions and the private sector in trade, and (3) monitoring and evaluating the trade facilitation.",""],[1,"221","8","International Agricultural Trade Cooperation and Market Expansion","Strengtheing international cooperation with neighboring countries and developing partner countries in bilateral and multilateral frameworks, and regional and international cooperation and enhance the cooperation and negotiation leading to an extended market for Cambodian agricultural products in other countries in the context of globalization.",""]],"104":[[1,"238","17","Affordable Housing Programme Implementation","strengthening the implementation of an affordable housing program",""],[1,"240","2","Social Land Concession Program","Continuing social land concession programs to distribute lands to 500 poor and landless families per year",""],[1,"240","2","Border Forces Housing and Land Allocation Program","continuing to distribute 500 land plots and/or houses per year to the armed forces standing at the borders",""],[1,"240","3","Formal Village Planning for Social Land Concessions","Formulating a formal village for social land concessions prepared and integrated into commune Sangkat development plans and investment programs.",""],[1,"240","4","Settlement of Disordered Buildings in Municipal and Urban Areas","Encouraging the settlement of disordered buildings in muncipalities and urban areas in the form of on-site development or resettlement in accordance with Directive No: 03 on the settlement of temporary buildings on state land which are illegally occupied in the capital, municipalities, and urban areas.",""],[1,"240","5","Affordable Housing Construction Program","Promoting the construction of housing units for rent and sale to low and medium- income and vulnerable people in accordance with National Program for Development of Affordable Housing.",""],[1,"240","6","Incentives Policy and National Program for Affordable Housing Development","Incentives Policy and National Program for Affordable Housing Development.",""]],"105":[[1,"56","12","Regulatory Implementation Support through Circulars and Technical Guidelines","Organized and implemented the circular, directive, decision, memorandum of understanding, technical guidelines to support the implementation of existing sub- decrees and regulations.",""],[1,"58","7","National Agenda for Research on Science and Technology","National Agenda for Research on Science and Technology: policy, regulation, guidelines and agreements on science and technology",""]],"106":[[1,"215","9","Public Investment Management Program","The strategic goal of the RGC is to establish and fully implementation a public investment management program through a comprehensive and integrated public-private partnership mechanism in accordance with the international best practices.",""],[1,"215","13","Public-Private Partnership Mechanism for Managing Public Investment","Continueing to carrying out the works under the \"Policy paper on the development of public-private partnership mechanism for managing public investment",""],[1,"216","1","Public-Private Partnership Public Investment Policy","formulating a long term \"policy to implement public investment projects under public-private partnership\"",""],[1,"216","2","Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","Developing further the legal and regulatory framework with the introduction of a joint operation management procedure and assessing the possibility to launch the necessary supporting financial arrangements in line with Cambodia's economic development context.",""],[1,"216","3","PPP Project Management Capacity Building","Reinforcing institutional and human resource capacity at relevant ministries/institutions on the management and implementation of projects under the public-private partnership mechanism.",""],[1,"216","4","Public-Private Partnership Public Investment Expansion","Expanding the portfolio of public investment projects through the public-private partnership mechanism in order to attract additional private funding to advance the development of infrastructure and increase quality public service delivery",""],[1,"216","6","Public Investment Framework and Public-Private Partnership Development","Developing a public investment framework and public private partnership.",""],[1,"216","8","Private Sector Government Forum Mechanism","Continuing to implement and operate the Private Sector Government Forum mechanism to further address the concerns of the private sector and to further strengthen the private sector with greater ownership and independency.",""],[1,"216","10","Public-Private Partnership Mechanism for Public Investment Management","Continuing to implement the \"Policy Paper on the Development of Public Private Partnership Mechanism for Public Investment Management 2016-2020\".",""],[1,"216","11","Investment Promotion for Large Infrastructure Projects","Continuing to promote and attract local and foreign investors to invest in large infrastructure projects such as transport, roads, bridges, energy and communications and information, to support the reduction of funding from the national budget and public debt.",""],[1,"216","12","Public Investment Project Implementation Policy Review and Regulatory Framework Development","Continuing to review and provide inputs on the design of \"public investment project implementation policies under the public private partnership mechanism\" and continuing to formulate relevant regulation framework and povisions.",""],[1,"216","13","Priority Project Review and Approval under Public-Private Partnership Mechanism","Continuing to participate in reviewing and approving the list of priority projects and the feasibility study results of the priority projects, including those that will be piloted under the public private partnership mechanism.",""],[1,"250","7","Public-Private Partnership Expansion for Infrastructure Investment","the RGC will continue to expand the scope and use of Public Private Partnership (PPP) arrangements to deliver investment needs, again with a focus on key infrastructure needs.",""]],"107":[[1,"39","8","Public Debt Management Strategy","Public debt is properly managed and consistently adhered to the four key areas (1) having the appropriate loan size that the budget and the economy can handle; (2) having a loan with a high concession or favorable conditions; (3) haing a loan for the priority sectors only, focused on sustainability, growth and sector, increasing economic productivity; and (4) using credit in a transparent, accountable, efficient and highly effective manner.",""],[1,"40","8","Program Budget Expansion to Ministries and Provincial Administrations","The full pilot program budget is implemented and expanded to all ministries, with 10 ministries implementing the program budget in 2015, 15 additional ministries in 2016 and 11 additional ministries for 2017 and three more ministries in 2018.",""],[1,"40","11","Full Program Budget Implementation","Through implementation of full program budget at all ministries and institutions from 2018, it will support ministries and agencies to make more budget-related policies.",""]],"108":[[1,"238","14","Land Reform and Land Use Planning Enhancement","Continuing to enhance land reform and accelerate the development of a master plan and a land use plan for land management, urban planning and construction, at both national and sub-national levels, aiming to manage and use land more efficiently.",""],[1,"238","15","Urbanization and Land Use Planning Strengthening","Strengthening the competency to manage urbanization, land use plan for the capital, developing land use plans for municipalities, district-khan, commune-sangkat nationwide; preparing strategic directions for land zoning; and residential management by using technology.",""],[1,"238","16","Urban Infrastructure Master Plan for Main Cities","Formulating an infrastructure master plan for main cities and urban area to support the development of roads, railways and waterways as well as electricity networks, and clean water networks, especially sewage and water treatment systems.",""],[1,"238","17","Urban Construction Regulation and Smart City Standards Enforcement","by enhancing the development and enforcement of laws, regulations, technology and construction standards that ensure quality, safety, beauty, efficiency and smart city principles",""],[1,"238","18","Urban Waste and Sanitation Management","Further enhancing the beauty and services in cities and major urban areas through managing waste and sanitation; preparing pedestrian sidewalks, parking spaces, public parks; constructing rivers' edges and dam; improving public order and lighting",""],[1,"239","15","Land Use Master Plans for Municipalities and Urban Areas","Land use master plans for 22 municialities and urban areas.",""],[1,"239","16","Land Use Master Plan for 38 Districts/Khans","Land use master plan for 38 districts/Khans.",""],[1,"239","18","Administrative and Land Use Mapping for Municipalities and Districts","Promoting and approving the administrative boundary maps, infrastructure maps, and current land use maps for all 197 municipalities, districts/Khans, and capital and provincies by 2019.",""],[1,"239","19","Cambodia Coastal Areas Physical Planning","Developing and approving the Cambodia's Coastal Areas Physical Plans: (1) land use master plan for 7 islands of the Cambodian coastal areas, (2) land use master plan for Koh Rong Town, (3) land use master plan and detailed plan of the beaches, seas, rivers, streams, lakes, and waterways connecting the sea and the water surface close to the beaches.",""],[1,"239","20","Land Boundary Construction and Demarcation for Coastal and Waterway Areas","Constructing and demarcating the land boundary of beaches, seas, rivers, streams, lakes, and waterways connecting the sea of the Cambodian coastal areas.",""],[1,"239","21","Geodetic Benchmark and Aerial Mapping Programme for Coastal Islands","Putting the geodetic benchmarks and producing aerial photo maps on the islands of the Cambodian coastal areas.",""],[1,"240","13","Municipality and Urban Area Development Strategy","Formulating policies and strategies: National Policy on Public Private Partnership on Land and National Strategy on Municipality and Urban Area Development.",""]],"109":[[1,"139","5","Merit-Based Civil Service Recruitment and Performance Incentives","Promoting meritocracy in the recruitment, appointment and promotion process along with the provision of incentives and other benefits to civil servants and public institutions, especially the implementation of performance-based system in the public sector.",""],[1,"140","4","Government Staffing Plan Alignment System","Developing a system of government staffing plans to be consistent with the budget plan.",""],[1,"140","7","Quality Management System with Incentive Mechanism","Preparing and implementing the Quality Management System with an incentive mechanism.",""],[1,"141","2","Civil Service Capacity and Professional Ethics Improvement","Improving to strenthen the capacity and professional ethics of civil servants in the front and back office.",""],[1,"141","7","Civil Service Management and Recruitment Strengthening","Strengthening the management and recruitment of civil servants through the arrangement of civil servants, positions descriptions in civil dervice.",""],[1,"141","9","Performance Management System Implementation","Implementing the performance management system in ministries and insitutions at the national and sub-national levels.",""]],"111":[[1,"142","12","Anti-Corruption Education and Awareness Campaign","The RGC will focus on (1) Strengthening educational awareness on the prevention, obstruction, and crackdown on corruption activities in line with the National Anti-Corruption Strategy and its Action Plan under the slogan of \"Not Daring, Unable and Unwilling\" to commit corruption",""],[1,"142","12","Public Sector Inspection and Audit Strengthening","The RGC will focus on (5) Strengthening the effectiveness of public sector inspection and audit mechanism",""],[1,"142","12","Public Sector Work Ethics and Conflict of Interest Reform","The RGC will focus on (6) Improving the effectiveness of the preparation and implementation of work ethics, including the respect of the principles of functional incompatibility and conflict of interest for public officials",""],[1,"143","2","Anti-Corruption Core Measures Strengthening","the ACU will strengthen and enhance the effectiveness of the following three core measures:",""],[1,"143","3","Anti-Corruption Education and Awareness Expansion","To continue strengthening and expanding the scope of disseminating laws, and education to fight corruption in and out of school in all aspects of all sectors and at all levels and to continue expanding to higher education institutions to promote awareness of fighting corruption and a sense of integrity in work and livelihood.",""],[1,"143","3","Competitive Knowledge Forum on Anti-Corruption","Promoting anti-corruption engagement will continue to be promoted through the establishment of a Competitive Knowledge Forum on Anti-Corruption.",""],[1,"143","4","Anti-Corruption Plans and Joint Cooperation Initiatives","Continue to promote, develop and implement anti-corruption plans in public institutions and anti-corruption programs in the private sector and create new joint initiatives on anti-corruption cooperation.",""],[1,"143","4","Observer-Based Civil Service Recruitment Oversight","Continue to prevent negative phenomena as well as regulatory violations through the participation of observers in the examinations of the recruitment of the civil servants, students, and the key roles of the ministries.",""],[1,"143","4","Asset and Debt Declaration System Expansion","Asset and debt declaration is a preventive measure to curb corruption and support an effective investigation that will continue to increase efficiency in delivering services in the form of assets and liabilities, especially to newly-appointed individuals who are finishing their mandate or retire and expand the scope of the declaration of assets and liabilities to the target to be announced in accordance with the Law on Anti-Corruption.",""],[1,"143","5","Crime Suppression and Complaint Monitoring Mechanism","Suppression of crimes by referring all cases to court: To continue strengthening the mechanism of monitoring and analyzing complaints and continuing to take strict actions against corrupt perpetrators without exception, as well as continuing to strengthen their staff capacity through training both internally and externally on investigating allegations of money laundering, spy investigation, search for the seizure of corruption offenses.",""],[1,"143","6","Anti-Money Laundering Institutional Coordination Offices","Continue to work closely with relevant institutions, both locally and internationally, through the creation of the Interstate Office and Anti-Money Laundering Office in the Anti-Corruption Unit.",""],[1,"143","9","Anti-Corruption Education Expansion in Higher and Vocational Institutions","Expanding the scope of education on anti- corruption in higher education institutions and vocational training institutions.",""],[1,"143","10","Anti-Corruption Lesson for Higher Education and Vocational Training","There is a lesson on anti-corruption for higher education institutions and vocational training",""],[1,"144","3","UNCAC Implementation Process Continuation","Promoting the continued implementation of the UNCAC implementation process in Cambodia",""],[1,"144","7","Anti-Corruption Office Establishment","Establishing an anti-corruption office in the capital and provinces",""],[1,"144","20","Complaint Monitoring Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening the mechanisms to monitor complaints",""],[1,"144","22","Interagency Asset Pursuit and Confiscation Collaboration","Strengthening the collaboration with relevant ministries, national and international institutions on the pursuit and confiscation of results of offense.",""],[1,"144","23","Interagency Collaboration on Pursuit and Confiscation of Crime Proceeds","Collaborate with relevant national ministries, national and international institutions on the pursuit and confiscation of the results offenses.",""],[1,"145","3","Administrative Inspection and Anti-Corruption Oversight","For this important task, the ministry continues to set (1) inspection on administration, finance and property management at ministries and agencies at national and sub-national levels; (2) monitoring the enforcement of laws on agriculture, forestry and fishery; public works and transport; land management, urban planning and construction; social affairs, veterans and youth rehabilitation; and tourism and telecommunications; (3) the work of receiving complaints and investigations continues to receive complaints from citizens from all backgrounds and to investigate, resolve the complaints under the Ministry's mandate; (4) inspection with the ministries and agencies, increasing the communication with inspection units within the ministries and agencies at national and international level; and (5) conflict work, continuing to investigate the extent of misconduct of individuals, ministries, public institutions, public enterprises and stakeholders.","the Ministry"]],"113":[[1,"205","4","Digital Government Policy Development","Developing the policy on digital government.",""],[1,"205","5","National Information Network Infrastructure for Cloud Technology","Developing the national information network infrastructure for cloud technology.",""],[1,"205","6","Micro Data Center for High-Speed Internet Projects","Establishing a micro data center for running high-speed internet projects to homes, information centers, and e-learning.",""],[1,"205","7","Management Software System and Common National Website","Creating new management software system and creating a common national website.",""],[1,"205","8","Digital Government Infrastructure Expansion","Expanding server capability, website, e-mail server, and setting up a digital signature certification mechanism for ministries and agencies, capital/provinces, and the national and sub-national authorities.",""],[1,"205","9","Business Licensing and Digital Permit Registration Mechanism","Setting up a licensing mechanism, digital signature for businesses, and registering permits for businesses in ICT.",""]],"114":[[1,"217","6","Anti-Trust and Competition Law Reform","Drafting and enacting the Anti-Trust/Competition Law; establishing a legal framework for strengthening industry structures and promoting a culture of competition.",""],[1,"217","7","Insolvency Law Review and Amendment","Reviewing and amending the Insolvency Law to encourage risk taking and protect entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"217","8","Promotion of Commercial Arbitration","Promoting the use of commercial arbitration as a capable and credible alternative dispute resolutions mechanism.",""],[1,"217","9","Product, Service, and Management Standards Upgrading Initiative","Stimulating the establishment of products, services and management standards and upgrading those standards to enhance quality and the adoption of new technology.",""],[1,"217","10","Consumer Protection Law and Implementation Mechanism","Drafting and enacting Consumer Protection Law including its implementation mechanism to promote health and protect the rights and safety of consumers, enhance product and service standards and propping up more competition.",""],[1,"217","11","Customs and Tax Compliance Strengthening","Enhancing fair level playing field, particularly through stricter custom and tax compliance and transparent and proper public procurement procedure.",""],[1,"217","13","National Competition and Consumer Protection Measures","Strengthening the process of preventing any fraudulent attempts of products' quality and safety of all means, at the markets nationwide, (2) continuing to promote the effectiveness of managing and monitoring activities to provide accurate information to users such as product labels, product usage, product promotions, which is especially deceptive or misleading for the consumers, (3) continuing to monitor the standards of food safety by adopting the national standard and related codec standard, and (4) promoting the Competition Law including document compilation, training, and dissemination of the law.",""],[1,"218","1","Trade Dispute Resolution Cooperation and Commercial Court Process Support","Continuing to cooperate with the National Arbitration Center for Trade and conducting research on relevant law enforcement documents of the Ministry of Justice in order to promote the commercial court process.","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"218","6","Strengthening Meteorology and Standards Institutional Framework","Continuing to strengthen the institutional framework and the capacity to manage the meteorolgy and standards that are the foundation for industrial activities",""],[1,"218","6","Legal Recognition of National Meteorology and Standards Institutions","efforts to establish the legal framework and international recognition of key national institutions such as the National Center for Meterology and the Cambodia Institute of Standards",""],[1,"218","8","Standards and Meteorology Capacity Strengthening","Supporting and enhancing the competence and authority of standards and meteorology in assuring quantity, quality, safety, environmental services and management.",""]],"115":[[1,"126","15","Public Revenue Mobilization","Increase public revenue to sustain more than 20% of GDP and was supported by new sources",""],[1,"126","15","Fiscal and Monetary Stability Policy","Maintain a vigilant fiscal and monetary stance, deficit below 5% of GDP, a stable price level and balance of payment",""],[1,"127","3","Public Financial Management Reform Program","Public financial management reform program 2004-2025 is a huge reform program of RGC to build a financial system complying to the international standard of management of the mobilized resources and transform budget system to be performance information budget system.",""],[1,"127","5","Revenue Mobilization Strategy 2019-2023","Revenue Mobilization Strategy 2019-2023 will transform public revenue system to be modern to push for national revenue collection in response to the need for development with the fair principles in revenue collection, equity between taxpayers, and revenue management through modernizing the revenue collection administration.",""],[1,"127","6","Revenue Collection Effectiveness and Expansion","Continue to guarantee effectiveness of revenue collection and specify total current revenue collection objectives to increase at least 0.3 percentage point of GDP.",""],[1,"127","7","Tax Revenue System Modernization","Modernize tax revenue system through formulating policy by reviewing on current fiscal policy on principle of simplicity, transparency, accuracy, equity, and effectiveness.",""],[1,"127","8","Fiscal Policy Procedure Strengthening Reform","Strengthen main fiscal policy procedures including: (1) Revising the special tax and levies base on vehicles, tabaco, beers, wine and high sugar content beverage, (2) Examining tariff and special tax on luxurious products, (3) Strengthening revenue collection on real estate through updating real estate prices and enlarging the extension of tax collection on real estate, (4) Adjusting the public lighting tax to facilitate taxpaying and increase revenue effectiveness, ( 5) Thorough preparation to implement personal income tax, (6) Strengthening tax collection on casino businesses.",""],[1,"128","1","Tax Administration Modernization and Capacity Enhancement","Modernizing the tax administration through building and enhancing capacity of tax administration to adjust accordingly to the changing atmosphere of business and taxpayer attitudes to ensure the achievement of policy objectives of RGC with effectiveness and efficiency.",""],[1,"128","2","Tax Administration Modernization Programme","Modernizing tax administration which contributes to enhancing voluntary taxpaying compliance including (1) Formulating a plan to strengthen ownership of core operating function of department and provincial/khan branches, (2) Formulating and utilizing electronic data and information sharing system in every departments of General Department of Taxation, (3) Formulating plan to enhance a thorough compliance which includes national level strategy on strengthening quality service providing to the taxpayers and on strengthening credibility of auditing, (4) Implementing audits based on risks and make a decision on taxpayer risk level, (5) Enhancing characteristics, professionalism and capacity of tax officials through training and performance management system, (6) Completing the formulation of the master plan to invest on technological infrastructure.",""],[1,"128","3","Customs Administration Modernization Programme","Modernizing customs administration including (1) Enhancing ASYCUDA (2) Strengthening Pos-Clearance Audit, prevention and suppression on customs offenses (3) Strengthening compliance on all special tax goods, especially high revenue generating items, (4) Strengthening cooperation with relevant institutions to strengthen data sharing mechanisms and cooperation in the fight against tax evasion and smuggling.",""],[1,"128","4","Non-Tax Revenue Administration Modernization","Modernization of information technology system for non-tax revenue management to promote non-tax revenue collection with transparency, accuracy, timeliness and facilitation on taxpaying",""],[1,"128","4","Development of New Non-Tax Revenue Sources","Strengthening of potential new sources of revenue.",""],[1,"128","5","Budget System Reform Strategy 2018-2025","The Budget System Reform Strategy 2018-2025 aims to strengthen the budget discipline from planning and budgeting and implementation by linking the budget to the priority policy and the main rationalization (based on achievement information) to achieve key national policies.",""],[1,"128","6","Expenditure Prioritization and Rationalization Policy","Continuing to prioritize and rationalize expenditure policy in education, vocational training, health, agriculture, entrepreneurship and digital economy.",""],[1,"128","9","Public Expenditure Management Strengthening","Strengthening public expenditure management and promote continuous budget implementation through (1) Enhancing cash management (2) Strengthening the formulation of quarterly revenue and expenditure programs (3) Monitoring of quarterly and semester budget execution (4) Strengthening internal controls to further enhance the reliability of the budget achieved (5) Optimization of financial accountability.",""],[1,"129","2","Financial Decentralization Framework Development","Continuing to formulate policy and short-term and long-term financial decentralization frameworks to further contribute to the implementation of the Law on Capital/ Provincial, Municipal and District, especially the national program for Sub-National Democratic Development.",""],[1,"134","11","Tax Policy Development and Tax Administration Modernization","Develop tax policy, promote growth through improvements in tax services and tax administration modernization",""],[1,"134","14","Medium-Term Public Financial Framework and Budget Framework Introduction","Cambodia will introduce the medium-term public financial framework and medium-term budget framework by 2021.",""],[1,"135","1","Increased Social Services and General Administration Spending","In this sense, national spending on social services and general administration will grow at a fast and parallel phase, higher than GDP growth which makes its ratio to GDP incrementally increase.",""],[1,"154","3","Macroeconomic Policy Coordination and Structural Reform","Further implementing macroeconomic policy by combining public finance policy, monetary policy and structural reform in a proactive but vigilant manner to ensure growth stability, low inflation, exchange rate stability and investment promotion.",""],[1,"154","4","Economic Crisis and Risk Preparedness Mechanism","Preparing mechanism to deal with economic crises and risks which could occur in the financial sector, banking and non-banking sector as well as real estate and other sectors.",""],[1,"154","6","Tax System Reform and New Tax Law Formulation","Promoting comprehensive and in-depth reform of the taxation system, including the formulation of the new tax law based on the principle of enhancing the effectiveness of revenue collection, ensuring transparent, accountable, equal and fair competition environment, encouraging economic, business and investment activities as well as ensuring social equity.",""],[1,"154","10","Macroeconomic Stability and Credit Risk Management Measures","Continuing to ensure macroeconomic stability through (1) strengthening risk management mechanisms and financial crisis; (2) managing credit growth in the real estate sector to an appropriate level and increasing the quality of credit by focusing on production and trade.",""],[1,"154","10","Private Sector Capital Mobilization and SME Development","continuing to seek new sources of capital for the private sector such as the development of market and currency market and the establishment of SMEs",""],[1,"154","10","Affordable Housing Promotion and Real Estate Sector Management","continuing to focus on managing the real estate sector and strive to promote affordable housing in line with the RGC's policies",""],[1,"154","10","Microfinance Awareness Campaign","raising awareness of the general population, especially those in the rural areas, with loans from microfinance institutions.",""],[1,"155","1","Real Estate and Valuation Regulatory Framework Development","Preparing four regulatory documents: (1) drafting the Law on Management of Valuation Services and Real Estate Services; (2) developing the Law on Mortgage Business Management; (3) developing the Law on Real Estate Development Business Management; (4) drafting a Prakas on the Management of Consumer Goods Business and developing the real estate valation standard.",""],[1,"155","2","Insurance Awareness and Brokerage Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen the knowledge and confidence of the Cambodian people in the field of insurance through dissemination workshops and insurance brokerage.",""],[1,"155","3","Telecommunication-Based Insurance Sales Regulation","Strengthening sales management of insurance products though telecommunication by establishing necessary regulations.",""],[1,"155","4","Securities Market Development Initiative","Continuing to develop the securities market by urging and encouraging enterprises and companies to issue public securities, promoting trade, and examining the requirements for issuance of state securities.",""],[1,"155","5","National Committee for Cambodia's Financial Stability","Establishing the National Committee for Cambodia's Financial Stability.",""],[1,"155","6","Deposit Insurance Mechanism","Creating a deposit insurance mechanism in Cambodia.",""],[1,"155","7","State Securities Issuance and Open Market Operations Management","Managing the issuance of state securities, cash management, and open market operations.",""],[1,"155","8","Sovereign Securities Issuance Management","Managing the issuance of sovereign securities.",""],[1,"155","10","Credit Rating Agency Establishment","Establishing credit rating agencies.",""],[1,"155","11","Commodity Market Feasibility Study","Studying the feasibility to establish a future commodity market.",""],[1,"155","12","Financial Development Center Development Study and Partnership Initiative","Studying the geography and seeking partnerships to develop a Financial Development Center.",""],[1,"155","13","Casino Revenue Mobilization and Regulatory Enforcement","Strengthening revenue mobilization from casinos to the maximum extent permitted by the RGC, and enforcing the existing regulations and promoting the enactment of Casinos Management Law.",""],[1,"155","14","Public Investment Framework and Public-Private Partnership Preparation","Preparing public investment framework and public-private partnership.",""]],"116":[[1,"75","14","Business Environment Reform Agenda","From 2014, the Royal Government of Cambodia has launched a deep reform agenda to improve the business and investment environment, in particular to accelerate the provision of business services and further open market negotiations for Cambodian goods.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"76","3","Automated Business Registration System","Has been mplementing business registration through automation system, (2) issued Prakas on management and issuing permission for Businesses, recognizing legal representative for business registration transaction, and creating management and evaluation legal representative committee.",""],[1,"86","12","Functional Analysis List for Business Registration Delegation","In the process of preparing a functional analysis list for delegation to register enterprises and handicrafts with capital of less than US$ 50,000 and no risk to provincial, municipal, district and Khan administration.",""]],"117":[[1,"166","3","Youth Entrepreneurship and Innovation Promotion","encouraging the youths to have initiative, creativity, innovation or entrepreneurship mind",""],[1,"166","3","Youth Life Skills and Civic Harmony Development","developing youths to have knowledge, skill, ethics, living with each other with peace and harmony",""],[1,"166","3","Youth Participation in Community Decision-Making","creating opportunities for youths to participate in giving opinions, comments and decision making in the development of community and society",""],[1,"166","3","Youth Development Program Management and Monitoring Mechanism","strengthening mechanism for managing and monitoring the youth development program",""],[1,"167","21","Youth Digital and STEM Skills Strengthening","Strengthening digital skills and enhance the practical knowledge of science, technology, engineering and mathematics for youths in response to the Industrial Revolution 4.",""],[1,"167","22","Entrepreneurship and Self-Employment Support Services","Increasing the habit of creative and innovative thinking through entrepreneurial spirit, promoting self-employment and access to business and employment guidance services and market information.",""],[1,"167","24","Youth Participation in Community and Social Development Decision-Making","Encouraging young people to share their views, perspectives and participate in community and social development decision-making processes.",""],[1,"167","25","Youth Center Conversion to Community-Based Training Centers","Turning youth centers into community-based training centers.",""]],"118":[[1,"6","1","Result Framework Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","monitoring and evaluation of the Result Framework, especially setting the responsibility of the line ministries and agencies within each angle",""],[1,"23","5","NSDP Monitoring, Financing, and Governance Alignment with CSDG Framework","This includes proposals to \"hardwire\" the goals and targets within the M&E framework of the NSDP, and its financing and governance arrangements.",""]],"119":[[1,"111","6","Women’s Economic Empowerment Support Measures","The roles of women in the economy were promoted through social protection programs, vocational trainings, agricultural and rural development, entrepreneurship development, land reform, etc.",""],[1,"111","6","Women Development Centers","the Women Development Center in 14 provinces",""],[1,"111","6","Women Entrepreneurs Support Associations","Cambodia Women Entrepreneurs Association and Cambodian Business Women Federation are working to help develop careers, seeking for markets to sell the products, promoting entrepreneurship, leadership and strengthening the voice of women entrepreneurs in the economy.",""]],"120":[[1,"223","16","Mine and ERW Clearance Acceleration Programme","Cambodian Mine Action and Victim Assistance Authority (CMAA) will continually carry out its significant activities mentioned in the National Mine Action Strategy (NMAS) 2018- 2025, to speed up Mine/ERW clearance","Cambodian Mine Action and Victim Assistance Authority (CMAA)"],[1,"223","17","National Baseline Survey Completion","Complete national Baseline Survey of remaining districts by 2020.",""],[1,"223","18","Land Reclamation and Re-survey for Contamination Data Update","Conduct Land Reclamation/Land Cancellation (NTS) and re-survey to update contamination data.",""],[1,"223","19","Mine Contaminated Village Clearance Programme","Release prioritized known mine contaminated villages by 2021 and remaining villages by 2025.",""],[1,"223","20","Operational Systems and Capacity Enhancement","Review and enhance the existing operational systems and capacity.",""],[1,"223","22","Cluster Munition Contaminated Area Clearance and Release Planning","Plan and prioritize cluster munitions contaminated areas to be released.",""],[1,"223","23","Cluster Munition Contaminated Area Survey and Release Programme","Conduct survey and release confirmed cluster munitions contaminated areas.",""],[1,"223","25","ERW Contaminated Area Survey and Clearance","Survey and release known ERW contaminated areas.",""],[1,"223","26","Timely Emergency Out-of-Duty Call-Out Response Service","Provide timely EOD call-out responses as requested by community and authorities.",""],[1,"223","28","Mine and ERW Risk Education Programme","Provide effective gender-and age-appropriate mine/ERW risk education to people in current and emerging high-risk areas.",""],[1,"223","29","Mine and ERW Survivor Support Services","Support mine/ERW survivors and indirect victims by ensuring that they receive adequate and gender- sensitive medical and mental care, and physical rehabilitation.",""],[1,"223","30","Mine and ERW Survivor Livelihood Support Programme","Improve the livelihood capacity of mine/ERW survivors and indirect victims to enhance their inclusion and full participation in society.",""],[1,"224","1","Support for Local Development in ERW-Affected Communities","Support local development priorities in communities affected by mine, cluster munitions and other ERW.",""],[1,"224","3","Mine Ban and Conventional Weapons Compliance Promotion","Promote the compliance of the Anti-Personnel Mine Ban Convention (APMBC) obligations and the Convention on Certain Conventional Weapons (CCW).",""],[1,"224","4","Convention on Cluster Munitions Accession Support","Provide support acceding to the Convention on Cluster Munitions (CCM) and Support demining operations under the framework of the United Nations Peacekeeping Operations.",""],[1,"224","4","Demining Operations Support","Provide support acceding to the Convention on Cluster Munitions (CCM) and Support demining operations under the framework of the United Nations Peacekeeping Operations.",""],[1,"224","5","International Mine Action Cooperation and Assistance","Enhance international cooperation and assistance in mine action including South- South cooperation.",""],[1,"224","7","National Mine Action Capacity Strengthening Program","Strengthen national capacity to manage and implement an effective and efficient mine action program.",""],[1,"224","8","Mine Action Knowledge Preservation and Sharing","Preserve, enhance and share mine action knowledge within the sector and beyond.",""],[1,"224","9","Review of Legal, Institutional, and Operational Frameworks for Residual Threats","Review by 2020 the legal, institutional and operational frameworks, strategies and capacity needed to address the residual threats.",""],[1,"224","10","National Residual Threat Response Capacity","Develop, strengthen and maintain a sustainable national capacity to effectively address the residual threats after 2025.",""],[1,"224","11","Quality Management and National Information Management System Strengthening for Mine Action","Enhance the Quality Management System and strengthen the National Information Management System for Mine Action.",""],[1,"224","12","Gender Mainstreaming and Environmental Protection in Mine Action","Promote gender mainstreaming and mainstream environmental protection in mine action.",""],[1,"224","13","Performance Monitoring System for Mine Action","Apply the Performance Monitoring System (PMS) to mine action.",""],[1,"224","19","Emergency and Rapid Response for Mine and ERW Casualties","The Number of Mine and ERW casualties received emergency and rapid response from CMAA",""]],"121":[[1,"148","4","Prison System Reform and Reintegration Programme","Continuing to reform the prison system by managing the security-minded and humanitarian detainees under a sanitary environment, rehabilitation and vocational training and livelihoods when reintegrating into the community.",""]],"122":[[1,"91","2","Real Time Gross Settlement Development","Recently, the NBC has been developping the Real Time Gross Settlement (RTGS) to smooth the large value transaction payments.",""],[1,"91","3","Mobile Banking and Fund Transfer Services by MFIs","The Cambodian microfinance secotor (MFIs) has continued to grow remarkably and sustainably in the form of scope and scale of operations with profitability, and actively provided the mobile banking and fund transfer services.",""],[1,"130","2","Payment and Clearing System Strengthening","Likewise, the RGC has strengthened the payment and clearing system by promoting a more integrated system and the growing number of ATMs and mobile/internet banking.",""],[1,"141","12","Electronic Salary Payment System for Civil Servants and Banking Contractors","Continuing to organize and implement the opening of salaries of civil servants and banking contractors using the electronic system.",""]],"130":[[1,"33","10","Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Response","Carrying out border defense, sea security, exercise, and training; the UN peacekeeping operations; counterterrorism; humanitarian assistance and disaster response; international cooperation; and defense resources management.",""],[1,"60","24","Disaster Management Unit and Focal Point Coordination Mechanism","The only few numbers of line ministries-institutions has established a disaster management unit/ mechanism and assigned a focal point for effective and productive coordination;",""]],"131":[[1,"23","2","Youth Job Creation and Skills Development Programme","Creating more jobs, in terms of both quality and quantity aspects, for the citizens of Cambodia, especially for the youth through skill training, provision of job market information, improvement in working condition and promotion of business and investment inside and outside the country.",""],[1,"23","12","Human Resources and Skills Development","This has many dimensions, including: building human resources and skills;",""],[1,"47","3","Workforce Skills Upgrade for Productivity Improvement","In order to maintain this competitiveness, it is necessary to upgrade skills to the workforce to strengthen productivity.",""]],"132":[[1,"6","2","Greater Net Real Transfer to Targeted Beneficiaries","the RGC will vigorously work towards achieving a greater \"net real transfer\" of development resources to the targeted beneficiaries, particularly those in our rural areas.",""]],"133":[[1,"22","25","Public Institution Strengthening and Integrity Reform","Core to this strategy is the strengthening of public institutions, building a clean and high integrity public service, the democratic process and the rule of law.",""],[1,"22","25","Cross-Government Accountability and Coordination Reform","Three themes underpin the approach are accountability - a stakeholder system of responsiveness, adherence to mandate and to cross government cooperation, is coupled with emphasis on efficiency - building human resources, facilitating structural change and harnessing technology notably industrial revolution 4.0; improved opportunities for all, particularly the vulnerable groups, improved public services, as well as protecting natural resources and combating climate change.",""],[1,"23","4","Public Institution Capacity and Governance Strengthening","Further strengthening the capacity and governance of public institutions, at both national and sub-national levels, to ensure effectiveness and efficiency of public services delivery aimed at serving the people better as well as improving the business and investment environment.",""],[1,"29","8","National Public Administration Reform Programme","the National Program for Public Administration Reform 2015-2018 is structured for three main purposes: (1) developing public services that offer quality, simplicity, efficiency, reliability, rapidity, timely response to needs, easy access and allowing for the participation from all service users; (2) empowering and developing civil servants with more efficiency, effectiveness and reliability to provide public services, and adhering to the culture of public service, willfulness, loyalty and professional conscience; and (3) ensuring the salary system is equitable, increases productivity and efficiency, and ensures uniformity between the framework of the civil servants and the armed forces.",""],[1,"29","11","One Window Service Expansion","Cooperated with the Secretariat of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development in the development of legal documents for expanding the implementation of the One Window Service at capital, provincial, municipal, district and Khan councils.","Secretariat of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development"],[1,"30","1","Development of Public Service Standards Guidelines for ASEAN Countries","Cooperated with the ASEAN Secretariat to implement the Project on Development of Guideline on Public Service Standards for the 10 ASEAN countries.",""],[1,"30","3","Single Window Public Service Mechanism","Encouraged ministries and agencies to revise the structure to establish a single window office or mechanism in providing for public service such as SEZs, the district administration, and provincial administration, etc.",""],[1,"30","9","Improved Civil Servant and Contract Staff Deployment Planning","Improved employment planning for civil servants and contractual staffs to ensure deployment to right place.",""],[1,"30","11","Decentralized Management Information System for Civil Servants and Contractual Staff","Decentralized the management information system of Civil servants and contractual staffs which will be implemented in other Ministries and Institutions after successful project implementation.",""],[1,"30","13","Annual Civil Service Employment Planning and Recruitment Prioritization","In order to manage the civil servants and contractual staffs, Ministry has developed annual employment plans based on the number of retirements, death, professional Physical Unfitness, work abandonment and the prioritized needs in relation to specific positions, Units, and workplaces to serve the purpose of filling vacancies.","Ministry"],[1,"30","13","Civil Service Growth Rate Management","As a result, growth rates of civil servants have been implemented through statistic plan around 0.85% per year.",""],[1,"32","1","Decentralization and Deconcentration Program","Under the leadership and coordination of the National Council for Sub-national Democratic Development (NCDD) with cooperation of the public administration reform, public financial management reform and other sectoral reforms, the D&D program has been implemented",""],[1,"32","2","SNA Management System Review and Revision","the structure and SNA management system are continuously reviewed and revised to ensure compliance responding to the different characteristics of each SNA",""]],"134":[[1,"9","16","Trial Construction of Climate-Adapted Rural Roads","Studying and carrying out trial construction of rural roads 450 km with a bituminous surface which is 100% adaptive to climate change",""],[1,"9","17","Village Development Committee Capacity Building for Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation","Building the capacity of the VDCs in the option of adapting to and reduction of climate change and the use of appropriate and scientific knowledge acceptable at the locality",""],[1,"63","3","Dissemination Workshops and Official Capacity Strengthening","Dissemination workshops and strengthening the officials' capacity at national and sub- national level",""]],"135":[[1,"22","25","Human Resource Development and Structural Change Initiative","Three themes underpin the approach are accountability - a stakeholder system of responsiveness, adherence to mandate and to cross government cooperation, is coupled with emphasis on efficiency - building human resources, facilitating structural change and harnessing technology notably industrial revolution 4.0; improved opportunities for all, particularly the vulnerable groups, improved public services, as well as protecting natural resources and combating climate change.",""],[1,"23","12","Industry 4.0 Technology Adoption Support","enabling adoption and adaptation of new (Industry 4.0) technologies,",""]],"136":[[1,"22","25","Inclusive Public Services and Vulnerable Group Support","Three themes underpin the approach are accountability - a stakeholder system of responsiveness, adherence to mandate and to cross government cooperation, is coupled with emphasis on efficiency - building human resources, facilitating structural change and harnessing technology notably industrial revolution 4.0; improved opportunities for all, particularly the vulnerable groups, improved public services, as well as protecting natural resources and combating climate change.",""]],"137":[[1,"34","5","Village-Commune Safe Policy Implementation","The Ministry of Interior has implemented activities to ensure security, public order and safety for the people, especially through the implementation of \"Village-Commune Safe\" policies","Ministry of Interior"],[1,"34","5","Police and Community Officer Training","strengthening the training of officers under the theme of \"Police and Community\" aims to change the attitude of police officers, administration posts so that they can serve as security service providers with an effectiveness, friendliness and closeness to people","Ministry of Interior"]],"138":[[1,"35","7","Drug Demand Reduction and Rehabilitation Programme","It has made efforts to reduce the demand for drugs focusing on education, prevention, drug rejection, accident reduction, treatment, physical rehabilitation, vocational training, life skills, integration and moving away from drugs.",""],[1,"35","7","Multi-Agency Drug Control Coordination","The National Authority for Combating Drugs has enhanced cooperation with relevant ministries and agencies at national and sub-national levels and development partners.",""],[1,"35","8","Drug Offense Crackdown Coordination","The National Authority for Combating Drugs has coordinated and enhanced cooperation with relevant ministries and agencies, the Provincial Drug Control Committee and law enforcement units to take actions in time to crack down on drug offenses.","relevant ministries and agencies"],[1,"36","2","Anti-Drug Trafficking Campaigns","Implemented the campaigns against drug trafficking in accordance with the Decision on Strengthening Anti-Drug Action.",""]],"139":[[1,"36","10","Buddhist Education Services and Training Programme","The Ministry of Cults and Religion has been operating smoothly with the aim of providing equitable education services, improving the quality and efficiency of education services in the field of Buddhism by training both monks and Buddhist men about the discipline from Buddhist disciplines to higher education.","Ministry of Cults and Religion"],[1,"38","4","Buddhism Promotion and Clergy Capacity-Building Programme","The ministry has been organizing a live performance of Buddhism and promoting Buddhism linkages with society, Buddhism Concept Program, training course on duties, Code of Ethics, Khmer priests, and Cambodian Association of Khmer Priests.",""],[1,"38","5","Cultural and Religious Documentation, Preservation, and Dissemination Initiative","the Ministry has organized research, documentation, preservation and dissemination of cultural and religious documents.","Ministry | Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts"],[1,"57","10","Cultural Heritage Protection and Preservation Initiative","Participated in the protection and preservation of the \" Yaknaing\" temple at Virak Chey National Park, Rattanak Kiri and the Historic Village of \"Choeung Ek\" round village to be sustainable in collaboration with Department of Culture and Fine Arts.","Department of Culture and Fine Arts"]],"140":[[1,"38","9","Public Financial Management Reform Program","The Ministry of Economy and Finance has made good progress in implementing the Public Financial Management Reform Program.","Ministry of Economy and Finance"],[1,"39","1","Budget Management and Financial Accountability Strengthening","increasing confidence, consolidating budgeting, strengthening management and revenue collection, strengthening financial accountability through financial information management systems, expanding the implementation of program budgets and improving the implementation of budget strategic plans.",""],[1,"40","5","Budget Transparency and Public Financial Disclosure","Budget transparency has been steadily increasing through the dissemination of key documents, including (1) summary of budget proposals approved by the Council of Ministers, 2) easy to understand budget brief after the Budget Law is approved, (3) outcome report of mid-year budget implementation review, (4) Law of Settlement of State's General Budget for annual management, (5) audit reports on Annual Public Financial Management, (6). Audit Report Specifying the Draft State General Payment Law, (7) Cambodian Public Debt Statistics Bulletin, and (8). Procurement Plan, Bidding Notice, Procurement Contract and Audit Report, subject to the procurement entity's decision/budget entity for 2016 on the date 2015.",""],[1,"40","6","Implementation of Relevant Laws and Regulations","Relevant laws and regulations, budget management, procurement, property management and state securities are promulgated and implemented.",""],[1,"40","6","Budget Management, Procurement, Property Management and State Securities Administration","Relevant laws and regulations, budget management, procurement, property management and state securities are promulgated and implemented.",""],[1,"40","7","FMIS Pilot Expansion and Core Financial Management Mechanism","FMIS has so far completed pilots in the Ministry of Economy and Finance and is expanding the pilot implementation to other ministries and agencies.","Ministry of Economy and Finance"],[1,"40","10","Budget Entity Mechanism","The budget entity mechanism promotes transparency, accountability, transfer of authority and responsibility, and high participation of professional entities in the budget cycle.",""],[1,"40","13","Budgeting, Accounting, Payment, and Procurement Training Programme","Trainings have been organized continuously and collectively on budgeting, accounting, advanced payment, and procurement, among others.",""],[1,"41","3","Joint Budget Coordination Mechanism","Joint coordination mechanisms between specialized units of the MEF with other ministries and agencies, especially in the implementation of unregulated budget.","MEF"],[1,"41","9","Public Financial Management Reform Working Group Incentive Preparation","The preparation of incentives for the Public Financial Management Reform Working Group at line ministries and agencies is still in the process of developing rules and procedures to be implemented in 2018.",""]],"141":[[1,"45","2","ASEAN Economic Community Integration","Cambodia continues to implement an agreement with ASEAN to integrate into the ASEAN Economic Community as an equal partner.",""],[1,"45","6","Flexible and Responsive Foreign Policy Implementation","Implementation of foreign affair policy that is flexible, smart and responsive to the geo-poltic pressure and tense competition of the powerful countries",""],[1,"45","8","ASEAN Regional Cooperation and External Relations Engagement","Worked actively with all ASEAN member states to achieve ASEAN's goals as a community based, legal, caretaker and people-centered community based on \"One Perspective, One Identity, One Community\"and to promote ASEAN's relationship with other countries and regional organizations by adhering to the principle of neutrality, non-discrimination, openness, transparency, inclusiveness, an outward looking approach and peaceful resolution of disputes.",""],[1,"45","11","Opening of Three New Cambodian Embassies in Europe","the Ministry has decided to open three new Cambodian embassies in Europe: Turkey, Serbia and Bulgaria in order to strengthen ties, increase political confidence and open new markets.","Ministry"],[1,"46","4","ASEAN Integration Participation","Cambodia carried out obligations and participated in initiatives as an active member of ASEAN, which will continue to deepen integration to achieve the ASEAN Community Outcome 2025.",""],[1,"46","11","Cambodia-EEC Relations Development Memorandum of Understanding","Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo HUN SEN, the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, signed a Memorandum of Understanding with Mr. Tigran Sargsy, Chairman of the Board of the European Economic Commission for Asia to promote the development of relations between Cambodia and EEC member countries.",""],[1,"47","3","National Capacity and Systems Strengthening for Trade Integration","Cambodia's integration with the Asean Economic Community, including global trade relations, will require cooperation and coordination between governments and other development actors in strengthening national capacities and systems to improve service delivery and strengthen competitiveness of economic trade and build capacity for monitoring trade trends in all sectors.",""]],"142":[[1,"33","10","Border Defense and Security Operations","Carrying out border defense, sea security, exercise, and training; the UN peacekeeping operations; counterterrorism; humanitarian assistance and disaster response; international cooperation; and defense resources management.",""],[1,"33","10","UN Peacekeeping Participation","Carrying out border defense, sea security, exercise, and training; the UN peacekeeping operations; counterterrorism; humanitarian assistance and disaster response; international cooperation; and defense resources management.",""],[1,"33","10","Counterterrorism Operations","Carrying out border defense, sea security, exercise, and training; the UN peacekeeping operations; counterterrorism; humanitarian assistance and disaster response; international cooperation; and defense resources management.",""],[1,"33","10","Defense Resources Management","Carrying out border defense, sea security, exercise, and training; the UN peacekeeping operations; counterterrorism; humanitarian assistance and disaster response; international cooperation; and defense resources management.",""],[1,"45","4","Peaceful Border Negotiation and Demarcation Effort","Cambodia has been negotiating with neighboring countries to peacefully find a solution to the remaining border problem",""],[1,"45","5","Rescue and Repatriation of Cambodian Citizens Abroad","Cambodia has been working closely with its representatives abroad as well as with relevant ministries and agencies, including host countries, rescuing and repatriating Cambodian citizens, especially Cambodian workers abroad.",""]],"143":[[1,"51","8","Geodetic Benchmark Establishment Programme","Establishment of Geodetic Benchmarks as follows: 7 of the Zero Order points, 155 of the First Order points, 496 of the Second Order points, 1383 of the Third Order points and 835 Levelling Benchmarks;",""]],"144":[[1,"52","1","Home-Based Work Promotion and Demonstration Support","Adoption of appropriate techniques for women to perform the job at home requires multiple motivation and promotion, and practical demonstration.",""]],"145":[[1,"54","5","Fisheries Product Quality and Safety Monitoring and Control","In quality and safety monitor and control on fisheries products, Fisheries Administration has strongly taken attention through sending specialized officials to cooperate with relevant authorities to prevent the use of prohibited chemicals, especially imported fisheried products.",""]],"146":[[1,"63","5","Internal Rule on Management and Utilization of Ethnic Minority Communities","Preparing the internal rule on the management and utilization of the ethnic minority communities (450 communities)",""]],"147":[[1,"63","12","National Khmer Product Consumption Day","Designated April 9 of every year to mark the national day of Khmer product consumption to enable the Cambodian people to understand and purchase Khmer products during the Khmer New Year celebrations.",""],[1,"76","7","Domestic and Overseas Khmer Product Promotion Campaigns","Organizing campaings to sell Khmer products in all the provinces thoughout Cambodia, and participating in oversea annual exhibitions under the bilateral, regional or global frameworks.",""],[1,"76","12","National Price Tagging Requirement","Promoting for the price tag in national currency in businesses nationwide to ensure price transparency and protect consumer interests.",""]],"148":[[1,"63","15","Low-Interest Loan Support for Associations and Producers","Limited financial concession or low-interest loans for the associations, communities, makers and producers.",""]],"149":[[1,"64","18","App-Based Participation in Road Maintenance Program","Introduced App operation for participation in road maintenance program.",""],[1,"67","1","Construction and Public Works Quality Compliance","Implemented to duty to experiment the construction and public works in compliance with the technical standards to ensure all physical infrastructure have good quality and long-term use.",""],[1,"67","15","Transport Infrastructure Coordination and Problem-Solving Forum","As a co-chair of the Working Group on Transport Infrastructure between the RGC and the Private Sector and the Technical Working Group on Infrastructure Techniques and Regional Integration, established legal frameworks and organized a forum to support development and problem solving.",""],[1,"67","16","Guidance Principles for Private Highway Project Feasibility Studies","Provide a set of principles to private companies in their feasibility studies on highway projects as a priority project as set out in the Master Plan.",""],[1,"67","18","Technical Assistance for Road Construction Investment Procedures","Communicating with development partners to provide technical assistance in the formulation of procedures relating to investment projects for road construction projects.",""]],"150":[[1,"64","20","Phnom Penh Automatic Train System Feasibility Study","Studying the feasibility to construct the automatic train system in Phnom Penh.",""],[1,"65","8","Urban Rail Feasibility Studies","Studying the feasibility of building an automation train system and the possibility of constructing a tramway in Phnom Penh.",""]],"151":[[1,"67","11","Renewable Energy Street Lighting","Encouraged to use renewable energy such as solar LED, for street lighting",""],[1,"67","13","Energy Efficiency and Climate Change Mitigation in Transport Project","is collaborating with GIZ on the project on energy efficiency and climate change mitigation in transport.",""],[1,"67","14","Wastewater Treatment System Development","Developing a waste water treatment system in the city",""]],"152":[[1,"72","20","Nuclear and Radiation Regulatory Capacity Development","In technical cooperation with the International Nuclear Energy Agency and Vietnam, the MME focused on laws and regulations, safety of substances and sources of radiation in health, agriculture, water resources, energy development plans, environment, industry, conservation of cultural heritage and human resource development and the creation of nuclear and radiation regulator structures.","MME"]],"153":[[1,"76","9","Strategic Reserved Food Inventory Maintenance and Expansion","Maintaining and expanding the strategic inventory of reserved foods for victim intervention and market research.",""],[1,"102","7","Reserve Food System Management for Emergencies","The MEF continues to manage the reserve food system to support emergencies in times of natural disasters or severe weather events.","MEF"]],"154":[[1,"76","11","Private Sector Institution Development through Chambers and Business Associations","Promoting the development of private sector institutions through the establishment of chambers of commerce, business associations throughout the country.",""],[1,"78","3","Accelerating Inclusive Markets for Smallholders (AIMS)","Implementing the Accelerating Inclusive Markets for Smallholders (AIMS): The project covers 17 provinces and five types of products: fragrant rice, vegetables, chicken, cassava, and silk.",""],[1,"126","15","SME and Entrepreneurship Support","SMEs are supported by the state and commercial banks, entrepreneurship with skills, and an effort to push further",""],[1,"134","9","SME Development Support Measures","Support SME development policy by providing SME tax incentives, SME establishment and entrepreneurship fund, and entrepreneurship promotion center.",""]],"155":[[1,"76","14","Statistical and Business Information Publication Capacity Development","Developing the ability to publish statistical information and business information through business newsletters, and information technology.",""]],"156":[[1,"80","14","Cultural Promotion and Cultural Creativity Programme","The MOCFA has expanded the cultural promotion and cultural creativity as a priority program that contributes significantly to raising awareness and public participation through public service delivery and the organization of the cultural events.","MOCFA"],[1,"81","15","Khmer Sculpture Training and Dissemination Programme","Training and disseminating Khmer sculptures in 14 provinces: Kandal, Kampong Speu, Kampong Thom, Prey Veng and Kratie.",""],[1,"84","3","Cultural Exchange and Friendship Events Programme","Organized cultural exchanges through art performances, cultural events, or bilateral and multi-lateral cultural weeks with friendly countries.",""],[1,"84","8","Art Forum Stakeholder Dialogue Platform","Strengthened the dialogue through \"Art Forum\" to provide opportunities for stakeholders both public and private, NGOs, CSOs, and social media practitioners to express their opinions and understanding of each other to conserve and develop the national cultural development such as organizing a cultural forum on the \"Cultural Industry in Cambodia\", etc.",""],[1,"84","10","International Cooperation for Cultural Heritage Capacity Building and Promotion","Cooperated with international organizations and countries in capacity building, conservation and dissemination of cultural arts, national culture, festivals, exhibitions, special seminars with UNESCO in the implementation of the Convention for the Safeguarding of the Intangible Cultural Heritage 2003 and the Convention on the Protection and Promotion of the Diversity of Cultural Expressions 2005.",""]],"157":[[1,"85","1","SME and Handicraft Regulatory Enforcement Reform","The Ministry of Industry and Handicraft (MIH) has reformed the work of managing small and medium enterprises and handicraft by strengthening the law enforcement and amendment of the Law on Factory and Handicrafts Management, with a focus on key inspection work by helping to guide directly the factory owners about the regulation and technical standars and avoiding the inspection work as the disturbance or oppression.","Ministry of Industry and Handicraft (MIH)"],[1,"85","1","Industrial Safety Specification and Machinery Risk Management","In addition, the MIH has already issued a Prakas on the technical specification and industrial safety management on the risky mechanical machinery and equipment, and strengthened the management of the steamer to minimize the phenomenon that causes disasters to humans and other assets eventually.","Ministry of Industry and Handicraft (MIH)"],[1,"88","1","Workplace Safety Inspection Requirement","Issuded measures to prevent fainting accidents by requiring all factories and enterprises to inspect the technical conditions and surroundings of the factory to ensure safety before letting workers to work.",""]],"158":[[1,"86","5","Salt Processing Plant and Iodine Fortification Technical Assistance","Requested a specialist from UNICEF to assist in the development of salt processing plants and iodine fortification techniques.",""],[1,"86","8","Software and Hardware Skills Training for Employers, Workers, and SMEs","Building human resources on software and hardware skills to employers, workers and SMEs and handicraft officials through short courses, on-job trainings, local and oversea training.",""]],"159":[[1,"87","15","Online Foreign Labor Force Data Management System","Strengthened the use of foreign labor force data management system by requesting work quota, work permits and employment cards through online system.",""],[1,"87","17","Better Factories Cambodia and Labor Law Implementation Strengthening","Furthered Better Factories Cambodia (ILO-BFC) and strengthened the implementation of the Labor Law and International Labour Conventions.",""],[1,"87","18","Workplace Accommodation Directive for Pregnant Women and Muslim Workers","Issued directive to the owners of the factories, enterprises, and establishments to allow pregnant women to leave the work places at least 15 minutes early and allow Cambodian Muslim workers to use traditional Islamic clothing.",""],[1,"87","19","Workplace Breastfeeding Rooms and Crèche Facilities","Encouraged factories to prepare breastfeeding rooms for women having children whose age are under 12 months and to have a crèche (day-care center) for women having children whose age are over 18 months.",""],[1,"88","16","ASEAN Pension Scheme Cooperation for Migrant Workers","Cooperated with ASEAN countries in implementing the pension scheme, by allowing workers to transfer thier membership, seniority, and social security contributions from one country to another after the employment contract and to be a basis for the pension calculation.",""]],"160":[[1,"89","12","Legal Framework and Registration Support System","Establishing legal frameworks and supporting infrastructure such as the legalization supporting system for the people and the vulnerable, and the registration of the operating institutions is unclear.",""]],"161":[[1,"89","15","Policy and Strategic Plan Inspection, Audit, and M&E Strengthening","Inspection and audit, monitoring and evaluation implementation of policies and strategic plans as well as strengthening the mechanisms of the committees and other working groups well functional.",""],[1,"110","11","Annual Progress Reporting for the NPP Action Plan","Prepare the Annual Progress Report and Progress Report of the Action Plan 2016- 2018 of the NPP 2016-2030.",""],[1,"125","11","National Strategy Implementation and Monitoring Framework","The initial purpose of NSDP is to transform RGC's policies which are set out in the RS IV into actual implementation which will be implemented by line ministries, agencies, and sub-national authorities to inform back to national authorities to monitor the result of policy implementation on the macro-level.",""],[1,"125","11","Inter-Sectoral Results Framework","Table 3.4 depicts inter-sectoral result framework which provides direction and assure the relation and cooperation among the coordinating agencies.",""],[1,"125","11","National Strategy Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","This framework will be reexamined in Chapter 6 since it forms the basis of monitoring and evaluating NSDP 2019-2023.",""]],"162":[[1,"93","5","National Youth Development Framework and Youth Policy Instruments","The MOEYS has developed a document on national youth development framework, National Youth Service, Risk Management in Implementation on Cambodian Youth Development, draft Entrepreneurship Policy and Monitoring and Evaluation.","MOEYS"],[1,"93","5","Youth Councils and Volunteer Network Expansion","The MOEYS has updated the documentation for the Children Council and the Youth Council, organized the Youth Volunteer Network at both national and sub-national levels, the Youth Red Cross Movement, 150,000 Scout Movement Members, and expanded 5,000 Scout members in 2017.","MOEYS"],[1,"93","7","Life-Skills Training Seminars","The MOEYS has organized life-skills training seminars on AIDS prevention, drug and alcohol elimination, Traffic Law, elimination of violence among youths.","MOEYS"]],"163":[[1,"102","4","Social Protection Pilot Project Support","The development partners collaborated with the CARD and the SNAs in the pilot project support, which will provide lessons and experiences for the preparation of the income support components of social assistance in the National Policy on Social Protection Framework.","CARD | SNAs"]],"164":[[1,"102","10","Family Development and Domestic Violence Prevention Programme","Developed and implemented programs on family development, encouraged good family planning and prevented domestic violence by organizing national and international day on family on 15 May each year.",""],[1,"102","10","Gender Equality and Women's Decision-Making Promotion Initiative","Promoted gender equality at the national and sub-national level and the roles of women in decision-making through the dissemination of the Gender Perspective and the CEDAW to the focal points at the national and sub-national level and the dissemination of awareness on preventing domestic violence to the communities.",""],[1,"111","4","Gender Mainstreaming in National and Sector Plans","Over the past five years, the RGC has paid the much attention to promoting gender equality and empowering women in all sectors and at all levels, especially through in-depth mainstreaming into the NSDP 2014-2018, incorporating specific indicators for monitoring the implementation.",""],[1,"111","4","Gender Mainstreaming Strategic Plans for Ministries and Agencies","gender mainstreaming strategic plans of the ministries and agencies were developed and updated.",""],[1,"111","4","Budget Support for Sector Gender Roles","The 28 ministries and agencies have received the national budget and partnership budgets for the implemenation of their sector's gender roles.",""],[1,"112","9","Multi-sector Social Morality and Family Promotion Strategy","The National Committee for Promoting Value of Social Morality, Women and Families cooperated with relevant national and sub-national units, local authorities at all levels, authorities, CSOs, and national and international development partners, to jointly implement the multi-sector strategy and high-level recommendations of Samdech Ketti Pretpanditta Bun Ray Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and the honorable chairman of the National Committee for Promoting Value of Social Morality, Women and Families.",""],[1,"112","9","Youth Forums on Social Morality and Family Values","The National Committee also organized youth forums with debates broadcasted on national television network on social morality- and the value of Cambodian women and families in order to preserve national culture, ensuring the social morality respect.",""],[1,"112","9","Positive Child Raising Strategy","The inter-ministerial working group officially approved and implemented a Positive Child Raising Strategy in 2017-2021, responding to the National Action Plan on the Prevention of Violence against Women and Children.",""]],"165":[[1,"103","1","Human Trafficking Combat and Victim Rescue","combat human trafficking and rescue the victims.",""],[1,"103","1","Poipet Transit Center Construction","the construction of Poipet Transit Center is underwent to receive victims from the Thai authorities.",""]],"166":[[1,"104","6","Non-formal Education and Vocational Training for Juvenile Offenders and Children of Incarcerated Mothers","Cooperated with the MOI, international non-governmental organizations, providing non-formal education and vocational training to the juvenile children violating the laws and and children with mothers in prisons.","MOI"]],"167":[[1,"106","9","Regulatory Framework for the National Center for Veterans Protection","Meanwhile, the Ministry has issued a Prakas on the organization and functions of the National Center for Veterans Protection in Phnom Penh and is drafting the Sub- decree on Social Protection for the poor helpless elderly.","the Ministry"],[1,"108","7","Veterans Social Security Adjustment and Survivor Allowance Increase","The Ministry has paid attention to the situation of veterans by adjusting the social security system to the veterans since 2014 and increasing the monthly allowance to the parents or guardians of the dead soldiers.","The Ministry"],[1,"108","10","Veterans Day Commemoration Coordination","Cooperated with the Cambodian Veterans Association to organize the 21st Anniversary of Veterans Day each year at the national and sub-national level.",""]],"168":[[1,"107","5","Civil Servants Retirement Procedure Revision","The RGC has issued a circular on the revision of the procedure for the retirement of the civil servants to ensure effective retirement and pensions.",""]],"169":[[1,"109","6","National Institute of Social Affairs Capacity-Building Programme","Strengthened and expanded the activities of National Institute of Social Affairs to build human resource for the public sector, private sector, national and international NGOS related to social affairs.",""],[1,"109","9","NGO and Development Partner Resource Mobilization for Victims and Vulnerable Groups","Encouraged and cooperated with national and international NGOs and development partners in the spirit of solidarity and mobilized resources, including financial and technical resources, to serve the needs of all types of victims and vulnerable groups in society.",""],[1,"109","9","ASEAN Social Welfare and Social Protection Cooperation","At the same time, the MOSVY also closely cooperated both within the ASEAN Framework for Social Welfare and Development, including the ASEAN Regional Action Plan on Eliminating Violence Against Women and the ASEAN Regional Action Plan on Eliminating Violence Against Children, Guidance on Gender in Solving Women in Human Trafficking, Kuala Lumpur Declaration on the elderly people to \"empower the elderly people in the region\" to develop an action plan to implement the ASEAN Declaration on Strengthening Social Protection.","MOSVY"]],"170":[[1,"112","8","Women and Girls Health Information Expansion","by expanding information on the importance of health, sanitation and nutrition for women and children.",""],[1,"112","9","Scholarships, Local Institutions, and Dormitories for Girls and Students","The gender gap in the education sector has decreased at all levels by increasing the number of scholarships to students, especially women, increasing the number of local institutions, increasing the number of dormitories that provide affordable and safe services for students and girls.",""],[1,"112","9","Gender Mainstreaming in Curriculum","Gender equity and inclusiveness, including the incorporation of gender topics and key indicators are included in the curriculum.",""],[1,"113","1","Literacy Classes for Home-Stay Workers","the MOWA has contributed to the development of literacy classes for 1,926 home-stay workers (1,559 workers)","MOWA"],[1,"113","1","Community Kindergarten Mobilization Initiative","mobilize communities to organize the functions of community kindergartens for 12 target provinces","MOWA"]],"171":[[1,"130","5","Cash Management Measures","RGC will implement the following specific measures: Cash Management",""]],"172":[[1,"130","12","Deposit Protection Scheme Proposal Development","The NBC is supported by the Ministry of Economy and Finance to prepare proposals for deposit protection schemes, especially for small depositors.","Ministry of Economy and Finance"],[1,"131","6","Bank Consumer Protection Expansion Review","Review the desire to expand the bank's consumer protection by identifying requirements for loan products, promotions and promotional materials, claims procedures, fee calculations, interest rate calculations, and collection practices.",""],[1,"131","8","Microfinance Institution Compliance and Regulation Strengthening","Compliance with the promotion of microfinance institutions with Basel Committee policy with a focus on monitoring and regulation and changing levels of practice with banks.",""],[1,"131","9","Enforcement Against Illegal Microfinance Operators","Strengthen enforcement by taking strict actions against unregistered microfinance operators and those who operate illegally.",""],[1,"131","11","Microfinance Cost Reduction through Market Mechanisms","Find sources of low-cost funds and learn about the factors that contribute to microfinance institutions' borrowing costs and find ways to reduce interest rates through market mechanisms.",""],[1,"131","13","Microfinance Consumer Protection Implementation","encourage MFIs to implement their own consumer protection through SMART campaigns.",""]],"173":[[1,"126","15","Decentralized Budget and Personnel Management","Decentralization of budgetary functioning and personnel in main sectors, and resource allocation for monitoring and measuring of personnel which qualify to work effectively.",""],[1,"138","4","Public Institution Capacity and Governance Strengthening","Further strengthening the capacity and governance of public institutions, at both national and sub-national levels, to ensure effectiveness and efficiency of public services delivery aimed at serving the people better as well as improving business and investment environment.",""]],"174":[[1,"142","5","Civil-Military Cooperation for Disaster Response and Environmental Protection","Promoting the cooperation between all levels of the armed forces with the Ministry of Environment and the people through disaster response, humanitarian assistance, farming by contributing to the physical infrastructure, and the protection of the environment and natural resources.","Ministry of Environment"]],"175":[[1,"156","1","Intellectual Property Services Capacity Building","Improve the ability and capacity of management to provide and use intellectual property services in supporting to Cambodia's economic development;",""],[1,"156","1","Government Intellectual Property Policy and Services Strengthening","improve the Cambodian government's ability and capacity to provide intellectual property policy and services in supporting to agriculture, trade, industry, culture, and tourism industry sector;",""],[1,"156","1","Public Intellectual Property Awareness Campaign","increase knowledge and understanding among public about the role of intellectual property in the economy to support the increase of using intellectual property system by Cambodian business people;",""],[1,"156","1","Intellectual Property Law Alignment and Maintenance","develop and maintain the Cambodian intellectual property laws in line with international standards in order to complete Cambodia's economic and social needs.",""],[1,"156","7","Science, Technology, Innovation, and Human Resource Development Promotion","Promoting the development of science, technology, innovation, human resource development, raising awareness, using green technologies and nuclear technologies for peace purposes to support sustainable development.",""],[1,"156","9","Research Agenda Implementation Support","Developing and supporting the implementation of the research agenda in order to ensure sustainable development.",""],[1,"170","19","National Productivity Plan Promotion","Continuing to promote the National Productivity Plan to enhance national competitiveness in the region, especially in the ASEAN Economic Community.",""]],"176":[[1,"150","2","Cybercrime Enforcement Capacity Building","Building the capacity of law enforcement to deal with cybercrimes",""],[1,"150","3","Cybercrime Prevention Capacity Building","strengthening law enforcement and capacity building to prevent systematic cyber crimes.","MOI"],[1,"151","10","Cybercrime Prevention and Law Enforcement Capacity Building","Continuing to strengthen the law enforcement and capacity building to prevent cyber crimes and collaboration in preventing and suppressing this crime, pursuing the implementation of strategies, reducing crime, recording and incorporating accurate crime data;",""]],"177":[[1,"150","2","Border Dispute Resolution and Border Development Strategy","Continuing efforts to tackle the following: resolving both land and maritime boundary disputes with neighboring countries based on the foundation of international law; formulating and deploying a border development strategy to achieve peace and develop friendship and cooperation with neighboring countries; and preventing the use of the Cambodian territories for activities against neighboring countries",""],[1,"150","3","Border Peace and Land and Water Dispute Resolution","continuing to settle land and water issues with neighboring countries on the basis of the common international law along with the continuing to organize and promote regional development strategy the border is a border of peace, friendship and cooperation, while continuing to adhere to the principles do not allow territory against neighboring countries;","MOI"],[1,"151","6","Border Settlement and Border Area Development Strategy","Continuing to settle land and water border issues with neighboring countries on the basis of international law, along with continuing to develop and implement strategies to develop border areas as a border, peace, friendship and good cooperation.",""],[1,"151","7","Implementation of the RGC Open Sky Policy","participating in implementing the RGC's Open Sky Policy",""],[1,"163","2","Land Border Settlement and Border Area Cooperation Initiative","Continuing to completely settle land border issues with neighboring countries in accordance with international law and the principles of restructuring the post-colonial borders (Uti Possidetis) and transforming the border areas into a peaceful, friendly and cooperative area with development.",""],[1,"163","3","Flexible and Responsive Foreign Policy Implementation","Implementation of foreign policy which is flexible, smart and responsive to geopolitical pressure and tough competition of the world powers",""],[1,"163","4","Active Regional and Global Cooperation on Transboundary Security and Humanitarian Challenges","Cambodia continues to be actively involved with all countries in the region and the world in addressing the challenges facing the world, especially in the Middle East, Iran's nuclear program, the Korean Peninsula issue, the South China Sea crisis, the crisis in the state Rakhine, terrorism, disaster, crackdown on drug trafficking, human trafficking and transboundary crimes, communicable diseases, and illegal immigration.",""],[1,"163","6","Diplomatic Relations and International Cooperation Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen diplomatic relations with countries around the globe and further promoting the role and prestige of Cambodia on the regional and international levels within the ASEAN community, as well as in international cooperation frameworks, including preparations for the chairmanship and the host of the 2020 Asia-Europe Meeting, serving as Vice-President of the 73th United Nations General Assembly and a member of Economic and Social Council (ECOSOC).",""],[1,"163","8","ASEAN Regional Cooperation and Connectivity Initiative","Continuing to actively collaborate with all ASEAN member states to reduce the development gap among ASEAN member countries, integrate regional economies, and ASEAN Connectivity to further enhance people's living conditions and economic development to achieve ASEAN's goals as a single community following the \"one vision, one identity, one community.\"",""],[1,"163","10","Peacekeeping Force Deployment and Capacity-Building Training","Cambodia continues to send Cambodian peacekeeping forces to participate in the UN peacekeeping operation and to strengthen the capacity of Cambodian peacekeeping forces through trainings.",""],[1,"163","11","Institutional Reform for Diplomatic Professionalization","Reinforcement of institutional reform in the ministry to organize professional, patriotic, active and capable diplomats",""],[1,"163","12","Internal and Institutional Reform for Diplomatic Capacity","The ministry will continue to pursue internal and institutional reforms including enhancing the work environment, enhancing accountability and solidarity within the institution, and training officials both domestic and abroad to be the qualified diplomats.",""]],"178":[[1,"167","15","Non-Formal Education Program Development and Improvement","Developing and improving non-formal education programs.",""],[1,"167","16","Adult Literacy Programme","Promoting adult literacy programs.",""],[1,"167","17","Community Learning Center to Lifelong Learning Center Transformation","Turning a Community Learning Center into a Lifelong Learning Center.",""],[1,"167","18","Stakeholder Support for Non-Formal Education Programs","Promoting private sector, development partners, NGOs and the stakeholders' participation in support to non-formal education programs in the lifelong study framework.",""],[1,"167","19","Non-Formal Education Management Information System Improvement","Improving the effectiveness and quality of non-formal education management information system.",""],[1,"167","20","Capacity Development for Non-Formal Education Officers","Developing the ability of all levels of non-formal education officers.",""]],"179":[[1,"165","5","SEA Games Sports Infrastructure and Athlete Preparation Programme","Preparing for the 2023 SEA Games by continuing to develop key sport infrastructures, prioritizing sport types, training coaches and high sport technics, enhancing training of succeeding players and encouraging the movement of \"one youth can play at least one sport in life\" and enhancing sport health science to support the SEA Games competition process.",""],[1,"166","4","Physical Education and Sport Development Reform Strategy","Physical Education and Sport Development Reform Strategy: (1) developing regulations, (2) developing high-level sports, (3) developing sports for all, (4) developing physical education and sports at all education institutions and communities, and (5) conserving and developing all kinds of sports.",""],[1,"167","28","Sports for All Development Initiative","Developing sports for all.",""],[1,"167","29","School and Community Physical Education and Sports Development","Developing physical education and sports in all schools and communities.",""],[1,"168","1","Sports Participation Promotion Initiative","Encouraging education staff, students and the public to participate in sports.",""],[1,"168","2","School Physical Education and Sports Promotion","Promoting physical education and sports activities in schools.",""],[1,"168","3","Sports Federations Strengthening and Support","Strengthening and encouraging sports federations.",""],[1,"168","4","Sports Infrastructure Renovation Programme","Continuing to renovate sports infrastructure, especially national stadiums, provincial stadiums, National Institute of Physical Education and Sports, and educational institutions.",""],[1,"168","5","Sports Training for SEA Games Preparation","Continuing to train sports to prepare for the 2023 SEA Game.",""]],"180":[[1,"142","12","Citizen Participation in Policy Formulation and Implementation","The RGC will focus on (3) Encouraging people's participation in the formulation and implementation process of various policies",""],[1,"148","9","Civil Society and Political Party Legal Enforcement and Support","Continuing to enforce the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations and Law on Political Parties, updating the Association of Non- Governmental Organizations, Indigenous Communities, and Political Parties; continuing to disseminate the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations and Law on the Parties Politics; continuing to support and grant full rights to legitimate activities of the associations and non-governmental organizations.",""]],"181":[[1,"171","7","Health Strategic Plan Implementation and Update","Further implementing and updating \"Health Strategic Plan 2016-2020\" to enhance the quality, effectiveness and equity of health services.",""],[1,"171","9","Healthcare Quality Accreditation System","putting in place quality accreditation system at healthcare establishments, improving the capacity to manage regulatory inspection at both public and private health establishments .;",""],[1,"171","9","Health Regulation and Medical Ethics Enforcement","preparing and strengthening the enforcement of laws, regulations, and medical professional ethics especially the responsibility and changing the attitude of health service; and providers to comply with medical ethics;",""],[1,"172","10","Health System Accountability and Responsiveness Improvement","Make the health system more accountable and responsive health needs of the population.",""],[1,"174","2","Referral System Strengthening for Comprehensive Health Service Access","Strengthen referral system to enable client access to a comprehensive package of health and health-related services based on need.",""],[1,"174","3","Quality Service Delivery Compliance Initiative","Provide quality services in compliance with national protocols, clinical practice guidelines and quality standards.",""],[1,"174","4","Health Provider Behavior Change and Care-Seeking Promotion","Encourage behavior change of providers in interaction with patients and consumers of health services and improve health care seeking of the population.",""],[1,"174","5","Innovative Health Service Delivery Improvement","Strengthen and implement innovative approaches for effective, efficient and sustained health service delivery with increased accountability for results.",""],[1,"174","8","Health System Financial Efficiency and Accountability Improvement","Increase efficiencies in the use of available financial resources in transparent and accountable manner at all levels of the health system.",""],[1,"174","10","Alignment of External Health Funding with Ministry of Health Priorities","Align external funding with MOH policy, strategies, plans and priorities and strengthen coordination of funding for health by Development Partners.","MOH"],[1,"175","8","Health System Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Prepare institutional structures and functions at all levels of the health system to effectively respond to changing environment and the implications of major national reform programs.",""],[1,"175","9","Health Policy, Legislation, and Regulatory Capacity Development","Develop health policies, legislations and regulations, and build regulatory capacity at all levels of the health system.",""],[1,"175","10","Health Outcomes Ownership and Accountability Strengthening","Increase national ownership and accountability to improve health outcomes, and enhance coordination and collaboration among relevant stakeholders.",""],[1,"175","11","Public-Private Partnerships for Health Service Delivery and Policy Implementation","Use potential public and private partnerships in health service delivery, capacity development and implementation of the national health policies and regulations.",""],[1,"175","12","Community and Subnational Participation for Local Health Accountability","Encourage active participation of communities and subnational level administrations to strengthen local accountability in health.",""]],"182":[[1,"171","10","Health Sector Human Resource Development Strategy","Preparing and implementing the human resource development strategy for health sector in an effective and efficient manner to improve the competency and skills by uplifting the quality of training, both basic training before starting the career and refresher training after starting the career; preparing and strengthening health education quality accreditation mechanism; developing database for managing human resources",""],[1,"172","1","Health Official Redistribution and Rural Incentive Mechanism","and redistributing competent health officials in equitable manner; and strengthening incentivization mechanism especially for health officials based in rural areas.",""],[1,"174","11","Unified Health Workforce Planning Approach","Adopt a unified approach to health workforce planning, to ensure health workforce development is responsive to population and service needs.",""],[1,"174","12","Education and Training Quality Improvement","Improve the quality of education and training to meet skill and development needs of the workforce in a changing demographic and epidemiological environment.",""],[1,"174","13","Health Workforce Retention and Skill-Mix Improvement","Promote equitable distribution, ensuring retention and skill mix of health workers to enable effective delivery of health services.",""],[1,"174","15","Health Workforce Regulation and Management Strengthening","Strengthen health workforce regulation and management to ensure safe and quality of health service delivery.",""]],"183":[[1,"171","9","Healthcare Infrastructure and Medical Technology Investment","Uplifting the quality, safety, and effectiveness of health services, especially the essential and emergency services through increasing investment in healthcare infrastructure and medical technology;",""],[1,"174","21","Health Infrastructure Upgrade and Construction Programme","Build and upgrade infrastructure according to updated Health Coverage Plan and Health Infrastructure Building Briefs.",""],[1,"174","22","Public Health Facility Equipment and Transport Upgrade","Equip public health facilities with appropriate basic medical equipment and medical technology to improve diagnostic capacity and quality of healthcare service, and means of transportation.",""],[1,"175","1","ICT Infrastructure Expansion for Health Facilities","Expand ICT infrastructure to health facilities to allow transfer and use of ITs to support service delivery, teaching, and monitoring.",""],[1,"175","2","Infrastructure Maintenance Management Strengthening","Strengthen management of maintenance system for physical infrastructure, medical equipment, transportation and ICT.",""]],"184":[[1,"172","2","Medical Product and Food Safety Regulatory Enforcement","Strengthening the enforcement of laws and regulations related to the control and inspection of medical product quality, the use of medicines without doctor prescription, the use of chemical products in food, and the use of alcohol and tobacco.",""],[1,"174","16","Public Health Medicines and Health Commodities Supply","Provide public health facilities with sufficient quantity of quality assured, efficacious, safe and affordable medicines and health commodities, including vaccines, reagents and medical devices.",""],[1,"174","17","Rational Use of Medicines and Health Commodities Improvement","Improve the rational use of medicines and health commodities.",""],[1,"174","18","Pharmaceutical Quality Regulatory Enforcement Mechanism","Enforce regulatory mechanism to safeguard quality of pharmaceutical products, including medicines, health commodities, medical devices and equipment.",""],[1,"174","19","Medical Laboratory Capacity and Quality Control Strengthening","Enhance capacity of medical laboratories, with associated improvement in test reliability, along with strengthened quality control mechanisms.",""],[1,"174","20","Blood Supply and Patient Blood Management Strengthening","Provide safe and sufficient blood and blood products and strengthen patient blood management and use.",""],[1,"192","11","Laboratory Quality Strengthening Programme","Strengthening the laboratory quality in accordance with ISO/IEC17025.",""],[1,"192","12","Establishment of Laboratory Branches in Key Development Provinces","Strengthening the service of laboratory closer to development areas through the establishment of laboratory branches in key development provinces.",""],[1,"192","13","Laboratory Development through Partner Collaboration","Seeking collaboration with partners to develop laboratories.",""]],"185":[[1,"177","1","Social Protection Responsiveness Improvement","Improve responsiveness of Social Protection mechanisms with a view to FSN.",""],[1,"177","2","Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction Focus","Increase focus on climate change adaptation (DRR), including protection against environmental degradation.",""],[1,"177","3","Disaster Management Risk Reduction and Preparedness Mechanisms","Continue to strengthen disaster management (risk reduction, preparedness and response) mechanisms for all possible shocks (incl. climate, economic, health etc).",""]],"186":[[1,"187","20","Eco-Friendly Roadside Land App","Setting up an eco-friendly app for roadside land (Japan).",""],[1,"189","19","Green Logistics Temperature Management Chain Logistics Policy","Establishing a logistics policy such as management of goods in the Green Logistics Temperature Management Chain.",""],[1,"189","20","Environmental Management Technical and Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen technical and institutional capacity in environmental management.",""],[1,"189","21","Transport Sector Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming","Mainstreaming adaptation practices to climate change in policy guidelines and revising strategic plans and climate change action plans in the transport sector.",""],[1,"190","1","Research on Technical Standards for Road Infrastructure Construction","Continuing the research of technical standards for the construction of road infrastructure to ensure environmental sustainability and preparedness in response to climate change.",""],[1,"190","2","Sustainable Transport Promotion for Emissions Reduction","Continuing to promote the reduction of greenhouse gas emissions from vehicles by encouraging people to use buses, trains, bicycles and walking.",""],[1,"190","3","Climate Change Mainstreaming Training for Public Works Budgeting","Continuing to train national and sub-national technical staff on integrating climate change into the National Budget Plan for Public Works using the Economic Analysis and Training of Focal Points of an economic analysis approach to mainstreaming climate change into road construction projects using the national budget.",""]],"187":[[1,"191","23","National Port Policy Implementation and Port Development Master Plan","Continuing to implement the National Port Policy and develop a Master Plan on Port Development and promoting the development of ports in accordance with the correct technical standards.",""],[1,"192","1","Sustainable Port Development and Port Operations Modernization","Collaborating with the private sector and development partners to ensure sustainable port development, along with modernization of port operations such as the preparation of a port data exchange system.",""],[1,"192","2","Port Security Crew Training Center and Staff Skills Training","Establishing a training center for crews, disseminating and providing skills trainings to staff responsible for the port security.",""],[1,"192","3","Tbong Khmum Port Development Project","Promoting the development of the Tbong Khmum Port Project (Tonle Bit).",""],[1,"192","9","Port Construction Measurement and Technical Standards Development","Measuring for port construction and setting up technical standards for ports and waterways.",""],[1,"192","14","Container Port and Shipyard Rehabilitation Project","Constructing a container port of 350 meters, a depth of 14.5 meters, a container terminal and shipyard rehabilitation with a depth of 14.5 meters.",""],[1,"192","15","Goods and Container Storage Space Development Study","Studying the development of a storage space for goods and containers covering more than 54 hectares.",""],[1,"192","16","International Cruise Terminal Upgrade Study","Studying the plan for upgrading the international cruise terminal at the old port.",""],[1,"192","17","Preah Sihanouk Port Special Economic Zone Logistics Hub Development","Studying more about Preah Sihanouk Port's Special Economic Zone by creating a \"Customs Manufacturing Bonded Warehouse\" and \"Free Port\" serving as Logistics Hub.",""],[1,"192","21","Development Phase III Expansion","Continuing to push forward for the development Phase III on an area of 5.5 ha. which has the capacity to load up to 200,000 TEUs per year.",""],[1,"192","22","UM2 Harbor and Satellite Port Development","Continuing to promote the development of the UM2 harbor and to build a satellite port along the river and to build the dockyard near the LM17 container terminal.",""],[1,"192","23","Port Support Areas and Logistics Warehouses Development","Continuing to promote the establishment of port supporting areas, dry warehouses and cooling warehouses, and developing a goods collection and distribution service center.",""],[1,"192","24","TS1 Passenger and Tourist Terminal Modernization and Expansion","Continuing to modernize and expand TS1 Passenger and Tourist terminal.",""]],"188":[[1,"199","11","Inclusive Business and Social Enterprise Promotion","Promoting and encouraging the implementation of an inclusive business model or business activity, social enterprise initiatives to create a new dynamics for a systematic solution to accelerate the innovative business of the private sector that can help to solve problems for the poor and the people with low income in Cambodia.",""],[1,"199","13","Business Development Advisory Center Establishment and Cooperation","Continuing to establish a Business Development Advisory Center and cooperate with private business development advisory bodies.",""],[1,"199","14","Business Environment Improvement and One-Window Service Office Enhancement","Creating a business environment in order to increase registration, authorization, establishment of a small-scale manufacturing enterprise and handicraft as well as the better One Window Service Office.",""],[1,"199","15","Local Handicraft Processing Capacity and Digital Business Support","Improving the processing capacity of local handicraft and using digital system in businesses, especially innovative businesses and businesses providing social benefits such as social enterprises in contribution to local job creation.",""]],"189":[[1,"171","1","Freedom of Association and Trade Union Rights Protection","Ensuring the freedom of association to protect the rights of workers and employers, and to protect the rights and interests of workers and employers in accordance with the provisions of the Law on Trade Unions, the Labor Law and the International Labor Conventions.",""]],"190":[[1,"189","1","Tonle Sap Surrounding Environment Management Improvement Project","project to improve the management of the surrounding environment around the Tonle Sap.",""],[1,"197","7","Tourism Sector Master Plan","Preparing a master plan for the tourism sector with a focus on diversification of tourist products and destinations, attracting high-spending tourists and encouraging tourism- supporting industries.",""]],"191":[[1,"204","2","Science, Technology and Innovation Human Resource Development","Prioritizing the development of human resources in science, technology and innovation, based on the existing education system and vocational training, with support from the society and international cooperation.",""],[1,"204","2","Attracting Scientists and Talent from Abroad","Likewise, encouraging well- known scientists and attracting talented persons from abroad, which contributes to effective human resource building.",""],[1,"204","3","Science, Technology and Innovation Human Resources Development","Building human resources components in science, technology and innovation, necessary at all levels and the relevant ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"204","4","National Research and Development and Inclusive Innovation Ecosystem","Enabling the effective and efficient national research and development activities and building an inclusive innovation ecosystem, focusing on adaptability and imported technology localization.",""],[1,"204","4","National Priority Industry Upgrading for Domestic Consumption and Exports","Upgrading the national priority industry to serve domestic consumption and exports, which will lead to better development.",""],[1,"204","4","International Technology Absorption Capacity Enhancement","At the same time, increasing the ability to absorb international technology to increase momentum and move from the status of a lower middle-income country to an upper middle-income country that promotes sustainable development.",""],[1,"204","5","Experimental Research and Development Promotion","Promoting research and development (R&D) by focusing on experimental R&D which are national priorities and can help absorbe and adapt foreing technologies, based on strategies of self-inventing and purchasing (if necessary) and transfering the burden to the private sector at each stage.",""],[1,"204","6","Research and Development Funding Mechanisms","Creating, implementing, and managing (1) research and development funds of ministries and agencies; (2) technology procurement funds for ministries and agencies that do not conduct direct research; and (3) the national research and development fund, which is competing to support the national research and development activities set out in the national agenda of science, technology and innovation to stabilize the budget for key research and development, which is one of the main pillars of the development of the science, technology and innovation.",""],[1,"204","7","Science, Technology and Innovation Institutional Strengthening","Strengthening institutions, legal frameworks and financial support systems on science, technology and innovation to enable the national science, technology and innovation ecosystem to work together to implement human resource development, national research and development programs, as well as the commercialization of the results of this research",""],[1,"204","8","Institutional Strengthening for Science, Technology and Innovation","Organizing and strengthening the institution to be responsible for science, technology and innovation and research and innovation.",""],[1,"204","9","Public Services Strengthening for Innovation Ecosystem","Strengthening the public services as a key part of the innovation ecosystem such as patents and national standards for recognition and recognition of technology with national pride and global confidence.",""],[1,"204","10","Science, Technology and Innovation Enabling Framework","Developing laws, regulations and financial support systems, which form the basis for the development of science, technology and innovation.",""],[1,"204","11","International Science, Technology and Innovation Cooperation and Scientific Diplomacy","Strengthening the international cooperation in science, technology and innovation and preparing for official scientific diplomacy with the agenda of the science, technology and innovation for top-level discussion to make the relation of science, technology and innovation proceed smoothly.",""],[1,"205","2","Science, Technology and Innovation International Cooperation and Public-Private Partnership Strengthening","The effective development of science, technology and innovation requires international cooperation and the improvement of the public-private partnerships and cooperation which aim to build joint strategies and create an innovation system.",""],[1,"207","9","Scientific, Technological, and Innovation Cooperation Promotion","Strengthening scientific, technological, and innovative cooperation and promoting research activities and encouraging new innovations in business, services and products that are appropriate in national and digital contexts or industry revolutions 4.0.",""],[1,"207","10","Science, Technology, and Innovation Policy Development","Continuing and participating in policy development promoting science, technology innovation.",""],[1,"207","11","Technology Transfer Law Drafting","Preparing a draft proposal for a draft Law on Technology Transfer.",""],[1,"207","12","Patent Registration and Licensing Support","Strengthening the procedures and cooperation with domestic and international partners in strengthening and facilitating the registration, protection, and provision of patent licenses in the industry sector.",""],[1,"207","21","Curriculum Framework Development for Industrial Revolution 4.0","Developing a curriculum framework in response to the Industrial Revolution 4.0.",""],[1,"208","1","Teaching and Learning Methods Strengthening Initiative","Strengthening the new teaching and learning methods, such as descovery learning approach and other approaches for 21st century skills.",""],[1,"208","2","STEM and Creative Arts Skills Training","Training skills in science, technology, engineering, creative art and math.",""],[1,"208","3","STEM Policy Implementation Promotion","Promoting the implementation of policies on science, technology, engineering and mathematics.",""]],"192":[[1,"211","6","Private Sector Development Package","private sector development will be implemented through a package of comprehensive measures which covers: (1) Job market Development (2) Promotion of Small and Medium Enterprises and Entrepreneurship (3) Organization and Implementation of Public Private Partnership and (4) Strengthening Competition.",""],[1,"211","10","Job Forum and Labor Market Information Services Expansion","Further strengthening the \"Job Forum\" mechanism; providing job orientation training and expanding job recruitment and advertisement services; and streamlining labor market information, both inside and outside the country, in order to increase employment opportunities in an equitable manner and reduce migration for high risk jobs.",""],[1,"211","11","Minimum Wage Law Implementation and Wage Payment Enforcement","Implementing the Law on Minimum Wage for workers/employees subject to the provisions of the Labor Law by effectively reinforcing the tripartite mechanism; establishing criteria and principles considered in minimum wage negotiation process in line with socio- economic situation and productivity level; biweekly payment of wages and regular annual seniority payment to workers/employees.",""],[1,"211","12","Apprenticeship and Internship Program Expansion","Strengthening and expanding the implementation of apprenticeship/internship programs by making amendments to the Labor Law; institutionalizing the apprenticeship/",""],[1,"212","2","Work Inspection Strengthening and Workers' Data Management System","Strengthening the quality and effectiveness of work inspection in compliance with the Labor Law, the Law on Unions, the Law on Social Security, and international labor standards in order to improve workers' rights, freedom of association, the working conditions, travel to work safety of workers-employees; Strengthening workers- employees data management system in order to manage the issuance of work certificates, payments of seniority bonuses and pensions.",""],[1,"212","3","Industrial Relations and Labor Dispute Settlement Reform","Improving the industrial relations by reinforcing the work dispute settlement mechanism, better enforcement and proper interpretation of legal provisions related to the Labor Law, the Law on Unions, the Law on Social Security and other international labor conventions.",""],[1,"212","4","Migrant Worker Governance and Reintegration Support","Strengthening the governance of migrant workers and expanding bilateral and multilateral cooperation to open up job markets in foreign countries; preventing illegal migrant workers; promoting the protection of workers' rights, work safety and dignity; facilitating communication with migrant workers' families; and reintegrating returning migrant workers through skills recognition, transfer of their social security entitlements back to the country; and consultations on job seeking opportunities and the prospect for self-employment.",""],[1,"212","5","Worker Welfare Support Measures","Endeavoring to reduce the cost of electricity and clean water for workers-employees, and students living in rented houses; promoting safe accommodation and transport arrangements for workers-employees; implementing the 3-month maternity leave with 120% salary; providing free healthcare service and pregnancy examinations at public hospitals/health centers; providing assistance to female workers who are pregnant or have just delivered babies; and reviewing the tax exemption threshold for the minimum wage and providing tax exemption for additional benefits.",""],[1,"212","7","Industrial Relations and Working Conditions Improvement Programme","Developing working conditions and harmonization in industrial relations by continuing to improve working conditions, occupational safety and health, prevent the use of child labor and forced labor, strengthen the mechanism of minimum wage determination and benefits of workers, employers and strengthen the harmonization in industrial relations aiming to promote working conditions and harmonization of industrial relations that brings about trust for workers and employers who are investing in Cambodia.",""],[1,"212","8","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Modernization","Modernizing the system of technical vocational education and training development by further strengthening of the quality of technical skills training, expanding skills training to support the socio-economic development policies, strengthening the partnership between the public and private sectors and other partners to ensure the sustainability of technical vocational education and training, promoting governance in technical vocational education and training and promoting research and innovative technology",""],[1,"212","9","Career and Employment Services Expansion","Broadening career and employment space by increasing decent work and employment productivity; expanding mechanisms, scope and efficiency of career and employment services to better respond to meet the needs of consumers, management of the use of labor force in the country and protection of the Cambodian migrant workers; providing orientation prior to entering into work to increase equitable",""],[1,"213","2","Social Security Fund Expansion and Pension Scheme Preparation","Developing social security fund for workers and public officials, former civil servants and veterans by continuing to strengthen and expand practices of social security on occupational risk scheme, strengthening and expanding the implementation of social security fund in health care, promoting the preparation to launch pension schemes and to strengthening social security fund in the informal economy as well as developing the capacity to optimize the provision of services",""],[1,"213","3","Electricity and Clean Water Affordability Support for Renters","Continuing to cooperate with the MME and the MIH to promote the linkage of electricity and clean water at affordable price to workers and students living in rented houses","MME | MIH"],[1,"213","3","Special Lease Law Implementation and Tax Exemption Measures","promote the implementation of special lease laws (lease of rooms), tax exemption for additional benefits and continue the adjustments of the taxable minimum wage from 1 million riels",""]],"193":[[1,"213","5","Poor Household Identification and Equity Card Issuance","Continuing to identification of poor households and produce ID poor or equity cards as soon as possible.",""],[1,"213","6","Expanded Poor Household Identification Coverage","Expanding regional coverage for the identification of poor households, including urban areas, and on specific requests for vulnerable populations such as persons with disabilities or veterans, families, and people living with HIV/AIDS.",""],[1,"213","7","Poverty Data Dissemination to Ministries and Stakeholders","Disseminating the data on poverty to all ministries and agencies and other relevant stakeholders.",""]],"194":[[1,"218","11","Drinking Water Supply Expansion Programme","Expanding the supply of drinking water in the capital, towns, industrial areas and SEZs by expanding the capacity of public and private water units in accordance with technical standards and in compliance with national drinking water standards.",""],[1,"219","11","Economic Land Concession Management Strengthening","Strengthening the management of economic land concessions; continuing the clearing of landmines and unexploded ordinances; and carrying on work related to the grant of social concession lands to poor households for family-based farming.",""],[1,"219","11","Landmine and Unexploded Ordnance Clearance","Strengthening the management of economic land concessions; continuing the clearing of landmines and unexploded ordinances; and carrying on work related to the grant of social concession lands to poor households for family-based farming.",""],[1,"219","11","Social Concession Land Allocation for Poor Households","Strengthening the management of economic land concessions; continuing the clearing of landmines and unexploded ordinances; and carrying on work related to the grant of social concession lands to poor households for family-based farming.",""],[1,"219","12","Irrigation System Investment and Maintenance Programme","Prioritization of investment in irrigation systems by focusing on linkages with agricultural production areas together with regular maintenance and reinforced management of these systems.",""],[1,"219","13","Rural Development Investment Expansion","Maintaining the efforts to promote a vibrant rural development with additional investment in rural roads, small-scale irrigation systems, expansion of electricity supply coverage",""],[1,"225","7","Administrative Process Strengthening and Staff Training for MOWRAM","Strengthening administrative processes and provide training to the MOWRAM officials in response into international and national standards.","MOWRAM"],[1,"225","8","Water Governance Capacity-Building and Public Awareness Programme","Continuing to strengthen the capacity of officials, at the central and sub-national levels for both males and females, with FWUC being aware of the advantages of water on daily livelihood and economic development in order to advise them to actively participate in management planning, maintenance, conservation, and effective and sustainable water usage to maintain good eco-system, through training, workshops, school curriculum, bulletins, magazines, radio, TV and other media.",""],[1,"225","9","Gender Network in Provincial Water Resources and Meteorology Departments","Setting up a gender network in all Provincial Departments of Water Resources and Meteorology.",""],[1,"225","10","Gender Awareness and Gender Analysis Training for Gender Network Officials","Increasing the awareness of gender and gender analysis to gender network officials at all levels.",""],[1,"225","11","Gender Working Group Participation Requirement","Ensuring all the programs and projects of ministry must have gender working group participation.",""],[1,"225","12","MOWRAM Technical and Managerial Capacity Building for Irrigation and Drainage","Improving the technical and managerial capacity of both male and female officials of MOWRAM to implement irrigation methods and drainage technology.","MOWRAM"],[1,"225","14","Irrigation Scheme Rehabilitation and Construction","Rehabilitating and constructing the existing irrigation schemes to meet the urgent needs of water for agriculture.",""],[1,"225","15","Irrigation Scheme Rehabilitation and Construction","Prioritizing the rehabilitation and construction of irrigation schemes and drainage systems in areas with high poverty.",""],[1,"225","16","Reservoir and Waterbody Maintenance and Expansion","Encouraging the maintenance and expansion of reservoirs, lakes, ponds, intake canals and drainage systems to ensure an adequate water supply for the cultivation zone, aquaculture, daily living and animals.",""],[1,"225","17","Water Management Innovation Technology Dissemination","Promoting the dissemination of water management innovation technology in rain-fed agricultural areas which depend on rainwater.",""],[1,"225","18","Irrigation System Construction and Rehabilitation","Building and rehabilitating irrigation systems to ensure adequate water supply to farmers.",""],[1,"225","19","Farmer Water Users Community Support","Establishing, strengthening, and providing technical support to the Farmer Water Users Community (FWUC).",""],[1,"225","20","River Basin Development Planning","Studying and preparing river basin development plan on a short, medium and long term basis, with a consideration placed on the changing of water discharge, water current, and aquifers to ensure the sustainable use of water.",""],[1,"225","21","Integrated Water Resources Management and Development","Implementing integrated water resources management and development, while thoroughly considering a clear link between water sources and other sectors of the environment, including the changing needs of humans and the environment for water and other resources needed to achieve the effective management.",""],[1,"225","22","River Basin Development and Management Plan Implementation Awareness Campaign","Increasing the awareness and encouraging the implementation of river basin development and management plans with the cooperation of concerned ministries, stakeholders and beneficiaries, especially women.",""],[1,"226","1","Farmer Participation in Irrigation and Drainage Project Development","Encouraging the farmers' participation, especially from women, stakeholders, and the private sector to in all stages of project preparation and project improvement as well as irrigation and drainage system development.",""],[1,"226","2","Farmer Water Users Community Capacity Building for Irrigation Scheme Operation and Maintenance","Improving Farmer Water Users Community's (FWUC) capacity on the operation and maintenance of irrigation schemes with farmers' and development partners' participation.",""],[1,"226","3","FWUC Strengthening and Establishment for Water Management","Strengthening and establishing FWUC to participate effectively in sustainable water resources management, water distribution, and irrigation maintenance.",""],[1,"226","4","Irrigation Scheme Management Investment Mobilization","Encouraging investments from international donors and the private sector to support the management of irrigation schemes with farmers' and development partners' participation.",""],[1,"226","5","Irrigated Agriculture Income Generation and Water Sector Investment","Generating income through irrigated agriculture and continual investments in the water sector for agricultural productivity.",""]],"195":[[1,"222","25","Agricultural Sector Anti-Trafficking and Crime Prevention Measures","Promote the effectiveness of participation in preventing and eliminating human trafficking activities and other crimes in the agriculture sector which harm agricultural",""]],"196":[[1,"230","10","Human Resource Development for Public Service Delivery","Continuing human resource development to increase the effectiveness of the delivery of public services.",""],[1,"230","11","Village Development Committee Capacity Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen the capacity of the Village Development Committee.",""],[1,"230","12","Integrated Village Development Programme","Continuing integrated village development.",""],[1,"230","13","Community Disaster Preparedness Awareness Campaign","Continuing to raise awareness of disaster preparedness and to reduce disaster in the community.",""],[1,"230","15","Strengthening Rural Development Centers","Continuing to strengthen the Rural Development Centers in Takeo, Kampong Speu and Cambodia-Korea.",""]],"197":[[1,"230","17","Indigenous Peoples Livelihood Development Initiative","Developing indigenous peoples' lives to move away from starvation and extreme poverty.",""],[1,"230","20","Basic Education and Vocational Training for Indigenous Peoples","Providing at least 9-year basic education to indigenous people and providing vocational training in accordance to their needs and based on the geography of each ethnic group.",""],[1,"239","4","Collective Land Registration for Indigenous Communities","Registering the land of 10 indigenous communities as a collective ownership per year.",""]],"198":[[1,"231","14","Human Resource Capacity Building for Clean Water Sector","Building human resource capacity both in quantity and quality in response to the needs of the General Directorate of Clean Water and the private sector in a systematic and sustainable manner.",""],[1,"231","15","Technical and Water Sector Capacity-Building Training Courses","Increasing the training courses that build the capacity of technical officials and officials from the public and private water units on production operation, electrical and mechanical systems maintenance, and other skills required for the emergency phase.",""],[1,"231","16","Water Supply Training and Research Center Development","Seeking assistance sources to build a water supply training and research center.",""]],"199":[[1,"233","5","Implementation of the National Policy on Mineral Resources","Promoting the implementation of \"National Policy on Mineral Resources 2018- 2028\" by strengthening the governance and management of mineral resources and business while encouraging the contribution of community in order to reduce the negative impact on environment and society and strengthen the national revenue mobilization.",""],[1,"233","6","Sand Resource and Business Management Mechanism","Strengthening sand resource and business management mechanism by minimizing the social and environmental impact.",""],[1,"233","11","National Mineral Resources Policy Implementation and Mining Governance Strengthening","the MME will continue to implement the National Mineral Resources Policy 2018- 2028 by strengthening the governance and management of mineral resources and business, while promoting participation from the communities to minimize social and environmental impact and increase the revenue collection, strengthen the mechanism for managing mining","MME"],[1,"234","2","Mineral Resource Governance Strengthening","Strengthening the institutional roles in managing and developing mineral resources, with an emphasis on eliminating illegal mining businesses and collecting non-tax revenue to the state.",""],[1,"234","4","Decentralized Small-Scale Mining Licensing and Management","Managing and developing small-scale mining handicrafts and mining businesses through delegations to sub-national authorities to license and manage mining businesses within their mandate.",""]],"200":[[1,"235","2","Creative Conservation and Sustainable Ecotourism Financing Mechanisms","Developing creative solution in conservation and development, as well as creating opportunities for sustainable ecotourism and financing mechanisms.",""],[1,"235","10","Community Employment Integration in Commune Investment Plans","Expanding employment opportunities for local communities by providing direct and beneficial opportunities for employment generation and encouraging the integration of activities in community management plans into each commune investment plan.",""],[1,"235","12","Protected Areas Community Livelihood Support Programme","Mobilizing support and resources for establishing and expanding production, contributing to improving the livelihoods of protected areas communities in the Mekong River region and north and south parts of the Tonle Sap.",""],[1,"235","13","Ecotourism Development and Natural Resource Conservation","Preparing ecotourism and conserving natural resources.",""],[1,"235","16","Protected Areas Tourism and Ecotourism Partnership Strengthening","Strengthening the cooperation and partnerships with relevant ministries and agencies, especially with tourism and ecotourism companies, and ecotourism development projects and ecotourism services to be improved and increase the number of tourists visiting the protected areas.",""]],"201":[[1,"238","1","Legal and Performance Support Framework for the Cultural Sector","Developing legal norms and performance mechanisms for supporting artists, producers, organizations, and entrepreneurs with careers in culture.",""],[1,"238","2","Cultural and Labor Market Product Development Collaboration","Collaborating with line ministries and agencies to promote the creation of cultural and labor market products in culture and arts.",""],[1,"238","3","Cultural Products and Services Market Expansion","Expanding the market of cultural products and services by providing opportunities for artists, producers and businessmen in culture and arts.",""],[1,"238","4","Creative Industries Promotion Initiative","Encouraging and promoting creativity, original accomplishments and new in music, cinema, visual arts, crafts, handicrafts, traditional weaving and designs.",""],[1,"238","5","Creative Works Exhibition Promotion","Promoting the exhibition of creativity works in the arts, culture and creative industry.",""],[1,"238","6","Film Industry Promotion Initiative","Promoting filming industry in Cambodia.",""],[1,"238","7","Cultural Product Promotion Initiative","Promoting Cambodia to be a cultural product promotion site.",""],[1,"238","8","Database on Cultural Organizations, Associations and Enterprises","Creating a database on cultural organizations, associations and enterprises.",""],[1,"238","10","Technology Equipment Import Facilitation Mechanism for Culture Sector Entrepreneurs","Establishing a mechanism to facilitate the import of standard and legitimate technology equipment for entrepreneurs in the culture sector.",""]],"202":[[1,"240","7","Construction Control and Permit Compliance Enforcement","Strengthening construction management by taking strict measures to control and prevent the construction on the state public land and unauthorized construction; and promote constructions, in alignment with permits to avoid impacts on the beauty, safety, public order, environment and beaches of Cambodia.",""],[1,"240","8","Construction Business E-Registration and Service Expansion","Launching public service on construction business e-registration and moving to provide more services.",""],[1,"240","9","Property Construction Data Management IT System","Introducing IT system for the management of property construction data by connecting to GIS of Google Maps.",""],[1,"240","10","Transparent Construction Sector Dispute Resolution","Promoting transparent dispute resolution in the construction sector.",""],[1,"240","11","Design and Construction Business Management Strengthening","Strengthening the management of individual and legal entities in design and construction business.",""],[1,"240","12","Development of Construction, Land, Housing, and Coastal Area Laws","Developing laws: (1) Law on Construction, (2) New Law on Land, (3) Law on Land Management and Urbanization, (4) Law on Housing, (5) Law on Cambodia's Coastal Area Management and Development.",""],[1,"240","13","Public-Private Partnership on Land Policy","Formulating policies and strategies: National Policy on Public Private Partnership on Land and National Strategy on Municipality and Urban Area Development.",""],[1,"240","14","Construction Sector Regulatory Framework Reform","Formulating Royal Decrees, Sub-decrees and regulations: (1) Royal Decree on Organization and Fuctioning of National Council for Construction Technical Regulations, (2) Royal Decree on Organization and Fuctioning of National Council for Construction-related Professional Board, (3) Sub-decree on Cambodia's Coastal Area Management and Development, (4) Sub-decree on Professional Code of Conduct in Construction Sector, (5) Sub-decree on the Management of Tradespersons in Construction (for tradespersons whose professional boards have not been established yet), (6) Sub-decree on Licensing in Construction, (7) Sub- decree on the Organization and Fuctioning of the National Construction Laboratory, (8) Sub-decree on Building, Repairing and Demolition Permit, (9) Sub-decree on Conditions and Procedures of Construction Regulation, (10) Sub-decree on the Uniforms, Insignias, and Decorations of the Construction Inspectors, (11) Sub-decree on Conditions and Procedures of the Complaints in Construction, (12) Sub-decree on the Organization and Fuctioning of the Commissions for Construction Dispute Resolution, (13) Sub-decree on the types and sizes of construction which require insurance for building or demolition (14) Sub-decree on the Establishment of Cambodia's Coastal Area Conservation Fund and (15) other regulations supporting the land management, urbanization, construction and housings.",""]],"203":[[1,"242","3","Clean and Renewable Energy Investment Promotion","Continuing to encourage and increase investment in clean energy and renewable energy, especially solar power while reducing the production of energy from unclean sources to ensure long-term energy security.",""],[1,"242","8","Renewable Energy and Energy Efficiency Policy and Legal Reform","Enhancing and improving policies and legal instruments to increase the contribution of renewable energy in Cambodia's energy mix and energy efficiency",""]],"204":[[1,"242","4","Regulatory, Research, and Capacity Development for Sustainable Environmental Management","Strengthening regulatory framework, research, as well as the development of skill and capacity for national and sub-national official in terms of environment, green development, climate change, integrated water resource management, and the usage of natural resources in a sustainable manner.",""],[1,"242","6","Policy Alignment and Consistency Mechanism","Ensuring the consistency on the development of the priorities of the national sustainability policies, plans and programs and aligning the priorities of the policies, plans and programs with national, regional and international policy instruments to which Cambodia is amember.",""],[1,"242","7","Science, Technology, and Innovation Research and Development Promotion","Promoting research and development in science, technology, innovation, human resource building, awareness raising, and the use of green and nuclear technology for peaceful purposes to support sustainable development.",""],[1,"242","9","National Research Agenda Development and Implementation Support","Developing and supporting the implementation of a national research agenda to ensure sustainable development.",""],[1,"242","10","Strategic Environmental Assessment Integration","Encouraging the incorporation of strategic environmental assessments into decision-making processes, policies, plans and legal instruments",""],[1,"242","12","National Council for Sustainable Development Modernization","Modernizing the National Council for Sustainable Development in fulfilling its roles and duties to ensure good governance and the needs of the Cambodian people are met.",""],[1,"242","13","Green City Sustainable Strategic Plan","Developing and starting the implementation of Green City Sustainable Strategic Plan.",""],[1,"261","14","Implementation of the National Sustainable Development Strategy 2019-2023","the NIS/MOP continues to implement the NSDS 2019-2023 with the 8 strategic objectives as follows:","NIS/MOP"]],"205":[[1,"245","2","Public Investment Prioritization for Social Sectors and Disadvantaged Areas","During the new planning cycle, public investment will continue to prioritize the social sectors, and the need to target investments on disadvantaged groups and lagging communities.",""],[1,"245","2","Private Sector Productivity and Technology Transfer Investment Promotion","Within the private sector, investments are needed to deliver step changes in productivity and the transfer of new technologies to maintain competitiveness and high levels of employment.",""],[1,"245","2","Monitoring and Tracking of Private Investment Flows","new efforts will be made to monitor and track these flows and influence their composition.",""],[1,"245","3","Strengthening Government Capacity for Investment Sourcing and Delivery","Efforts will also be made to strengthen the capacities of government institutions for the sourcing, management and delivery of investments.",""]],"206":[[1,"260","6","Statistical System Restructuring through the NSDS","Extension of the NIS's efforts (via the NSDS) to reshape the statistical system, including administrative data is a priority",""],[1,"261","12","National Statistical Development Strategy","The NSDS will provide a roadmap to support the sustainable data production.",""],[1,"261","15","National Statistics System Core Data Set Development and Maintenance","Strategic Objective 1: Develop, implement, and maintain a core data set of high quality, by all institutions of the National Statistics System (NSS), under the leadership",""],[1,"262","1","National Statistical System Alignment and Data Infrastructure Improvement","To achieve these strategic objectives, there are 4 priority activities: (1) link the operation of national statistic system to development policies; (2) improve data policy and statistical infrastructure; (3) support for data compilation for CSDGs; and (4) continue to improve socio-economic statistics.",""],[1,"262","2","Strengthening of Statistical Legislation and Institutional Infrastructure","Strategic Objective 2: Strengthen further statistical legislation, institutional infrastructure, organization structures, independence of the NIS & operational, financial & administrative management systems of the NSS to support statistical production & development",""],[1,"262","3","Human Resource Management and Policy Reform for the National Statistical System","introduce human resource management and policy",""],[1,"262","3","National Statistical System Training Programme","develop and continue widely training program with national statistical system",""],[1,"262","4","ICT Strategy and Plan for Statistical Capacity","Strategic Objective 4: Develop & implement the ICT Strategy & Plan to provide state- of-the-art ICT capacity to support all aspects of statistical collection, processing, analysis, maintenance & dissemination by focusing on strategic use of the ICT with minimum reduction of labor.",""],[1,"262","5","Statistics Dissemination and Advocacy Strategy","Strategic Objective 5: Develop and implement a Dissemination Strategy & an Advocacy and Literacy Strategy to provide improved access to all users & increased demand for statistics through the priority activities as follows: (1) support using data for policies and plans preparation and (2) promote and interact effectively with consumers across the country.",""],[1,"262","6","National Statistical System Coordination Strengthening","Improve coordination of the NSS to eliminate data conflicts and produce comparable, timely statistics in the NSS as efficiently as possible by focusing on extending the scope and mechanism of coordination in the national statistical system.",""],[1,"262","8","Revised Financing Procedure for Priority Statistical Programs","Promote stability and growth of budget support for the NSS from both domestic and international sources to allow effective planning and implementation of priority statistical programs through the implementation of the provisions of the Law on the Statistics concerning the revised procedure for financing.",""]],"207":[[1,"275","5","Government Capacity and E-Governance Improvement Initiative","Improving capacities within the government (both at the national and sub- national levels) to deliver quality services through better inter-ministry/agency communication and sharing of information, improved (vertical) integration between the sub-national levels and the apex ministries/agencies, and promoting e-governance in the context of Industrial Revolution 4.0.",""],[1,"275","6","National Strategic Development Plan Alignment Framework","The NSDP's purpose is to ensure that the actions, programs and projects of all ministries, agencies and sub-national authorities are aligned to implement the RGC's prioritised policies outlined in the Rectangular Strategy IV.",""],[1,"275","6","Policy Implementation Strategy Alignment with Graduation Impacts","While doing so, the NSDP 2019-2023 also aims to ensure that the strategies to implement these prioritised policies (by the ministries, agencies and sub-national authorities) take into account the potential impact of Cambodia graduating from the",""],[1,"276","3","Inclusive National Development Planning Process","the Ministry of Planning (MOP) has taken concrete steps to ensure active participation from the line ministries and agencies as well as sub-national authorities in the planning process","Ministry of Planning (MOP)"]]}});